{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal","id":945621,"title":"Why is immortality such a big deal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-07T13:21:06-07:00","id":945621,"title":"Why is immortality such a big deal?","content":"The rules seem to demonize attempting to become immortal quite a bit, especially on p. 237 under Liches, claiming that any mage having the austerity to want to live forever has &quot;deeper rooted problems&quot;, because who would dare be so bold as to survive their own children? It's also claimed that it's incredibly difficult to live such a long time. But why? It seems like a Life Perfecting spell should do the job. The example spell &quot;Knit&quot; can only repair damage that your body could repair on its own, but I don't see why that should logically be the case. Seems someone was really worried about mages going for immortality?<br /> <br /> It's not very important to me, but it seems like an odd stance and I wondered if I missed anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:24:09-07:00","id":945626,"title":"","content":"Morally safe solutions usually either have drawbacks (look at the &quot;immortality&quot; spell of Time - even after Reaching the hell out of it, you will NEVER develop a new condition, and NEVER spend XP while under it's protection), or are very fragile - &quot;one dispellation from death&quot; fragile.<br /> The &quot;safe&quot; and &quot;sturdy&quot; methods of immortality are often, well, morally dubious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:31:17-07:00","id":945632,"title":"","content":"It is weird. Especially from Onyx Path. But it happens across the lines, 'normalcy' is something to aspire to. Genderfluidity and sexuality are part of that normal, a good thing, but there's a lot that hasn't been accepted. And deviance from that is inherently monstrous and soul-damaging.<br /> <br /> Mage has some reason for the immortality thing, in that most of the ways to achieve immortality involve harming others. But if a method had been created that doesn't harm others, why would it involve deeper rooted problems? Especially in a game with hubris and overreach as such powerful themes they're entwined with the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-07-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:33:34-07:00","id":945634,"title":"","content":"From an out-of-setting perspective, there are two reasons that immediately appear to me why the game would go out of its way to present a certain image of lichdom, and enforce that with rules:<br /> <br /> 1. Thematically, immortality is a massive act of hubris, and one which serves to divorce the individual from humanity. This is, in Mage's humanistic cosmos, generally a dangerous thing to do. It's worth noting there are a number of example liches who are perfectly fine people - barrow-wights who use their undeath to pursue ultra-long-term magical experiments, for example - but all of them are weird, inhuman, and kind of sideshows to the magical world. And most forms of immortality that already exist - Vampirism, for example, which inspired and was the origin of the Tremere Liches - are morally horrible, because it's a horror-fantasy setting. Being pessimistic about mages being able to hold onto humanity in the face of the abyss of time just follows from the basic themes.<br /> <br /> 2. Mechanically, the easier and less risky it is for mages to gain immortality, the more ultra-powerful elder mages there are in the setting. If immortality is trivial and costs almost nothing, you get a social structure where everything is permanently run by ancient supermages, until they become Archmages, who are plentiful. The Free Council and the Player Characters become almost powerless in the face of legions of multi-degree lich masters. OR, you ignore the mechanics you wrote and write the setting the way you want to write it, and players feel dissonance about that.<br /> <br /> That's my 2c, anyways<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:37:43-07:00","id":945638,"title":"","content":"2nd reason is one I personally care about the most, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:52:13-07:00","id":945646,"title":"","content":"It's definitely the more generally important to players! But I would argue that having coherent themes and ideas underlying the setting make the whole much more functional and interesting, and can and should be a major influence on writers' decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:57:12-07:00","id":945648,"title":"","content":"It's a fairly common motif that the pursuit of immortality is an act of <b><i>extreme</i></b> hubris. See also: Qin Shi Huang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:26:10-07:00","id":945663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal#post945621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules seem to demonize attempting to become immortal quite a bit, especially on p. 237 under Liches, claiming that any mage having the austerity to want to live forever has &quot;deeper rooted problems&quot;, because who would dare be so bold as to survive their own children? It's also claimed that it's incredibly difficult to live such a long time. But why? It seems like a Life Perfecting spell should do the job. The example spell &quot;Knit&quot; can only repair damage that your body could repair on its own, but I don't see why that should logically be the case. Seems someone was really worried about mages going for immortality?<br /> <br /> It's not very important to me, but it seems like an odd stance and I wondered if I missed anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, thing is, when, not if, but when it gets dispelled, say hello to the afterlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T16:57:04-07:00","id":945748,"title":"","content":"First, pretty sure you mean &quot;audacity&quot;, not &quot;austerity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Second, there is an &quot;acceptable&quot; way to achieve immortality in the <i>Mage</i> setting: seek Archmastery. The irony, of course, is that in many ways Archmastery is even more hubristic than even being a Tremere. Sure, Tremere consume souls to survive, but an Archmage creates Aponia as part of their quest and fundamentally alters reality with every 6+ spell they cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:32:47-07:00","id":945885,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact that Death is one of the major ruling forces of the known Mage cosmology. Everything has its time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T00:55:09-07:00","id":946005,"title":"","content":"I would say that it isn't as much about immortality being <i>wrong,</i> it's more about utter majority of mages who even consider it going about acquiring it the wrong way. They *could* modify their genome bit by bit and clear their body of stuff that degraded over time, but that 1) requires careful study of several Arcana *and* exoterics like biology over a significant period of time, sometimes to the point of Mastery and 2) related to that, <b>some patience and foresight</b>. Many mages want things <i>now</i>, they cannot wait and become lured into various left-handed Legacies (like the Tremere), that in the end do more harm to them than good.<br /> <br /> Add to that the cultural bias: Moros Path bias + war with the Tremere, which created a pretty good indoctrination system in a mage society that tells people, that they shouldn't <i>want</i> immortality. Ask any random person on the street whether they want immortality and they will usually say no, either because they believe it either isn't possible or because &quot;they wouldn't want to live a lone life&quot;, not realizing that their friends and family would be immortal as well. Mage society is misguided in a similar way, just with different reasons at the root of those attitudes.<br /> <br /> In short, this means that most mages don't even try for immortality, and those few who try do it the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T02:01:48-07:00","id":946022,"title":"","content":"Using the real world is missing the point slightly. The real world doesn't have a grand spiritual cosmology (or at least it's very well hidden). The CofD does.<br /> <br /> The Moros aren't bias, they're made intimately aware of profound metaphysical truths. I mean, the setting has an exarch to represent the fear of death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T02:08:35-07:00","id":946026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946022#post946022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using the real world is missing the point slightly. The real world doesn't have a grand spiritual cosmology (or at least it's very well hidden). The CofD does.<br /> <br /> The Moros aren't bias, they're made intimately aware of profound metaphysical truths. I mean, the setting has an exarch to represent the fear of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, fear of death that causes you to disregard life is a bit different from wanting to live longer to enjoy said life.<br /> <br /> You could argue that metaphysics are different, but even in CofD exist organisms that don't age, some people have progeria and some have good genes that let them live longer that most of the population. Their lifespan is dependent on their biology, not on any metaphysics. Also, why would species that evolve over millions of years to live longer be any more &quot;metaphysically correct&quot; than a situation when the same physical change is introduced by an act of will over a shorter timespan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:00:02-07:00","id":946047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946026#post946026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their lifespan is dependent on their biology, not on any metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. I mean, biology doesn't have active forces of death, fate and life which apparently are things in the CofD; that's before you get to souls being real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, why would species that evolve over millions of years to live longer be any more &quot;metaphysically correct&quot; than a situation when the same physical change is introduced by an act of will over a shorter timespan? </div> </div> </div>Because the former would be part of a coherent cycle, and your version is basically just damning up that cycle without any regard to the broader system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:38:34-07:00","id":946059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946047#post946047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the former would be part of a coherent cycle, and your version is basically just damning up that cycle without any regard to the broader system.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that could be said about <i>anything</i> happening in modern civilization. Rest of the world couldn't prepare for the arrival of humanity during such an astronomically short time. What makes long life stand out from the ton of things humanity imposed on the world in such a short time? If extensively and quickly taming the environment to serve men is alright...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:41:51-07:00","id":946061,"title":"","content":"The impact of humanity on the natural world has been largely to speed up entropy on the whole which is still part of the natural cycle of existence. Using magic to live a longer life probably isn't that big of a deal, but straight up immortality would be flying in the face of one tenth of the natural metaphysics of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:52:29-07:00","id":946062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946061#post946061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impact of humanity on the natural world has been largely to speed up entropy on the whole which is still part of the natural cycle of existence. Using magic to live a longer life probably isn't that big of a deal, but straight up immortality would be flying in the face of one tenth of the natural metaphysics of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, than it was probably a misunderstanding. I meant &quot;not aging&quot;, not &quot;can't die&quot; and even then thanks to physical changes to the body, not soul metaphysics. Magic would only be used as a more advanced technology, to slightly modify the body in a way that will probably be possible in the near future anyway even without it. Hence the requirement to understand modern sciences, so you know what to affect.<br /> <br /> Of course that screwing with the soul with the Subtle Arcana is not bound to end well. Mages don't understand nearly enough to not screw up when they meddle with the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:01:26-07:00","id":946064,"title":"","content":"Interesting discussion so far, guys.<br /> <br /> Some things I want to respond to:<br /> <br /> - Immortality being hard to achieve so that there would not be too many archmages present: Can be solved by just leveraging the threat of the Exarchs, too, as well as the natural dangers involvd in the study of magic and its practice. There are not a lot of archmages because people who get that strong attract attention from the Abyss and beyond, and their Obsessions raw them into ever more dangerous pursuits. I think just a &quot;natural lifespan&quot; solution is actually less dramatic and more boring a solution.<br /> <br /> - Immortality being an act of hubris: So are lots of other things the PCs can and probably wil do, yet these do not get restrictions imposed on them because of this. <br /> <br /> - If your spell gets dissolved, you will quickly die: How so? Healing damage from guns or healing damage from aging really is no different in the long run, so I don't see why both would not be Lasting, else neither would be. Interesting remark, too: The limitation that has been put on the Knit spell, seemingly to prevent healing aging, also makes mages unable to heal Cancer. Seems... weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:14:13-07:00","id":946067,"title":"","content":"It was stated that it's on purpose that you can't permanently heal cancer or brain damage, and person you are healing is forever reliant on a dispellable, non-lasting 4dot spell. (Regeneration)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:43:47-07:00","id":946073,"title":"","content":"There is a very simple reason why immortality or even invicibility spells cannot be lasting: &quot;NOT beeing something&quot; cannot be a lasting condition. Mages do age. Not aging is an unnatural state, you cannot achieve. It's the same with stuff like, not having cancer. You can heal the symptoms over and over again and probably recreate something like a chemo therapy and wipe all cancer cells from the body, but you cannot create a lasting, natural effect, that prevents rebuilding of cancer cells. I do agree though, that there is no reason for you to age faster after a non aging spell is dispelled on you. If you could freeze a body for 20 years, there is no logical reason for why it should age faster after the 20 years. So even if your spell get's dispelled after 2 years e.g. it was probably still worth it.<br /> <br /> I would also tune a bit down on the natural regeneration front. While there is a lot of research going on, there is no evidence that there will be any kind of gen therapy in the near future that will provide the human body with the means to constantly regenerate to e.g. the state at age 20. Even if this might be possbile, it might have significant complications, for example not beeing able to get any new memories and therefore learning anything. This is not so much a problem for a low brain function animal mainly acting on instincts, but for a human or a mage, this would have significant problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 08-08-2016, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:56:31-07:00","id":946076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946059#post946059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that could be said about <i>anything</i> happening in modern civilization. Rest of the world couldn't prepare for the arrival of humanity during such an astronomically short time. What makes long life stand out from the ton of things humanity imposed on the world in such a short time? If extensively and quickly taming the environment to serve men is alright...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a lot. I mean, I was actually wondering about making an analogy to the impact of humans on the natural world.<br /> The difference is that humans only really became aware of the impact they were having long after our society became dependant on those extremely destructive technology. The prospective immortal Moros is well aware of the issues beforehand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Immortality being hard to achieve so that there would not be too many archmages present: Can be solved by just leveraging the threat of the Exarchs, too, as well as the natural dangers involvd in the study of magic and its practice. There are not a lot of archmages because people who get that strong attract attention from the Abyss and beyond, and their Obsessions raw them into ever more dangerous pursuits. I think just a &quot;natural lifespan&quot; solution is actually less dramatic and more boring a solution. </div> </div> </div>You don't really need to do anything, that's pretty much how things are anyway.<br /> <br /> As for it being boring, I don't really see how your version is better. You've just made lifespan a non-issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:57:20-07:00","id":946077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946067#post946067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was stated that it's on purpose that you can't permanently heal cancer or brain damage, and person you are healing is forever reliant on a dispellable, non-lasting 4dot spell. (Regeneration)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. But you <b>can </b>use Life to make body stronger to resist the disease, you can use Fate to make the probability of various medicaments succeeding higher, etc...<br /> <br /> Using an Arcanum to brute force the condition to disappear by simply rewriting it to &quot;not be&quot; was never the point. Using it in conjunction with other tools and knowledge to get the result you wish for is the point of my 'use exoteric knowledge' idea I was making earlier. More advanced civilization = more of exoteric knowledge = better ability to use magic as a fine tool instead of a sledgehammer.<br /> <br /> Also, Death can actually do just that:<br /> <br /> <b>Deny the Reaper</b><br /> <br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: <b>Medicine</b>, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> &quot;...The mage reverses the effects of decay, <b>restoring the subject to its physical state of being from before</b> up to one month per Potency of the spell. On a living subject, the spell can <b>restore eyesight, the use of limbs, reversing irreparable damage, and restoring all bodily functions</b>...&quot;<br /> <br /> Notice the Potency as a primary factor. The spell is Lasting, otherwise it would be duration as primary. It's like that with every other spell in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:31:01-07:00","id":946089,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Masters already can easily mass ressurect people by doing something like &quot;Grab a Spirit of Rank 3, use Spirit 4th dot to make it a Spirit of Healing, use Bolster Spirit to make it Rank 4 and give it Ressurection Numina, don't care about Dissonance/Dispellation/Other stuff&quot;. I think it's much saner to generally consider 4th and 5th dot impacts on the world on local/individual scale, not potentially world-changing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:35:11-07:00","id":946092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946089#post946089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Masters already can easily mass ressurect people by doing something like &quot;Grab a Spirit of Rank 3, use Spirit 4th dot to make it a Spirit of Healing, use Bolster Spirit to make it Rank 4 and give it Ressurection Numina, don't care about Dissonance/Dispellation/Other stuff&quot;. I think it's much saner to generally consider 4th and 5th dot impacts on the world on local/individual scale, not potentially world-changing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can concede that point.<br /> <br /> It's the first part of my post I consider important. Normal Life magic may not directly cure cancer, but it sure as hell can be a useful tool in medicine's repertoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:46:35-07:00","id":946097,"title":"","content":"It is. In general, my favorite mode of using magic is to &quot;enhance your skills and abilities&quot;, instead of replacing them. For example, I vastly prefer an Alchemist who uses her knowledge of Science to nudge and push Matter in ways that enhance her chemical processes and opens up new avenues, instead of replacing the whole thing with &quot;I cast a spell, alchemy done&quot;. <br /> This in general works really great for most of things (instead of mentally reprograming your children, try to enhance the parenting process with your mind magic! instead of literally changing value of &quot;is he sick&quot; from true to false using life magic, try to cause things that will result in making that person less sick)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:53:45-07:00","id":946099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946097#post946097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. In general, my favorite mode of using magic is to &quot;enhance your skills and abilities&quot;, instead of replacing them. For example, I vastly prefer an Alchemist who uses her knowledge of Science to nudge and push Matter in ways that enhance her chemical processes and opens up new avenues, instead of replacing the whole thing with &quot;I cast a spell, alchemy done&quot;.<br /> This in general works really great for most of things (instead of mentally reprograming your children, try to enhance the parenting process with your mind magic! instead of literally changing value of &quot;is he sick&quot; from true to false using life magic, try to cause things that will result in making that person less sick)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say that this is actually the point of Wisdom. Mage with high Wisdom knows to, among other things, minimize the impact of his magic on the world and is subtle in its applications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:59:32-07:00","id":946105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946092#post946092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can concede that point.<br /> <br /> It's the first part of my post I consider important. Normal Life magic may not directly cure cancer, but it sure as hell can be a useful tool in medicine's repertoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the Fraying Practice used upon Cancer work very much like amazing precise Chemotherapy that only affected the Cancer? I mean combined with Unveiling to know exactly which cells were cancerous. Also could you just Unmake the Cancer as a Lasting effect, Unmaking is usually Lasting anyway. Sorry for quibbling over details.<br /> <br /> I would note in my homebrew Immortality (as per the Immortality Dread Power) is accessible to every Major Template at a price, and it works well both for Reoccurring NPC and even PCs. Vampire in particular seems to do well when a simple beat down of a violent thug doesn't solve anything permanently (unsurprisingly Immortality is already a theme in Vampire so the dark prices of blood sacrifices and ritual aren't that out of place)<br /> <br /> In Mage I tie it heavily to Reaping Lichdom, which is also thematically appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T06:08:18-07:00","id":946109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946105#post946105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would the Fraying Practice used upon Cancer work very much like amazing precise Chemotherapy that only affected the Cancer? I mean combined with Unveiling to know exactly which cells were cancerous. Also could you just Unmake the Cancer as a Lasting effect, Unmaking is usually Lasting anyway. Sorry for quibbling over details.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess so. As WHW said, at the Mastery level things get pretty wonky (and scary. Masters are scary.) In <i>Mage</i> in general, you are given a great amount of tools (and not just magic) that you can combine to get the results you want. The amount of combinations is practically infinite and cannot be all listed here. That's what the Creative Thaumaturgy is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:26:24-07:00","id":946149,"title":"","content":"These immortality topics keep coming back from the dead!<br /> <br /> Having immortality in your Mage game is completely irrelevant. You are not going to be playing forever, you know? You, the player, you will die. Or just get bored and stop playing. So what does it matter if your character is immortal or not? Being immortal grants you absolutely nothing. It can serve as a plot device to the ST if he wants, at most. And the ST can make any NPC or PC immortal if plot required it anyways.<br /> <br /> Since Mage is not a game about exploring immortality (if you want to explore that, I suggest the book Ancient Mysteries for Vampire the Requiem) it doesn't have much support to play stories about immortal mages. Even to archmasters, immortality is a side thought, the book didn't even talk about it. I feel like this is more or less the same thing I said in the last three Immortality threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:34:43-07:00","id":946156,"title":"","content":"For many people, it's relevant from worldbuilding point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:59:44-07:00","id":946170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946149#post946149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These immortality topics keep coming back from the dead!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they *are* immortality threads...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:29:21-07:00","id":946219,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Sans-Serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Sans-Serif\">That is not dead which can eternal lie,<br /> And with strange aeons even death may die</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:35:26-07:00","id":946226,"title":"","content":"The Dead Collector: Bring out yer dead.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">[a man puts a body on the cart]<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Here's one.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: That'll be ninepence.<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I'm not dead.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: What?<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Nothing. There's your ninepence.<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I'm not dead.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: 'Ere, he says he's not dead.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Yes he is.<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I'm not.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: He isn't.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Well, he will be soon, he's very ill.<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I'm getting better.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: No you're not, you'll be stone dead in a moment.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: Well, I can't take him like that. It's against regulations.<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I don't want to go on the cart.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Oh, don't be such a baby.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: I can't take him.<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I feel fine.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Oh, do me a favor.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: I can't.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Well, can you hang around for a couple of minutes? He won't be long.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: I promised I'd be at the Robinsons'. They've lost nine today.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Well, when's your next round?<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: Thursday.<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I think I'll go for a walk.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: You're not fooling anyone, you know. Isn't there anything you could do?<br /> <br /> The Dead Body That Claims It Isn't: I feel happy. I feel happy.<br /> <br /> [the Dead Collector glances up and down the street furtively, then silences the Body with his a whack of his club]<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Ah, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> The Dead Collector: Not at all. See you on Thursday.<br /> <br /> Large Man with Dead Body: Right.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (all credit to Monty Python, of course)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6770,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","user":"Midgardener","date":". 08-08-2016, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:06:46-07:00","id":946251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946073#post946073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a very simple reason why immortality or even invicibility spells cannot be lasting: &quot;NOT beeing something&quot; cannot be a lasting condition. Mages do age. Not aging is an unnatural state, you cannot achieve. It's the same with stuff like, not having cancer. You can heal the symptoms over and over again and probably recreate something like a chemo therapy and wipe all cancer cells from the body, but you cannot create a lasting, natural effect, that prevents rebuilding of cancer cells. I do agree though, that there is no reason for you to age faster after a non aging spell is dispelled on you. If you could freeze a body for 20 years, there is no logical reason for why it should age faster after the 20 years. So even if your spell get's dispelled after 2 years e.g. it was probably still worth it.<br /> <br /> I would also tune a bit down on the natural regeneration front. While there is a lot of research going on, there is no evidence that there will be any kind of gen therapy in the near future that will provide the human body with the means to constantly regenerate to e.g. the state at age 20. Even if this might be possbile, it might have significant complications, for example not beeing able to get any new memories and therefore learning anything. This is not so much a problem for a low brain function animal mainly acting on instincts, but for a human or a mage, this would have significant problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you're using the right definition of &quot;Lasting&quot; here. A &quot;Lasting&quot; magical effect is not a condition that can never change. Lasting simply means that a change wrought through magic will last past its duration, on its own. Healing spells like Knit are Lasting, but that does not mean you become immune to taking damage. A spell that pulls heat from one room into another will have a Lasting effect, because the heat will not magically return to the original room when the Duration ends. If you open a door between the rooms though, the fact that the effect was Lasting will not keep the heat trapped in the second room, and unable to go into the first.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you are not trying to cast a spell to &quot;not age&quot;. You simply cast a spell that heals your body back to the state it was, say, last year, once a year, and that effect should then be Lasting. Not because you can no longer age after that, but because you will not magically age a year at the end of the duration.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you're confusing it with a spell with Indefinite duration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-08-2016, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:32:47-07:00","id":946270,"title":"","content":"Immortality gets a lot of attention because it's, y'know, a major feature of mythology and the human imagination. <br /> <br /> The Great Awakening Immortality Wars have actually inspired some of my own work. In my remake of Mage (which is heavily based on Ascension and Genius), I was considering making immortality (which is pretty easy to achieve) a Wisdom transgression, but I think now I'll specify that immortality is a-ok with everyone and even the wisest and most careful Mages are fine with it, because spite. <br /> <br /> Why is it so easy to achieve in MtT? Same reason why reverse acting is cheap in Changeling and immortality is a two dot merit in Ascension (one of many things I love about that beautiful, wonderful game): it's not something likely to come up from a gameplay perspective, so letting a player do it doesn't risk unbalancing the game. Immortality is primarily a narrative and roleplaying concern, so that's how it's treated. As for the &quot;elder problem&quot;, mages are so volatile and capricious that even if most of them didn't blow themselves up there would be no risk of them stagnating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:58:08-07:00","id":946285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946270#post946270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it so easy to achieve in MtT?</div> </div> </div> </div>The question I raised in the OP is why it is made so hard to achieve when, logically, it *should* be easy, magic being what it is. Life spells are artificially restricted from doing it from the third dot onwards, and the fluff mentioning immortality marks it as left handed and abominable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:20:41-07:00","id":946304,"title":"","content":"Remember that while game is apolitical, sometimes you can see sparks of humanism and anarchism in the writing; try to look at it from that context. It might make certain decisions form a pattern that makes more sense to you, and thus, changing them will be easier.<br /> Anyway, I don't have a problem with Immortality being Hard And Potentially Monstrous, because it's Chronicles of Darkness and Modern Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:31:54-07:00","id":946317,"title":"","content":"To answer the OP's answer: well, when you get down to it, you never die if you are immortal, which is what everybody wants out of immortality... but you also live forever. At some point, does life become boring? When you have an indefinite number of lifetimes, does there come a point where you have literally done everything? If a 30-something person has trouble remembering details from their childhood, what about a 1,000-something person trying to recall details from their first century of life? You have to live with the consequences of your actions, and watch them play out, for centuries. And the ways you obtain immortality permanently separate you from humanity. You renounce it, declare yourself apart from and above humanity. Particularly in Mage, characters who seek that course of action are not thinking or acting in a way that speaks to Understanding or Enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:51:21-07:00","id":946387,"title":"","content":"In the Chronicles of Darkness, especially in Mage, one of the themes of the setting (even if you disagree with it) is that death is a natural and important part of life and that subverting that natural cycle is an act of hubris. Living longer--by doing things like eating healthy and using medicine--is OK because you're still not bypassing an eventual death, but using magic to make yourself deathless is Bad (or at least morally fraught). The metaphysics support this theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946077#post946077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice the Potency as a primary factor. The spell is Lasting, otherwise it would be duration as primary. It's like that with every other spell in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, not true. <i>Deny the Reaper</i> is not Lasting, and neither is <i>Quicken Ghost</i>, <i>Psychic Domination</i>, <i>Control Gravity</i>, <i>Transform Life</i>, etc, etc. There is no hard or fast rule about which spells have Lasting effects except that if it doesn't seem logical for the state to revert once the spell is over, it is a Lasting effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:35:10-07:00","id":946416,"title":"","content":"Well, as an example, the Quicken Ghost spell has Heal Corpus as a possible potency effect - that is Lasting. Psychic Domination creates commands that are temporary by definition. Control Gravity was errata'd to duration, and Transform Life has the caveeat that you can transfer the effects with +2 Reach to the descendants, if the spell is made indefinite. That is Lasting, otherwise this would have to be a practice of Dynamics. Also, an Unmaking spell has more power than a disciple lever practice.<br /> <br /> The primary factor is always what Dave defined as the first thing you consider when you think of the spell's effects. With the Deny the Reaper spell, if the spell was not Lasting, I would first think of duration, not potency. When you get the Lasting effect, duration has no meaning, hence the potency as a primary factor. The same with other spells.<br /> <br /> But thanks to all of the lower level spells you can use to physically (indirectly) modify the biology of an organism with Lasting results, it doesn't matter anyway. This spell is the sledgehammer I mentioned earlier. It's just that in this case, it actually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-08-2016, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:02:40-07:00","id":946435,"title":"","content":"I really wish that templating for &quot;is spell lasting, yes no&quot; would be clearer in this edition. It's very debatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:02:43-07:00","id":946436,"title":"","content":"One of the major barriers to immortality in Awakening is going to be gone in Transgression too, since there's no more Supernal and the Spheres are only rough classifications of what a magic can use their magic on or with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:06:43-07:00","id":946441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946435#post946435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish that templating for &quot;is spell lasting, yes no&quot; would be clearer in this edition. It's very debatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, now that I'm thinking about it, it may be for the best. As a storyteller, it allows you to slightly modify the rules to fit your setting and chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:14:52-07:00","id":946447,"title":"","content":"Eh, I prefer clarity. I can adjust slightly and home rule anyway; I currently can't hand over the spell list to players and say &quot;just follow the write up + remember these house rules&quot;. Instead of having 100 spells where I might homerule 3, I practically need to homerule all 100. <br /> *100 is a fake number here, I don't know how many spells do we have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:08:12-07:00","id":946531,"title":"","content":"Is there a *good* way to be immortal in CofD? Because whether it's Vampirism, becoming a spirit, being a Sin Eater, Promethean etc all ways of becoming immortal in the setting come with serious drawbacks. Some may not be deal breakers for the right person but mortality is the default and you *have* to give something up to buy power in COFD. There is no free lunch. It's a fundamentally dystopian setting at the cosmic level which is why it's biased against transhumanism. Must transhuman assumptions assume apotheosis without costs that might be objectionable or at least inconvenient to a subset of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:28:11-07:00","id":946543,"title":"","content":"Probably the cleanest way to become Immortal is becoming on of the Purified (WoD:Immortals). Immortality, powers,and you can still live like a regular person (mostly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:29:51-07:00","id":946611,"title":"","content":"One of the Legacies in Mage: The Transgression is going to be focused on immortality, but since it's relatively easy for Mages to have, they're primarily focused on giving it to others and spreading acceptance of it within and outside of Enlightened society. <br /> <br /> Their Attainments are based around helping them survive things, and their ultimate Attainment is a sort of berserker fury powered by their own fear of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:34:06-07:00","id":946616,"title":"","content":"Slaves of the Psychopomp then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:38:06-07:00","id":946621,"title":"","content":"I think much of it is rooted in Hollywood Morality, which does not reflect real life very well.<br /> But on the other hand, the older you are the higher chance you are to have some very stagnant beliefs.<br /> I don't want my racist grandma being immortal, because she shows no inclination to stop being racist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:55:48-07:00","id":946643,"title":"","content":"If you pass a not-racist test, then do you get the nanobots?<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure if we're talking morality here so much as mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:56:50-07:00","id":946644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946616#post946616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slaves of the Psychopomp then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even remotely, and not just because the Exarchs don't exist in the same way in Transgression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:04:53-07:00","id":946651,"title":"","content":"I think its important to note the difference between what Mages look at as life extention and true immortality.<br /> <br /> If its a fragile spell, that would be viewed as life extension, which would not make you a Lich. It'd ne like taking a pill that doubles your life span, you just a long lived human.<br /> <br /> But a true lich crosses the line into inhuman in order to achieve true immortality. The become a Spirit, Ghost, Treme, something stranger, and their humanity and connection gets weaker as time goes on.<br /> <br /> So the 4 choices for Mages who fear death are:<br /> <br /> 1. Life Extension, the mage equivilant of eating right.<br /> <br /> 2. Becoming a Lich, the worse of which are Reapers, none Reaper Liches would be more likely to looked up with dusgust, instead of as pure dangerous evil like a Reaper Lich.<br /> <br /> 3. Ascenion.<br /> <br /> 4. Look outside Mage Magic, certain Changeling magics for example could extend a mages lifespan, potentially to an unlimited to degree, but other Mages will see you as the pawn of such a powerful changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 08-08-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T00:00:07-07:00","id":946776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=946251#post946251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure you're using the right definition of &quot;Lasting&quot; here. A &quot;Lasting&quot; magical effect is not a condition that can never change. Lasting simply means that a change wrought through magic will last past its duration, on its own. Healing spells like Knit are Lasting, but that does not mean you become immune to taking damage. A spell that pulls heat from one room into another will have a Lasting effect, because the heat will not magically return to the original room when the Duration ends. If you open a door between the rooms though, the fact that the effect was Lasting will not keep the heat trapped in the second room, and unable to go into the first.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you are not trying to cast a spell to &quot;not age&quot;. You simply cast a spell that heals your body back to the state it was, say, last year, once a year, and that effect should then be Lasting. Not because you can no longer age after that, but because you will not magically age a year at the end of the duration.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you're confusing it with a spell with Indefinite duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did read that carefully, the problem is: there is no spell which can heal you to your past self. Mage has an objective present. To bring your past body back you need Temporal Summoning, which is explicitly not lasting. You can suspend yourself in time with Veile of Moments, but then you deny yourself the possibility to advance in any way. Time is objectively advandcing in Mage and you can only suspend it's effects on a human/mages body by active magic. And active magic is not a lasting effect. Lasting effects have to be something that can naturally sustain itself without magic.<br /> <br /> If you read the chapter about Liches, you will see that you can also sustain your body with permanent regeneration spells from Life or Death e.g. to stay healthy, but that also requires constant, active magic.<br /> <br /> It all boils down to the fact, that normal Mages have a body and that body ages. To become immortal you need to get rid of that body somehow or replace it constantly. And I hope everybody sees how this is first and foremost and act of hubris and has other ethical implications, too. On the very least you get disconnected from the world. You lose your ability to sense via a living body, you lose the needs for food, sleep and such. This disconnection will very practically make you unable to feel empathy towards human beeings or other mages after a while or will force you, to use an extrem effort to actually stay connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 08-09-2016, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:56:22-07:00","id":946896,"title":"","content":"They have a body...and a mind. And a soul. Who also age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:01:07-07:00","id":946978,"title":"","content":"It seems like with enough Life, it would be trivial to clone a young body, transfer your brain into it, and rejuvenate the cells in your brain. You could say that's all Life, or if you want to make it harder, make it Life+Mind. But still pretty easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:08:35-07:00","id":946986,"title":"","content":"In Mage cosmology, you can have a brick with no brain cells but with a mind. I don't think that rejuvenating your brain would enough. Then you have the Fate of all things to die. Then you have Prime symbols incorporated into &quot;Humans are things that do X, Y, Z, and are U, C, V&quot;, where probably there is a symbol of &quot;and they die&quot;. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:20:51-07:00","id":946991,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or is it kind of hilarious that immortality is harder to achieve in a game about magic superwizards than it is in real life? <br /> <br /> There's also the problem of game themes clashing. Mage makes immortality incredibly hard to achieve, yet becoming a vampire or any of the things in Immortals is something any random person could potentially do. <br /> <br /> If anything, all this stuff is making me even more confident about removing the Supernal and the symbology element in my remake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:24:37-07:00","id":946997,"title":"","content":"Yes, immortality in real life is so easy. Heck, I'm getting my youth booster shot this weekend.<br /> <br /> You can't call it easy until it's actually happened and is in fact easy.<br /> <br /> You know, if you want to keep plugging your homebrew make another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:25:52-07:00","id":946999,"title":"","content":"I mean easy in that real life doesn't have Supernal symbols or fate, so immortality is purely a biological matter and does involve tinkering with the fundamental foundations of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:27:06-07:00","id":947002,"title":"","content":"Death is part of the Human Condition. In the Awakened cosmology, the human condition is important. Bending your magical talents to escaping death is analogous to excise the ability to feel sadness, or joy, or the ability to make mistakes and learn from them. Pursuing immortality ostracizes the mage from pentacle society, because at it's core it's an attempt to stick around further in the Fallen world when the Fallen world is <i>bad. </i>It's something that probably edges a little too close to Seer outlook for a lot of pentacle mages to be super comfortable with as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:27:13-07:00","id":947003,"title":"","content":"Yeah, entropy isn't a thing in real life. What was I thinking, I keep forgetting physics is make believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:29:33-07:00","id":947005,"title":"","content":"I feel something's been overlooked here. Non-supernal magic.<br /> <br /> You can buy youth at a Goblin Market. It's not risk free, but Mages should have a fair chance of pulling it off. There's a Contract in 1E Changeling that trades 7 years younger for a Willpower dot, that's a very good exchange rate even when you account for the Goblin Merchant who you're paying to use it on you adds a markup.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:34:55-07:00","id":947011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947005#post947005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel something's been overlooked here. Non-supernal magic.<br /> <br /> You can buy youth at a Goblin Market. It's not risk free, but Mages should have a fair chance of pulling it off. There's a Contract in 1E Changeling that trades 7 years younger for a Willpower dot, that's a very good exchange rate even when you account for the Goblin Merchant who you're paying to use it on you adds a markup.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned when the Changeling 2E mechanics came out: You want to be unaging? Find yourself a fairy girlfriend.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:39:26-07:00","id":947018,"title":"","content":"As I said, there's the crossover problem. If mortality is a such a big whanging deal for Mages, it kinda shoots a hole in that. <br /> <br /> And entropy isn't an obstacle to removing brains from bodies, preserving them, and placing them in unaging cybernetic bodies, which seems like the best bet for immortality in real life. <br /> <br /> And there's that pesky, lazy deathism again. You could say that not being able to fly is part of the human condition, and that riding in an airplane makes a Mage a Lich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:55:09-07:00","id":947032,"title":"","content":"LOL &quot;lazy deathism&quot;. m'kay.<br /> <br /> Look, Awakening isn't a transhumanist game. You can run transhumanist games in it where lots of mages don't care about immortality and some people pursue it ardently, but the core game has &quot;death is a thing that is important because of vague reasons&quot; as a setting point. It's an important aspect of Stygia. It's a big &quot;whanging&quot; deal for mages because they have to deal with giant chunks of their cosmos that mean absolutely zilch for every other supernatural creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:59:58-07:00","id":947037,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and that's one of many parts of Awakening that just doesn't work, which is why I'm gutting them for my remake of the game. <br /> <br /> Also, you are aware that plenty of people seem to think it is? During arguments over transhumanism in Promethean, people have recommended Mage to me and others, specifically describing it as a transhumanist game because it's about transcending human limits and becoming posthuman entities. <br /> <br /> I find it kind of funny that throwing fireballs and teleporting is considered okay, but immortality isn't. I'm pretty sure pyrokinesis and apportation aren't inherent parts of the human condition either, but no one says you're Playing Wrong for making a Mage who's okay with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:06:31-07:00","id":947041,"title":"","content":"Just to puncture a hole in the idea that vampires are immortal, the suffer from a loss of personal continuity. The only thing that keeps moving forward unendingly is their body and the Beast.<br /> <br /> Also, cybernetic bodies with rejuvenated brains is not a solution to entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:10:47-07:00","id":947043,"title":"","content":"Entropy only gets to be a problem once we have to worry about large-scale cosmic decay. Even if it's insurmountable, life extension can still give you millions of years instead of less than a hundred. <br /> <br /> And the personal continuity thing is only a theory. I don't think you're going to be able to argue that vampires aren't immortal. <br /> <br /> You could argue, however, that while they're immortal, they're immortal monsters. Or that the themes and mechanics of vampire shouldn't influence the themes and mechanics of Mage.<br /> <br /> All of this comes back to my central problem with Awakening: mages aren't really monsters. I agree that in a horror setting immortality should make you monstrous, but major splats should ALREADY be monsters. Once you Awaken, you should already recognizably be an inhuman monster. That's what ChroD is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:11:38-07:00","id":947044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947003#post947003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, entropy isn't a thing in real life. What was I thinking, I keep forgetting physics is make believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Mage is a game that's as much about lying to yourself as it is discovering truths about the world, so she's got that right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:18:51-07:00","id":947050,"title":"","content":"Mage isn't a Transhumanist game. Neither is Exalted. There is a vocal faction of pro-transhumanist fans of those games (especially on this and the last forums) that have latched onto those games in the past and claimed that they totally are transhumanist but then spend a whole lot of time nit-picking all the stuff that doesn't jive with what they claim transhumanism is.<br /> <br /> Mage has never ever been a &quot;transhumanist game about transcending human limits and becoming posthuman entities&quot;, it's always been a game about humans who are given power and what they do with it. Even the mightiest archmage is still just a human with a lot of power. Trying to compare throwing fireballs and flying (which the setting says is okay) to immortality (which the setting says isn't okay) is splitting hairs. The game isn't about all this power that you can never use ever. It's a game of modern mages, not posthumans who used Awakening as a stepping stone to the Singularity.<br /> <br /> The fact that you can squish and squeeze the game to the point where you can play that if you want is a point in it's favor, not a mark against it because that's not the core setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:22:42-07:00","id":947053,"title":"","content":"Well, see, I'm entirely fine with a game about humans misusing power and how that makes them monstrous, but the game doesn't really live up to it. <br /> <br /> I'm fine with immortality being blasphemous and corrupting, but I think that in a horror game ALL magic should be like that. In my remake, what differentiates mages from sorcerers or other supernaturals is that theirs is a deeply personal and incredibly dangerous sort of magic that involves forcing reality to temporarily conform to their rules by basically blasting holes in it.<br /> <br /> There is no question in the game that this is Probably a Bad Thing. Immortality is actually one of the less dangerous things you can do, however, because it's much less Paradox-risky than throwing fireballs at people or trying to steal Fort Knox with a giant clockwork spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:24:39-07:00","id":947055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947050#post947050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has never ever been a &quot;transhumanist game about transcending human limits and becoming posthuman entities&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what Ascension to the supernal is about? There's at least one order gunning for it.<br /> <br /> The entire game is about the world being false, and looking into mysteries. Having a character trying to find a way to become immortal, to figure out the mystery of that part of the lie, shouldn't be dismissed as not part of the game, when characters are encouraged to do similar things. Mages defy Fate, play Time like a turntable, make a mockery of Space, control and create Minds and Life. Balking at defying Death seems a bit laughable. If it's something you don't want to do in your games that's fine, but there's no reason to tell people that they're playing the game wrong if they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Fixed as archmastery doesn't grant immortality 08-19-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:27:53-07:00","id":947059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947055#post947055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that what Archmastery and ascension to the supernal is about? There's at least one order gunning for it.<br /> <br /> The entire game is about the world being false, and looking into mysteries. Having a character trying to find a way to become immortal, to figure out the mystery of that part of the lie, shouldn't be dismissed as not part of the game, when characters are encouraged to do similar things.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had a nickel every time someone complained about Promethean's hostility to transhumanism and someone said &quot;but humans in ChroD are awesome and powerful and can become superbeings! What about Mages and Archmasters?&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:29:32-07:00","id":947061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947018#post947018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's that pesky, lazy deathism again. You could say that not being able to fly is part of the human condition, and that riding in an airplane makes a Mage a Lich.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, for someone who complains about people attacking other people for their ideas of fun, you sure do swing words around like a billy club at people who are just trying to have a civil discussion.<br /> <br /> Also, LOL, wut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:32:29-07:00","id":947063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947061#post947061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, for someone who complains about people attacking other people for their ideas of fun, you sure do swing words around like a billy club at people who are just trying to have a civil discussion.<br /> <br /> Also, LOL, wut.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't know what &quot;deathism&quot; means, google it. The second part was me pointing out that humans already transcend our own limitations in countless ways, and I don't consider immortality or life extension to be in any way different from the ways in which we already use technology to do things we are not capable of doing by ourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:35:41-07:00","id":947067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947063#post947063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you don't know what &quot;deathism&quot; means, google it. The second part was me pointing out that humans already transcend our own limitations in countless ways, and I don't consider immortality or life extension to be in any way different from the ways in which we already use technology to do things we are not capable of doing by ourselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, I know what you mean. That doesn't change the fact that you are so persistently aggressive that any good grace you have for people giving you flak has died ages ago, and the level to which you try to infantalize and demonize your opposition has reached comedy levels.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Too much, Arc, dial it down a notch please. Darksider</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 08-09-2016, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:38:53-07:00","id":947070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947043#post947043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this comes back to my central problem with Awakening: mages aren't really monsters. I agree that in a horror setting immortality should make you monstrous, but major splats should ALREADY be monsters. Once you Awaken, you should already recognizably be an inhuman monster. That's what ChroD is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not gonna make this an argument or anything. Mages are absolutely already inhuman monsters when they Awaken. But then, I don't get <i>any</i> of the problems you have with Awakening (and I would ask that instead of saying &quot;These things don't work in Awakening&quot; you should say &quot;I dislike these elements/These elements don't work for me&quot; but I'm not gonna hold my breath).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:38:58-07:00","id":947071,"title":"","content":"You know, the airplane thing was intended to be funny, so I'm glad you got it. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, you don't seem to see the humor in people writing off immortality as inherently inhuman and unnatural while using the Internet and getting vaccinations. <br /> <br /> Or assuming that enlightened superwizards who can teleport and throw fireballs would balk at the idea of immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:43:13-07:00","id":947075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947071#post947071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the airplane thing was intended to be funny, so I'm glad you got it.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, you don't seem to see the humor in people writing off immortality as inherently inhuman and unnatural while using the Internet and getting vaccinations.<br /> <br /> Or assuming that enlightened superwizards who can teleport and throw fireballs would balk at the idea of immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death is an integral part of how souls work.<br /> Death is an integral part of humanity.<br /> Prolong it? Sure. That's fine. But immortality? No. That's not fitting here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:44:00-07:00","id":947076,"title":"","content":"Some do, some obviously don't since liches are a thing.<br /> <br /> Also, I think you're undervaluing the horror that is magic. It drives Mages to do inhuman things all the while screaming that they're in control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:46:49-07:00","id":947082,"title":"","content":"Why not change how souls work or how humanity works? If Mages are enlightened ascendant superbeings, they should be able to do that.<br /> <br /> If Mages are profane, blasphemous monsters, then they shouldn't care about how humanity or souls or reality work. <br /> <br /> Approaching this from a gameplay and roleplaying perspective instead of a real-world moral one, I could not play a character who did not want to be immortal. My desire to live forever is such an integral part of who I am that I could not effectively portray someone who didn't have it. I have played characters with wildly different beliefs and personalities and ideologies from my own, but the idea of accepting or even celebrating mortality is so utterly alien and abhorrent to me that I could never get into the role of someone who felt that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:50:03-07:00","id":947085,"title":"","content":"Your problem is that you lack the ability to see both sides and that in Mage itself it's an unanswered question, because it's not spelled out for you where the line is drawn. The game isn't flawed for not lining up with your own moral agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:51:07-07:00","id":947086,"title":"","content":"I think its more a case of right form of immortality vs. wrong form of immortality. Gain immortality by ascending is honoured in mage society, because its moving towards the Supernal, but gain immortality by becoming a lich, wrong kind of immortality and you tie yourself to lie or cause horrible harm, and you in essence pull back from the Supernal.<br /> <br /> So Mage isn't anti transhumanism, its all about doing it right vs. taking short cuts.<br /> <br /> To be fair Mages may get around this by concidering ascension to be a form or reincarnation into a higher plane or an afterlifem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:51:54-07:00","id":947087,"title":"","content":"If you want to make &quot;people are dying&quot; a bad thing that should be fought, then you have a very easy lever to pull:<br /> Make &quot;humanity is destined to die&quot; an Exarch safety mechanism baked into the Lie in order to keep humanity in check and to make sure that no matter how Mages struggle, they will never get enough time to undermine Exarch plots. This way you make it a tragic situation where you are enslaved by death, and only way of defying and rebelling is to commit to Left Handed Paths. It's a seed for interesting stories that aren't black and white.<br /> And if a singular Mage attains immortality, you might literally send him an Ochema of Psychopomp who will tell them to keep the secret for themselves, or else.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> This way you don't have to celebrate mortality, but still have to deal with the idea that alternatives to it might be worse than good. Pick your poison, choose between evils, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-09-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:54:35-07:00","id":947089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947087#post947087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to make &amp;quot;people are dying&amp;quot; a bad thing that should be fought, then you have a very easy lever to pull:<br /> Make &amp;quot;humanity is destined to die&amp;quot; an Exarch safety mechanism baked into the Lie in order to keep humanity in check and to make sure that no matter how Mages struggle, they will never get enough time to undermine Exarch plots. This way you make it a tragic situation where you are enslaved by death, and only way of defying and rebelling is to commit to Left Handed Paths. It's a seed for interesting stories that aren't black and white. <br /> And if a singular Mage attains immortality, you might literally send him an Ochema of Psychopomp who will tell them to keep the secret for themselves, or else.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that comes to the problem that there are kind of two versions of Mage we're dealing with. <br /> <br /> In the urban fantasy game of dark but hopefully enlightened gnostic superheroes that Awakening is closer to being, that would be an awesome way to handle things. <br /> <br /> In the personal horror game of volatile monstrous reality-punchers with powers that will probably destroy them, I'm fine with having all forms of immortality be somehow monstrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:00:23-07:00","id":947094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947071#post947071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the airplane thing was intended to be funny, so I'm glad you got it. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, you don't seem to see the humor in people writing off immortality as inherently inhuman and unnatural while using the Internet and getting vaccinations. <br /> <br /> Or assuming that enlightened superwizards who can teleport and throw fireballs would balk at the idea of immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with you, I can see going for immortality via say becoming a Treme Lich or some other kind of reaper would be taboo, but the only reason I can see other forms being taboo, is if they're seen as blocing your shot at ascension. Like becoming a Ghost or Spirit Mage, blocks your soul from Ascension as long as the ghost mage or spirit mage exists, with Ascension being the only &quot;true&quot; form of transhumanism, with others, including vampires being seen by most mage society as heresy.<br /> <br /> Still away around this would be none reaper, by Lich based Nameless Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:01:04-07:00","id":947096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947075#post947075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death is an integral part of how souls work.<br /> Death is an integral part of humanity.<br /> Prolong it? Sure. That's fine. But immortality? No. That's not fitting here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legacies routinely reshape one's soul and often physical form. There's legacies that turn you part spirit and into three-eyed hermaphrodites. There's even a legacy called the Transhuman Engineers, which I'm imagining are at least a little about being transhuman. What with the name.<br /> <br /> And part of the reason this thread got started is because there's a section mentioning the liches and their flawed attempt to become immortal.<br /> <br /> One of the sample characters is Baphomet, a twisted 900 year old mage thing.<br /> <br /> All that said, since people seem to have an issue with transhumanity, lets keep in mind the topic is about mages attempting to achieve immortality in a world where immortals exist, and even immortal mages exist, with caveats, while also depicting a world where mundane science has been attempting to unlock the secrets of longer life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:02:30-07:00","id":947098,"title":"","content":"I remember reading about the Transhuman Engineers and thinking &quot;oh thank god, a transhumanist splat that aren't mustache-twirling bad guys&quot;. They almost got me to give Mage another chance, because of how much I liked them. <br /> <br /> *sad trombone noise*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:23:14-07:00","id":947111,"title":"","content":"And then it turns out they're just a group of Energizer Bunnies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:25:10-07:00","id":947115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947082#post947082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Approaching this from a gameplay and roleplaying perspective instead of a real-world moral one, I could not play a character who did not want to be immortal. My desire to live forever is such an integral part of who I am that I could not effectively portray someone who didn't have it. I have played characters with wildly different beliefs and personalities and ideologies from my own, but the idea of accepting or even celebrating mortality is so utterly alien and abhorrent to me that I could never get into the role of someone who felt that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that is true then there isn't going to be any kind of satisfactory conclusion to this discussion, because you've just expressed that you are unable to entertain any other perspective. The game as written is not designed to incorporate this concept because it goes against the themes the game is purposed to revolve around. If you want to hack it that's your business, but its work you've got to put in if you want it that badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:28:00-07:00","id":947119,"title":"","content":"Supposedly he has, nearly all of his posts make reference to his homebrew and how it will be more suited to his sensibilities which raises the question of is that actually contributing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:30:19-07:00","id":947123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947119#post947119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supposedly he has, nearly all of his posts make reference to his homebrew and how it will be more suited to his sensibilities which raises the question of is that actually contributing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really a question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:40:57-07:00","id":947127,"title":"","content":"Gotta leverage the Brand (TM).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:01:37-07:00","id":947140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947043#post947043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this comes back to my central problem with Awakening: mages aren't really monsters. I agree that in a horror setting immortality should make you monstrous, but major splats should ALREADY be monsters. Once you Awaken, you should already recognizably be an inhuman monster. That's what ChroD is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't start as monsters, but they become them.<br /> <br /> The desire to avoid death ultimately comes down to fear of it, which equates to fear of change or the loss of continuity of self, and Mage (and Promethean) take up the philosophical position that you should really just relax and not fear the Reaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:15:57-07:00","id":947152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947098#post947098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading about the Transhuman Engineers and thinking &amp;quot;oh thank god, a transhumanist splat that aren't mustache-twirling bad guys&amp;quot;. They almost got me to give Mage another chance, because of how much I liked them. <br /> <br /> *sad trombone noise*</div> </div> </div> </div>Gecko, I consider us friends, but do you need to rag on how much you dislike the games as written every single thread, regardless of topic? There's nothing wrong with not liking things, but please. It wears on and on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:29:36-07:00","id":947160,"title":"","content":"People tend to, for whatever reason, automatically equate immortality with the fear of death. That's a very limited point of view. For me, immortality is not about the fear of dying, it's about living to see humanity reach the stars, about living in a glorious new world full wonder, it's about <i>hope</i>. And I'm definitely not the only transhumanist who thinks like that. People often tend to jump to conclusions about other individual's opinions and beliefs witout getting to truly *know* those people and what they hold dear.<br /> <br /> Some people feel that they were born in the wrong body. Many transhumanists feel they were born in the wrong <i>age</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:35:54-07:00","id":947164,"title":"","content":"The transhuman engineers are a GREAT transhumanist legacy. They're dedicated to advancing and spreading the technological infrastructure throughout the sleeping world while they themselves are starting to outgrow it. They are engineering a better, more connected and informed future for everyone with every bit of tech they can get their grubby little paws on by hook or crook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:29:23-07:00","id":947198,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please stay on topic or the thread will be closed. Discussing people's posting history is not on topic, if you feel there is a problem with another user's posts then use the flag function. Thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:34:14-07:00","id":947201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947050#post947050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage isn't a Transhumanist game. Neither is Exalted. There is a vocal faction of pro-transhumanist fans of those games (especially on this and the last forums) that have latched onto those games in the past and claimed that they totally are transhumanist but then spend a whole lot of time nit-picking all the stuff that doesn't jive with what they claim transhumanism is.<br /> <br /> Mage has never ever been a &quot;transhumanist game about transcending human limits and becoming posthuman entities&quot;, it's always been a game about humans who are given power and what they do with it. Even the mightiest archmage is still just a human with a lot of power. Trying to compare throwing fireballs and flying (which the setting says is okay) to immortality (which the setting says isn't okay) is splitting hairs. The game isn't about all this power that you can never use ever. It's a game of modern mages, not posthumans who used Awakening as a stepping stone to the Singularity.<br /> <br /> The fact that you can squish and squeeze the game to the point where you can play that if you want is a point in it's favor, not a mark against it because that's not the core setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes this. I keep having to deal people over and over again. Especially with comparisions to classic and chronicles. You can play Classic in Chronicles, but playing chronicles in classic is so much headache. So much of the matieral in classic pushes that higher game state and continuely ignores the human aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:44:43-07:00","id":947276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947160#post947160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People tend to, for whatever reason, automatically equate immortality with the fear of death. That's a very limited point of view. For me, immortality is not about the fear of dying, it's about living to see humanity reach the stars, about living in a glorious new world full wonder, it's about <i>hope</i>. And I'm definitely not the only transhumanist who thinks like that. People often tend to jump to conclusions about other individual's opinions and beliefs witout getting to truly *know* those people and what they hold dear.<br /> <br /> Some people feel that they were born in the wrong body. Many transhumanists feel they were born in the wrong <i>age</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That too. Though that's more of out of universe argument. I would be lying if I didn't say I had a burning, all consuming fear of death and mortality, but I do also want to extend my life to see what the future holds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T17:55:39-07:00","id":947357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947018#post947018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, there's the crossover problem. If mortality is a such a big whanging deal for Mages, it kinda shoots a hole in that.<br /> <br /> And entropy isn't an obstacle to removing brains from bodies, preserving them, and placing them in unaging cybernetic bodies, which seems like the best bet for immortality in real life.<br /> <br /> And there's that pesky, lazy deathism again. You could say that not being able to fly is part of the human condition, and that riding in an airplane makes a Mage a Lich.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I see the issue here. It's not that &quot;mages think&quot; a concept like death is unfruitful. It's pretty much proven not to be. It's that it's literally one of the cornerstones of reality.<br /> <br /> You seem to be in a bit of denial there.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Active Deathism:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NdHJ0u5cLB0\" data-code=\"NdHJ0u5cLB0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NdHJ0u5cLB0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:22:47-07:00","id":947377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947357#post947357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I see the issue here. It's not that &amp;quot;mages think&amp;quot; a concept like death is unfruitful. It's pretty much proven not to be. It's that it's literally one of the cornerstones of reality.<br /> <br /> You seem to be in a bit of denial there.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Active Deathism:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NdHJ0u5cLB0\" data-code=\"NdHJ0u5cLB0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NdHJ0u5cLB0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't deny that in the setting of Awakening death is one of the core elements of reality. <br /> <br /> I just think that:<br /> <br /> A. That's kinda dumb<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> B. Even if death is one of the core elements of reality, enlightened superwizards would still try to overcome it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:15:27-07:00","id":947412,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that Entropy IS a problem and a consideration for brain in jar shenanigans. Everyone of your cells are breaking down. And your body continuously has to rebuild itself with nutrients and protein. Your brain would start to break down at a much higher rate, outside it's design bone housing department.<br /> <br /> And really when you look at it. Most if not all the arcane are tied to a person if not explicitly then implicitly. You are tied to a location and a time. You are the collective of a mind spirit soul and life in one package. Fate is your foot steps. Prime is the fact of you. Forces and Matter are a little tough for me to tag down. You certainly product forces and incorporate inorganic matter within your body. Need that daily Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:22:43-07:00","id":947417,"title":"","content":"Your body having to rebuild itself would be a lot easier to handle if your body was an easily replaceable shell. Besides, I have no doubt that's it's possible to develop a much more efficient container for the brain that the human body. <br /> <br /> Not sure how the second part in any way relates to the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:11:17-07:00","id":947467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947377#post947377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B. Even if death is one of the core elements of reality, enlightened superwizards would still try to overcome it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I have good news for you! there are superwizards that try to overcome it! They're called Liches. Some of them eat souls! Some of them engineer themselves perfect unchanging physical forms. Some of them hop from body to body as old ones wear out. Some of them simply steal years from other people. They're not exactly what you can call 'enlightened'.<br /> <br /> Part of enlightenment in mage is that you understand how existence is more than just the sum of your life experiences and that death has a spiritual meaning that at some point possesses more value than more time on earth. The Fallen world is a Lie that seeks to trap people within it, a prisoner that kills themselves seeking to escape it is just as trapped as someone that bricks themselves into their cell forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:41:14-07:00","id":947481,"title":"","content":"I much prefer the suggestion that death and mortality are parts of the Lie. After all, they make a handy way for Seers to keep people scared and busy. That's what I'd go for if I ever played or ran Awakening instead of Transgression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:42:38-07:00","id":947483,"title":"","content":"Your Brain is INCLUDED in that rebuilding. Stop ignoring biology.<br /> <br /> Second Point being In this metaverse (and in some ideologies) you are more than flesh and bone. Those ideas have sever implications. Trying to do without any one of those would have disastrous effects. All you'd have to look at are the Liches. They changed a fundamental part of their nature/soul and it back fired with weird additional effects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:46:33-07:00","id":947487,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about rebuilding. I'm talking about preserving the brain and moving it to a robotic body. <br /> <br /> And I'm saying that that just doesn't resonate with me, and I just don't see the way it's handled as good writing or worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:53:34-07:00","id":947492,"title":"","content":"Immortality's doable.<br /> <br /> Summoners has pacts you can make with other beings for it. And the Tremere aren't the only legacy trying to get it. The Scions of God also seek a way to become immortal by turning into ephemeral beings. There's the aforementioned ascension. And that's just factoring in Mage and not the other lines.<br /> <br /> It's not a simple spell to cast, and it likely has some conditions, but it seems pretty doable.<br /> <br /> While the passage may label any mage who wants to live forever as having deeply rooted issues, mages live in the World of Darkness and aren't above such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Fixed as archmastery doesn't grant immortality 08-19-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:57:30-07:00","id":947495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947481#post947481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I much prefer the suggestion that death and mortality are parts of the Lie. After all, they make a handy way for Seers to keep people scared and busy. That's what I'd go for if I ever played or ran Awakening instead of Transgression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested in this. What makes death and mortality more naturally part of the Lie? They seem like a pretty huge and pointless thing to add to the universe. After all, they make any status quo the Exarchs try to build much less easily maintained. It's been said that dictatorships cannot last as long as humans are mortal, after all, and while Exarchs have supernally transcended that particular consideration, their servants haven't.<br /> You seem to be using your conclusions as your axioms - death must be opposed at all costs, therefore death is monstrous, therefore...<br /> I'm not particularly against immortality; if I could just ignore the laws of the universe, and set my own, I think I'd make death an opt-in sort of program. But you seem to begin with your conclusion. How are the setting and the stories one can tell in it improved by making it easy to avoid, without consequences or costs, one of the most basic unifying human experiences?<br /> <br /> Also, as to worldbuilding, I think the current state of Death in Mage is far more interesting than the version you suggest, and the setting implications and construction of lichdom far more meaningful as humanism than they would be in your transhumanist construction. We have Eclipse Phase for transhuman horror, after all, and that's not what Mage is about.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I'm surprised transhumanists are so upset at the idea that someone who will do what it takes to live forever in the setting doesn't have the normal thought processes of a human. Isn't that part of the point, to transcend humanity? Having a greater than average fear of death seems like a reasonable take on someone doing anything they can to escape its clutches; I imagine anyone trying their hardest to escape vampires and defend themselves from bloodsuckers in the CoD has a 'greater than average fear of vampires' as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3547,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","user":"SonOfSilkAndStone","date":". 08-10-2016, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:04:46-07:00","id":947500,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm not at all upset about the search for immortality being connected to inhumanity in a horror game. <br /> <br /> It's just that this is a setting where you can be a vampire, a werewolf, a mummy, or a demon- and all of those creatures are treated with a great deal of depth and sympathy despite being obviously inhuman and monstrous. Why do immortal mages not get the same treatment? <br /> <br /> And why the hell can't I be a mad scientist, anyway?<br /> <br /> About the first part, if I were going to play Awakening instead of Transgression, I see Awakening as a dark but hopeful game about enlightened heroes fighting against an evil conspiracy that controls reality. That's an obvious setup for a story about fighting not just the laws of society but of reality itself. And challenging the dominant narrative that mortality is necessary and good would be an excellent addition.<br /> <br /> Now, &quot;magic heroes beat up death and everyone lives happily ever after forever&quot; does not fit in a horror game at all, but I've never considered Awakening to be a horror game. In Transgression, immortality inevitably makes you inhuman to some degree, but it's much more easy to obtain and much less hazardous than many other uses of magic (it's not even a Wisdom infraction, unless it's done in a particularly reckless way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:18:21-07:00","id":947514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947487#post947487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about rebuilding. I'm talking about preserving the brain and moving it to a robotic body.<br /> <br /> And I'm saying that that just doesn't resonate with me, and I just don't see the way it's handled as good writing or worldbuilding.</div> </div> </div> </div>No you're not getting it. Your body is Literally Rebuilding itself because it has to. that is it's method of preservation. Removing any part of it for any amount of time, can be very determintional. And thats in the lightest language. And because rebuilding IS it's method, that dictates that Deconstruction is also going on. And Therefore Entropy is in the system. I know it's really weird to think about Life in terms of deconstruction/Entropy but this is a base understanding<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://acufitliving.com/acufitlifestyle/wp-content/uploads/2013/04/body-rebuilds.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:18:54-07:00","id":947515,"title":"","content":"Did I say being inhuman made you be evil? I just said, 'having extreme fear of death compared to human normal' makes you abnormal for a human. It seems like a logical reason someone would go all the way and make themselves a Morphean, or a Ghost Mage, or what have you. There are plenty of forms of lich other than Tremere, Tremere are just the most successful.<br /> Actually, Morpheans seem right up the typical transhumanist alley - their great weakness is that they can't change, at all, and remain fixed as a certain concept, but that's actually a positive if you want to live forever as yourself. There are, obviously, downsides to the condition, but that just makes it interesting.<br /> <br /> Plus, I just remembered: many mages do see immortality for everyone as a decent part of their endgame - Hieraconis, the Silver Ladder name for the perfect city yet to come, is theorized by one wizard as containing not only every living soul but every dead soul as well, so that it encompasses all humanity. That's resurrection right there.<br /> Just, they see it as a communal goal, and there are so many ways the world can be improved right now and the Exarchs fought that are much more fruitful than personally living forever. Surely you'd agree that death can be more effectively fought, right now, by helping administer vaccines in the developing world? That's what the Pentacle is trying to do - help everyone, not just themselves. Liches chose personal salvation from change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:20:06-07:00","id":947518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947500#post947500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I'm not at all upset about the search for immortality being connected to inhumanity in a horror game.<br /> <br /> It's just that this is a setting where you can be a vampire, a werewolf, a mummy, or a demon- and all of those creatures are treated with a great deal of depth and sympathy despite being obviously inhuman and monstrous. Why do immortal mages not get the same treatment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the game is Mage, not Vampire. And even the core Vampire experience is at it's heart about Vampires who are only 3-30 years dead dealing with some vampires that are older than them, who represent what they might become. Further, in cases where immortal mages' immortality doesn't make up a great deal of their character (like Liches), the immortality aspect exists in a kind of footnote that doesn't matter as much compared to what they do. A chunk of the core Mage experience is about how there's a split between your Awakened life and your Sleeping life, but if you're immortal you've more than likely been forced to abandon any pretense at a regular life already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And why the hell can't I be a mad scientist, anyway? </div> </div> </div>The game is &quot;Mage&quot;, not &quot;Mad Scientist&quot;, so you can't really just ignore the need for magical trappings for pure mad science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:30:51-07:00","id":947525,"title":"","content":"In horror fiction, the archetypes of the wizard and the mad scientist are more or less the same. <br /> <br /> And as I've established, there are two settings we're talking about here: Awakening, which is about liberating people and reality from a vast cosmic conspiracy, and Transgression, which is a game of personal horror that draws from the conventions of horror media. <br /> <br /> And that chart is based on debunked assumptions that don't even reflect on what I'm saying. There are cells and structures in the brain that do not replace themselves at all. Immortality, in its basest essence, means keeping those alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:48:26-07:00","id":947537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947525#post947525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In horror fiction, the archetypes of the wizard and the mad scientist are more or less the same.<br /> <br /> And as I've established, there are two settings we're talking about here: Awakening, which is about liberating people and reality from a vast cosmic conspiracy, and Transgression, which is a game of personal horror that draws from the conventions of horror media.<br /> <br /> And that chart is based on debunked assumptions that don't even reflect on what I'm saying. There are cells and structures in the brain that do not replace themselves at all. Immortality, in its basest essence, means keeping those alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naw dude, you keep bringing up your home made game. What you do in your custom 'zine game that's totally cool doodz is your thing.<br /> <br /> But anyway, you aren't playing a wizard archetype when you're playing Mage the Awakening. You're playing an actual wizard. You're playing in a setting where the protagonists are granted the understanding that while science is a thing that works, it is unable to quantify the higher truths because it's intristic to the Fallen world and thus is unable to fully interface with the higher realms where magic comes from.<br /> <br /> You can totally play a &quot;mad scientist&quot; though, a mage who uses arcana to learn more about the world around them so they can use science to learn more about it. Enchanting a telescope so it can see dark matter with Forces is totally a thing that you can do. But if you try and build an army of battle robots, you're just making war golems. Your laser is just an enchanted magic wand with a different physical appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:52:39-07:00","id":947541,"title":"","content":"Splitting hairs. It's a layman's chart, but The sentiment is still the same. Your body deconstructs and reconstructs. To different degrees, but thats the truth. To lose any part is problematic. Yes you can lose alot of things. You need blood flow you need protein. Talking Head in a Jar is pure mad science. Not that you can't pull it off in universe Its just NOT easy and probably wouldn't give you the result you wish. If I may steal from Vamp real quick. That game is about trying to keep as much of your former human self, as you slowly realize you no longer work / think like a normal human anymore<br /> <br /> Yes you can play Awakening as The Matrix, but that's not it's selling point. It's about people with the power's of Gods, but the Understanding of Babes. and all the drama therewithin<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_19370_the-6-most-frequently-quoted-brain-facts-that-are-total-bs_p2.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cracked.com/article_19370...tal-bs_p2.html</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XqJWSyUbmkw\" data-code=\"XqJWSyUbmkw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XqJWSyUbmkw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:05:10-07:00","id":947548,"title":"","content":"To be honest, trying to read your posts is giving me a bit of a headache, and I really don't think trying to engage with you would be productive. <br /> <br /> As for our nun friend, I don't think Awakening handles that as well as it could. Besides, Awakening does actually have a generally pro-science bent as opposed to Ascension.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly the point. A mad scientist's devices might as well be magic. That's what divides mad science from actual science, and it's what Genius nailed so perfectly. <br /> <br /> But the topic at hand is immortality in Awakening, and I think all has been said about that that can be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:14:28-07:00","id":947554,"title":"","content":"There's a huge gulf between &quot;might as well be magic&quot; and &quot;actually is magic&quot; though. Even Doctor Doom, a mad scientist and sorcerer uses them as two different tools. His doombots might have wards placed on them, but the doombots themselves aren't magical. <br /> <br /> Frankly, it seems like a lot of unnecessary work to transform Mage into Genius-light when all you end up doing is watering down mage stuff and genius stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:16:14-07:00","id":947555,"title":"","content":"Eh, not really. I've found it's not that hard at all. Of the design challenges I've had with MtT, making magic and mad science equally viable and present has been incredibly easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:33:15-07:00","id":947563,"title":"","content":"Good for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:20:34-07:00","id":947578,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://orig06.deviantart.net/1cfa/f/2013/101/0/8/robobrain_by_yellow_jelly-d61dgfc.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> When that chive Scienist comes around the corner with a robotic shell and brain fluid, Just say its a bad idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:22:41-07:00","id":947604,"title":"","content":"We kind of totally left the actual topic of the Thread, which is: &quot;Why is immortality such a big deal?&quot; and I simply assume this is meant for MtA and not any other game. And while a lot of people have discussed if it <i>should</i> or <i>should not</i> be a deal, I'd like to go back on the fact why it actually <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> The answer is relatively simple: because it is either not easily achieved (ascension), hard to sustain and risky (having active magic on you your whole life) or done with ethically doubious methods (soul stealing, body stealing, ghost mages, etc.). There has been no sustainable argument that any of this is actually easy to do. If you want to transport your brain into a robot, you simply don't ackknoledge the problems with this. First: you most likely need active magic to build a robot/golem which is actually practical as a body, because simple walking is an insanely difficult to programm thing for a robot, which can only lately be done. Try running and climbing next. Second, you basically lose all natural senses and I cannot understand how anybody not find this problemetic with your sense of self conscience and any human empathy degenerating. And third: you don't really gain anything. If you still want to use your brain, your brain has to live and therefore it still ages. Alzheimer's and dementia are a thing and what good is that perfect robot, if your 100 years old brain can't do anything more but drooling.<br /> <br /> If you want immortality for your mage you just don't get past this. You either go for ascension, lose your humanity or steal the life of other people, if this is no big deal for your character: no real problem there, but most people would likely call your character a psychopath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:50:25-07:00","id":947609,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the probably safer options is regularly creating new bodies to inhabit. If done as an Attainment it has the added benefit of avoiding some of the weaknesses of such spells, mainly the dispell issue. Unwise? Maybe. Inmoral? Hardly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T02:20:25-07:00","id":947620,"title":"","content":"Safer, but still not easier and still ethically dubious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T02:36:28-07:00","id":947625,"title":"","content":"That probably is the most moral version of it, but you still need to create a <i>lasting </i>new body. This is not done with a &quot;simple&quot; making spell. Or you risk, that the creation of the body can be dispelled. Then transfer your mind into it whith a spell that can be dispelled, too. You can probably create a legacy, which does make it harder to dispell this stuff, but you won't get it undispellable. So yes, while this is debatable not much worse, than simply tatooing your body with regeneration runes, it has nearly the same problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T02:57:57-07:00","id":947633,"title":"","content":"In a game if a PC worked that method out I'd throw in further complications to keep it interesting, the Death part of their Pattern slowly growing in spite of their mind-exchanges, starting to accrue Destiny to drive them toward dying. I mean, make it a real challenge so if they succeed it's more rewarding because they didn't just work out a clever trick, they defeated the universe itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:23:47-07:00","id":947647,"title":"","content":"Well, an exemplar of a Legacy could do it if they took an Attainment of a 4 dot spell that changes living matter of an animal (or really any non sapient life) into a living human body as a five dot Attainment. They would have the necessary 2 Reach for a Lasting effect as a narrative Reach option and Attainments are flexible enough that using the Reach option should be possible for an 8 Gnosis exemplar.<br /> <br /> The Optional effect could be a Mind Attainment that replicates the Possession spell (errata'd as a Mind 4 spell). In this case, the 'possession' would be easier, as you would not have to share the new body with anyone and the mechanics should reflect that. Even if they didn't, the result would be the same as above.<br /> <br /> Even if the 2 Reach effect wasn't possible, the Mage would still earn an effect lasting for one year and the only thing they would have to do differently in comparison to a normal human is essentially painlessly killing one living non-sapient organism a year. When you consider the amount of hamburgers we eat over a year, it's a proverbial drop in the ocean.<br /> <br /> As for anything being called 'ethically dubious', that's just a phrase that always has to refer to a philosophical stance it's derived from. Without that it's meaningless. I'm fine with killing a fly, yet some people would have a big problem with that. I respect their decision, but they will always abhore the life I live. Some people call creating a new body for oneself abhorrent. Their fundamental beliefs are likely very different from mine. And so I just don't care.<br /> <br /> That said, I would definitely add complications, but I prefer the 'Ochemata are going to seriously come gunning after you' kind over the mechanical ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-10-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T04:02:54-07:00","id":947655,"title":"","content":"Exemplars of legacies tend to Ascend anyway, though you seem to be referring to masters of legacies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the fact that some would object to your method is exactly what I mean by it still being morally dubious. It's fine if you don't care, there are story repercussions regardless. On top of that I felt it was pretty obvious I think it's appropriate to go beyond merely mechanical road blocks to make obtaining immortality a possibility. Ochemata would certainly factor in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T04:16:44-07:00","id":947660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947655#post947655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exemplars of legacies tend to Ascend anyway, though you seem to be referring to masters of legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity's sake: In the 2E Legacies blog comments, Dave referred to the mages who attained their 5. Attainment as Exemplars. Some Exemplars apparently get a new mystery play at some point of their life and some of them Ascend at the end of it (the 'Final Attainment').","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:16:03-07:00","id":947682,"title":"","content":"Sorry to play the wise guy again, but there is no &quot;lasting&quot; effect for 2 reach. You can get infinite duration for 2 reach, which is close to the same for an attainment, since you cannot dispell an attainment, but it is not exactly the same. So yeah you can probably create a legacy with a 5 dot attainment combining a 4 dot shapechanging spell from Life, changing an animal into a human and then posess that changed body with Mind 4 both for indefinite duration. This way though, you would not have full control of the body, because you can neither wipe the mind of the animal with the same spell (Mind 5), nor can you create a body with no mind out of thin air (Life 5).<br /> So while totally doable and ethically easier to defend then just snatching the body of your nephew e.g. it's still no easy tast and has significant setbacks. These rules btw are their to underline the narrative and the narrative is: gaining immortality isn't easy and/or comes with a cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:21:01-07:00","id":947687,"title":"","content":"He might be referring to that one rule that says if a spell could logically have a Lasting effect you can append that descriptor to it for 2 Reach. Pg. 127, though that shouldn't apply since the effects can or at least should be able to be reversed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:25:27-07:00","id":947689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947682#post947682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to play the wise guy again, but there is no &quot;lasting&quot; effect for 2 reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I referred to the narrative Reach effects described in Creative Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Regarding insufficient number of Attainments, you could have two Legacies with compatible Attainments, but that's not even necessary as a Mind 5 spell, that can destroy memories can be used as a Lasting effect anyway. It doesn't even have to be an Attainment.<br /> <br /> That said, it doesn't change the fact that the universe would probably try to kill you. Exarchs like status quo, all else equal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd.<br /> <br /> I would *really* like to know, what exactly they mean by 'reversed', and not just because of cheating death spells. The definition seems terribly unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-10-2016, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:34:40-07:00","id":947691,"title":"","content":"How would spells to steal life / lifespan / years look anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:36:28-07:00","id":947693,"title":"","content":"I kind of feel like it's just a weird rule to have in there altogether, it doesn't really seem to fit in well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:38:01-07:00","id":947694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947691#post947691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would spells to steal life / lifespan / years look anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Patterning, maybe Unraveling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:44:49-07:00","id":947699,"title":"","content":"How would you perceive a Mage who takes year of your Life/Youth/Etc in exchange for tasks? Basically, as a currency? Assume that both sides are aware of the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:47:16-07:00","id":947701,"title":"","content":"As a non-coercive transaction it's probably less bad than other methods. I'd be worried about the temptation to abuse it though, with obfuscating contracts and what not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:56:22-07:00","id":947703,"title":"","content":"Sounds like something that could work and not be branded Left-Handed if the Life-Taker would be bound by specific Fate contracts that would check for abuses and coercion. I kinda like this idea, so anyone could explore it before going back to the brains in the jar :P?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T06:54:55-07:00","id":947735,"title":"","content":"Nothing in Mage's cosmology inherently says immortality is bad.<br /> Sure the Death Arcanum is an important part of reality, but that doesn't mean striving to overcome one's death is necessarily wrong.<br /> <br /> Liches make compromises, both of a moral and pragmatic nature; Tremere subsist on souls, Morpheans are unchanging, etc. Other forms of immortality are either unreliable or make a person exceedingly vulnerable.<br /> The lesson here isn't &quot;Don't strive for immortality&quot;, but rather &quot;Immortality has a price&quot;. I would say that that price is usually worth paying, unless someone else suffers as a result. While I'd love it in real life, in a game I don't find problem-free immortality that interesting; if anything I would have it be the sort of thing which comes at the end of a long story, if not an entire Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Also? Ascension is -literally- Transhumanism. It may not be the same sort of Transhumanism that is usually talked about, but it's still fundamentally the same thing. I'm not saying this because I'm personally a Transhumanist, but because it follows the definition perfectly; the belief that Humanity can evolve beyond its current limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 08-10-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:48:51-07:00","id":947766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947699#post947699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you perceive a Mage who takes year of your Life/Youth/Etc in exchange for tasks? Basically, as a currency? Assume that both sides are aware of the deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could imagen a deal with the devil kind of interaction. Deals done in the back alley, Contract Law, The mysterious Merchant, The token trade, Or even the Device! Or like something from Demon The Descent might be on the nose. It should all be coached in the symbolism that both parties can understand. Even if it only kind of makes sence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:00:26-07:00","id":947831,"title":"","content":"Now I'm hitting a roadblock with the Tremere in Transgression. I want to keep them, but at the same time I want immortality to be something that's fairly easy to obtain. So I need to give them another reason to take souls. I like the idea that they can use the souls for other things- like using them as batteries for magic or as shields to absorb Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:09:25-07:00","id":947841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947831#post947831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm hitting a roadblock with the Tremere in Transgression. I want to keep them, but at the same time I want immortality to be something that's fairly easy to obtain. So I need to give them another reason to take souls. I like the idea that they can use the souls for other things- like using them as batteries for magic or as shields to absorb Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Left-Handed Legacies were always treated as organizations that recruit members through underhanded means. Lying to and misguiding new mages was always a part of their recruitment efforts. Also, Tremere consider immortality a <i>bonus</i>. Their main goal is to consume souls for the 'Watchtower of the Soul' - in reality probably either the Abyss or an asshole Bound.<br /> <br /> I think you will be just fine representing them as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-10-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:12:01-07:00","id":947843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947831#post947831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm hitting a roadblock with the Tremere in Transgression. I want to keep them, but at the same time I want immortality to be something that's fairly easy to obtain. So I need to give them another reason to take souls. I like the idea that they can use the souls for other things- like using them as batteries for magic or as shields to absorb Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go that route the problem is that it needs to be something sufficiently enticing that someone would potentially be tempted to steal souls to do it without being such a prize that it baffles some people why others find its pursuit morally objectionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:46:12-07:00","id":947870,"title":"","content":"Hm, yeah. Transgression doesn't have Watchtowers, but it does have the Abyss. It could be that the Tremere are serving an Abyssal Disassociation that wants to destroy the concept of death itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:47:48-07:00","id":947871,"title":"","content":"Actually re-reading the Lich section of mage, there's nothing saying that Lichdom is actually a <i>difficult</i> thing to accomplish. It says that inexperienced mages can do it by applying Life or Death based spells to themselves with indefinite duration, but there's always going to be the risk of someone messing the spell up and the consequences only get more dire the longer you've been running around with the spells on you. The means to join a Lichdom legacy probably aren't altogether to difficult for someone to accomplish if they bend their full attention to it either, Liches of various types are common enough that people can get ahold of them to question them about their expert knowledge after all (even if it's socially unacceptable to admit it).<br /> <br /> I'm of the mind that Longevity spells weren't included in the book because they're a waste of word count for an effect that doesn't actually have any meaningful mechanical impact. Your standard immortality tattoo/scarification spell probably is a Death 2 shielding spell or a Life 3 perfecting spell tricked out with indefinite duration and bound with said tattoos/scars. Body hopping is probably a Death/Life 4 patterning spell. Binding your ghost to your body is probably a Death 4 patterning effect as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T11:15:02-07:00","id":947892,"title":"","content":"At least one longevity spell was included, go look in Time 2, and no longevity isn't hard, but there's always a price. If you go with spells it can be undone, that's the price easy to achieve to destroy.<br /> <br /> Body hopping is Death and Mind to remove their soul and mind and transplant your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T11:47:46-07:00","id":947916,"title":"","content":"You didn't need Mind to play Body Snatcher in the last edition and I'm disinclined to require it now. Nothing wrong with having a Mind variant though, there's a sidebar somewhere that says using different arcana to do the same thing isn't a bad thing.<br /> <br /> The point is that prohibitions against Lichdom are primarily social in nature. Mages that pursue it either have to hide it or more commonly remove themselves from mainstream awakened society. Mainstream Awakened society is against Lichdom because it goes against the understood underpinnings of the supernatural, but Liches don't care about that because they're obsessed with not dying. That obsession is the practical problematic aspect of it, because if you're still relying on spells to maintain your youth and life in a harmless fashion, you are utterly dependent on them not failing. If someone has spent their life staying young eventually their only options are going to be actually dying forever (which they have spent their lives avoiding) or going further into a form of Lichdom that isn't so fragile or close to moral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:15:13-07:00","id":947942,"title":"","content":"I'm just citing Dave who said it'd require Death and Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:26:19-07:00","id":948000,"title":"","content":"Meh. You can say Dave said whatever he wants but even if you linked a quote, until he publishes it I'm not taking it as gospel.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:35:19-07:00","id":948007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=948000#post948000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. You can say Dave said whatever he wants but even if you linked a quote, until he publishes it I'm not taking it as gospel.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But how? I mean, mind seems like its super needed to transfer your consciousness into a new body. How you would even do it without Mind?<br /> <br /> (Note: I really don't know 1st ed, so this is 2ed only)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:52:33-07:00","id":948025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=948000#post948000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. You can say Dave said whatever he wants but even if you linked a quote, until he publishes it I'm not taking it as gospel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm aware. Like I said I'm just reporting what I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=948007#post948007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how? I mean, mind seems like its super needed to transfer your consciousness into a new body. How you would even do it without Mind?<br /> <br /> (Note: I really don't know 1st ed, so this is 2ed only)</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e the FC book had a Death spell that let you put your soul in a target and destroy their soul as it was booted out. Some Masters of Death used it as a favored method for taking out foes during the Nameless War. It didn't require Mind and it's what TidyGamer is referring to. I agree though, it probably ought to involve Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-10-2016, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:56:13-07:00","id":948030,"title":"","content":"<b>Especially</b> in 2ed, simply moving the soul is insufficient to move the mind. The only published hopping spell was in <i>The Free Council</i> and required Mind... (Edit: err, my bad. I finally checked and it required Death and Life. Apparently it was more of a wrapping another's flesh around your mind and soul intact. That said, though, I disagree with leaving Mind out...)<br /> <br /> If you want to ignore that, feel free, obviously, but you will probably want to come up with some consistent rules to apply.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ed:<br /> 2e Rules on soul transfer are on pp.97-98. These <i>do</i> cover this question, albeit only from the side of what happens to the personality <i>et alis</i> when a soul is missing or replaced. RAW is pretty clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":".  Finally Looked 08-11-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:05:20-07:00","id":948042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=948025#post948025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm aware. Like I said I'm just reporting what I know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In 1e the FC book had a Death spell that let you put your soul in a target and destroy their soul as it was booted out. Some Masters of Death used it as a favored method for taking out foes during the Nameless War. It didn't require Mind and it's what TidyGamer is referring to. I agree though, it probably ought to involve Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, definetly different in second ed.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> says, taking out your own soul would not take your personality (mind), only your drive. Putting it in another persons body won't do any body hopping. It would just be bad for you. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7195_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7195\" data-vbnamecard=\"7195\">TidyGamer</a>, that's how it works in the published material, no word of god needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:24:12-07:00","id":949850,"title":"","content":"You no longer need Life to turn yourself into living shadow. In some cases the Devs have expanded old spells into doing more than they could. I feel that body snatching should be able to be acomplished via death/life. I'm not opposed to a Mind variant. The Many Roads sidebar on page 124 says this is okay. I'm also extremely leery about encouraging Mind bloat, something that plagued 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:10:34-07:00","id":950017,"title":"","content":"I have no idea why you don't need Life to turn yourself into a shadow. I find that to be pretty inconsistent with other spells in the book. It's actually one of the first things I asked about in the FAQ thread but I didn't get a reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the spells so far (I'm up to Matter) look pretty solid, but then we have Matter and I'm left wondering what the hell happened. There's a spell to determine where hidden things are and if you add Forces it involves also finding electronic data on a device. Couldn't just straight Forces accomplish the same effect?<br /> <br /> Also, Shrink Object mentions that if you add Life 3 you can use this spell to effect living things, but shouldn't that be a straight function of Life? Why is Matter needed to shrink living beings?<br /> <br /> Death 4 allows you to change into living shadows without Life conjunction, Matter 4 does not grant the same. Isn't this inconsistent? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-13-2016, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:15:21-07:00","id":950018,"title":"","content":"Maybe Shadow of a person is a Death part of them, and you aren't transforming into something different, just switching proportions.<br /> ...yeah, it's a weak justification, I'm tired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:17:59-07:00","id":950019,"title":"","content":"I have no idea, I just know there are a number of spells that have seemingly inconsistent and illogical arcana combinations. Fortunately, it's the easiest thing in the world to houserule more consistent fixes, but it does make it difficult to have one of these kinds of conversations where everyone can come away with a different interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T04:19:09-07:00","id":950499,"title":"","content":"For PC's, immortality is largely irrelevant. The vast majority of PC's are in the prime of their lives, and it's doubtful the game will move at such a pace to change that.<br /> <br /> However, immortality can be a HUGE motivator for NPC's especially villainous ones. The fear of death is powerful, and can be used to excuse all kinds of heinous acts.<br /> <br /> Having immortality be something that can be gained simply, or as a natural outgrowth of arcane mastery, or without breaking any morals/mores, doesn't really add anything to the game. &quot;You reached Life 5. You can cast the immortality spell now. Good for you!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also the &quot;power mad mage in search of immortality&quot; is a genre staple and the game would suffer without it.<br /> <br /> As for the idea that living forever is a bad thing, or that having a 5000+ year lifespan upsets some natural order... I don't know if I buy that. The idea seems to be the flip side of &quot;death comes for everyone&quot; and having one person who can live forever while the rest of us have to go through this whole &quot;death&quot; thing doesn't seem terribly fair, but what else is new?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T05:38:33-07:00","id":950515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=947691#post947691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would spells to steal life / lifespan / years look anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to do that would be for a mage to run a stall at a goblin market or be in indentured servant at a goblin market. Service for years of youth deal. That said I think most mages would die of enemy mage/horrible thing in ruin/paradox explosion/hunter and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:35:03-07:00","id":950665,"title":"","content":"There was a spell for stealing lifespan in 1E that did not make the cut for 2E. Would it still be valid for creative thaumaturgy in 2E? <br /> It allows for this &quot;I am immmoooooortaaaal!&quot; thing but you're taking lifespan from someone else, bringing Wisdom and morality into play. I quite liked that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:06:52-07:00","id":950799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=950665#post950665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a spell for stealing lifespan in 1E that did not make the cut for 2E. Would it still be valid for creative thaumaturgy in 2E?<br /> It allows for this &quot;I am immmoooooortaaaal!&quot; thing but you're taking lifespan from someone else, bringing Wisdom and morality into play. I quite liked that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Bring the sacrifice to the alter. Hurry Before the Eilcipes wanes and we lose the aura from Venus.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also think of those spells as big set pieces. Like thats a plot hook of a rouge mage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:46:58-07:00","id":953114,"title":"","content":"At risk of reigniting this topic, but I finally read it and...<br /> <br /> Archmasters aren't immortal. They keep getting brought up as being immortal, but they're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:27:06-07:00","id":953154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=953114#post953114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At risk of reigniting this topic, but I finally read it and...<br /> <br /> Archmasters aren't immortal. They keep getting brought up as being immortal, but they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it *is* fairly easy to render themselves immortal through Imperial Practices, right? I recall something about Excising the Death from someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:05:00-07:00","id":953219,"title":"","content":"Why is immortality hard for mages?<br /> <br /> The Exarchs did it!<br /> <br /> Seriously. The majority of living mages does NOT serve the Exarchs. If they could live forever they would sooner or later reach archmastery and start to meddle in the Exarchs plans. So they did something to supernal magic. It can't be done any more.<br /> To <i>Supernal</i> magic that is. There are other sources of magic/power that doesn't have that problem and whom over the Exarchs doesn't have (anywhere near) as much influence.<br /> <br /> If you manage to reach archmastery I imagine you can shake of this Exarchic influence but until then you will have to ... improvise. Find other sources of power, or use supernal magics with imagination.<br /> <br /> Slowing down aging, or just living longer, should still be able to be done with (supernal) magic. It is such a basic thing of existance so that completely deleting any such supernal magics might have side effects like making healing impossible. It should be rather finicky and never result in immortality or unaging-ness (in my opinion). And easy fixes comes with drawbacks. Look at Veil of Moments (Time 2), even the most powerful version makes you unable to spend XP (but you can still accrue it? Weird, I'd make gaining beats impossible as well). Making your body remarkably fit and able to live into your 150's, or stretching out your remaining time so that it takes a week to age a day, should (in my opinion) be possible with (advanced) supernal magic, but not outright immortality.<br /> <br /> Tremmies do it with soul-devouring. And attainments, which, if I understand it correctly, isn't quite supernal magic.<br /> <br /> This would all be under-the-hood immortality. You could cast a fairly simple (Life 3/Time 3) or some such spell and remain a certain age forever. But if the spell gets dispelled you'd revert to your 'True' age.<br /> <br /> <br /> TL, DR: The Exarchs made immortality impossible through supernal magic. Seek out other sources of power or reach Archmastery and shake of the influence of the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah ... easy immortality is <i>boring</i>. In a Horror game? If you <i>do </i>accomplish it, there should be a Price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:26:05-07:00","id":953238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=953154#post953154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it *is* fairly easy to render themselves immortal through Imperial Practices, right? I recall something about Excising the Death from someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quintessences by definition do not come cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:49:08-07:00","id":953838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gammelbraxen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=953219#post953219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL, DR: The Exarchs made immortality impossible through supernal magic. Seek out other sources of power or reach Archmastery and shake of the influence of the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah ... easy immortality is <i>boring</i>. In a Horror game? If you <i>do </i>accomplish it, there should be a Price.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think there doesn't have to be.<br /> What originally drew me to Mage is that generally there's no capital-P Price for magic.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's always a price for anything really, if you choose to look at it that way, but unlike for lesser magics, true (Supernal) Magic is deep understanding and immense power with price that a devoted athlete (or devoted anything that takes effort) would laugh at. And the Horror, to me, is in that. Who are you when you have unadulturated power?<br /> <br /> Personally, if I ever do manage to gather a table to play (I am scheming XD ) I will allow the Death 5 Steal Lifespan spell in 2E. Which is a great example both for this topic and for why I don't like 'But it has a Price' motiff for Mage.<br /> You can steal someone's life, with no consequence to yourself, if you scheme it well. And the horror comes from the result of this.<br /> To be clear, not that you have more years to your life. As a DM/GM/Storyteller, that elves can live 700 years and dwarves 500 and humans 100 is rather inconsequential to my campaign. Same for Mages. Lifespan of 80 years or 100? 100 or 200? You'll live as long as it's convenient for the game.<br /> The result is who you are afterwards. You're a person who stole someone's life.<br /> The two key versions of the aftermath of the Wisdom degeneration roll (for I would insist on this even at Wisdom 3, maybe not 2). You will either succeed on your roll and fell bad about it, properly guilty and troubled (Guilty Condition or not, you did some deep shit) or you will fail and become more of a monster. A person (when can that term stop applying, eh?) who's fine with stealing someone's life. What other acts are inconsequential in your pursuit of Mysteries, of power, of whatever Obsession drags you into the depts of Gnosis.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:51:10-07:00","id":954017,"title":"","content":"What even would be the quintessence for casting a spell that removed your ability to die?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:32:09-07:00","id":954062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954017#post954017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What even would be the quintessence for casting a spell that removed your ability to die?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about the remains of something immortal (not just ageless) that somehow died, thus upsetting 'the balance' and creating an opening. In other words, something that should be unable to die died, and now you make something else unable to die to counterbalance it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T16:48:08-07:00","id":954100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=953838#post953838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to think there doesn't have to be.<br /> What originally drew me to Mage is that generally there's no capital-P Price for magic.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's always a price for anything really, if you choose to look at it that way, but unlike for lesser magics, true (Supernal) Magic is deep understanding and immense power with price that a devoted athlete (or devoted anything that takes effort) would laugh at. And the Horror, to me, is in that. Who are you when you have unadulturated power?<br /> <br /> Personally, if I ever do manage to gather a table to play (I am scheming XD ) I will allow the Death 5 Steal Lifespan spell in 2E. Which is a great example both for this topic and for why I don't like 'But it has a Price' motiff for Mage.<br /> You can steal someone's life, with no consequence to yourself, if you scheme it well. And the horror comes from the result of this.<br /> To be clear, not that you have more years to your life. As a DM/GM/Storyteller, that elves can live 700 years and dwarves 500 and humans 100 is rather inconsequential to my campaign. Same for Mages. Lifespan of 80 years or 100? 100 or 200? You'll live as long as it's convenient for the game.<br /> The result is who you are afterwards. You're a person who stole someone's life.<br /> The two key versions of the aftermath of the Wisdom degeneration roll (for I would insist on this even at Wisdom 3, maybe not 2). You will either succeed on your roll and fell bad about it, properly guilty and troubled (Guilty Condition or not, you did some deep shit) or you will fail and become more of a monster. A person (when can that term stop applying, eh?) who's fine with stealing someone's life. What other acts are inconsequential in your pursuit of Mysteries, of power, of whatever Obsession drags you into the depts of Gnosis.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a good explanation of why immortality often has some kind of Price, in Mage and other media. Putting a Price on something so many people desire so strongly asks how much you're willing to sacrifice for it. The steeper the Price, the more it says about the priorities of those who are willing to pay it. Is extending your own life worth ending another? What about several others? Does it matter which others? Those are interesting questions. Though, there is something to be said for making the trade off tempting for the players to earnestly consider it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:58:58-07:00","id":954129,"title":"","content":"I hope we can see a future description of how to become a Morphean, and what one looks like in play. Immortality at the cost of becoming little more than a vessel for your Obsessions seeks like the ultimate in-theme endgame for Mage.<br /> <br /> Plus they make for fun baddies, both in Mage and as unexpected surprises in Changeling and Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T20:23:57-07:00","id":954171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954017#post954017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What even would be the quintessence for casting a spell that removed your ability to die?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:46:25-07:00","id":954320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=953114#post953114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At risk of reigniting this topic, but I finally read it and...<br /> <br /> Archmasters aren't immortal. They keep getting brought up as being immortal, but they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the earlier text suggested Archmasters convert bodily into a soul leading to the assumption that they must stop aging. I don't suppose you are splitting hairs between ageless and immortal, so what happens to Archmages now, if it has been covered? Are they more or less normal except for their magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T06:28:46-07:00","id":954338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954100#post954100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a good explanation of why immortality often has some kind of Price, in Mage and other media. Putting a Price on something so many people desire so strongly asks how much you're willing to sacrifice for it. The steeper the Price, the more it says about the priorities of those who are willing to pay it. Is extending your own life worth ending another? What about several others? Does it matter which others? Those are interesting questions. Though, there is something to be said for making the trade off tempting for the players to earnestly consider it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, everything has a price if you choose to look at it that way. One way of looking at that whole post of mine is that the Price is there, but it's internal rather than external. The personal horror of becoming a magical monster that I find interesting in Mage.<br /> Tremere, for example, have a rather drastic Price, very external, as well as internal.<br /> <br /> But even just the Steal Lifespan spell has included a violation of hubris, of morality, while, as you mention, being very tempting for the players to make.<br /> <br /> Afterall, it's just a few years, and the target is likely a bad person, surely you're justified in living more than that murderer, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:19:06-07:00","id":954365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954320#post954320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the earlier text suggested Archmasters convert bodily into a soul leading to the assumption that they must stop aging. I don't suppose you are splitting hairs between ageless and immortal, so what happens to Archmages now, if it has been covered? Are they more or less normal except for their magic?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As it clearly says in Imperial Mysteries - they age when they're in the fallen world, same as everyone else. Sitting in their Road stops their clock (they don't have to eat, breathe, or sleep, either), and it restarts as soon as they leave.<br /> <br /> This isn't a change. It's just something people <i>continually</i> get wrong, and one of my flags for &quot;this poster does not know what he is talking about&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:31:52-07:00","id":954400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954338#post954338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even just the Steal Lifespan spell has included a violation of hubris, of morality, while, as you mention, being very tempting for the players to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>A problem to be remembered is that players rarely need to make these sorts of decisions. Player characters are rarely in danger of ageing to death. Life extension in unethical manners is almost always the province of the NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:44:34-07:00","id":954488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954365#post954365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As it clearly says in Imperial Mysteries - they age when they're in the fallen world, same as everyone else. Sitting in their Road stops their clock (they don't have to eat, breathe, or sleep, either), and it restarts as soon as they leave.<br /> <br /> This isn't a change. It's just something people <i>continually</i> get wrong, and one of my flags for &quot;this poster does not know what he is talking about&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the clock restarting bit gets lost for some reason and only the other part is remembered. Obviously, I don't know anything about it hence the question. Thanks for reiterating anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:18:46-07:00","id":954505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954129#post954129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope we can see a future description of how to become a Morphean, and what one looks like in play. Immortality at the cost of becoming little more than a vessel for your Obsessions seeks like the ultimate in-theme endgame for Mage.<br /> <br /> Plus they make for fun baddies, both in Mage and as unexpected surprises in Changeling and Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e Astral Realms book, iirc, had a pretty straightforward description of the Morphean experience, which is that it is absolutely bonkers. Specifically, the most famous kind of Morphean involves flipping the basic relationship of one's soul to the universe inside-out, so that one no longer requires a body or non-Astral existence to maintain the Oneiros. The major second-order effect of this is that one's goetia are completely cut off from the outside world; rather than outside influence providing the material with which your subjective experience is constructed by your unconscious, the unconscious provides motivation and support for your conscious mind without any fuel. The goetia grow bizarre and twisted in isolation, while no experience the Morphean has can change their unconscious drives, because the basic relationship of experience/memory &gt;&gt;&gt; unconscious &gt;&gt;&gt; decisions (which is present in the Mastigos conception of the mind) has had its first two steps inverted: unconscious &gt;&gt;&gt; filters all experience &gt;&gt;&gt; conscious decisions. It's a fascinating concept for a character! Also quite mad, and only more so as time goes by. Morpheans are also noted to steal objects and memories from other people's Astral selves because then they can insert those as experience, learning and changing as people through suturing bit of other souls onto the outside of their hermetically-sealed self.<br /> Morpheans are great, and I would say considerably more inhuman than any other kind of lich I'm aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:48:18-07:00","id":954517,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, Masters of Life and Space can basically transform themselves into 'mini-archmasters'.<br /> Use Space to create your own pocket realm (your miniature golden road), use Life to transform into something biologically immortal like a Lobster (your limited immunity to aging), and use Create Life get bodies that look like your original one that you can posess with Animal Minion so you can interact with the rest of the world without endangering yourself while your Lobster-self stays in the pocket realm(your Ersatz-Ochemata).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:26:43-07:00","id":954580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954517#post954517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, Masters of Life and Space can basically transform themselves into 'mini-archmasters'.<br /> Use Space to create your own pocket realm (your miniature golden road), use Life to transform into something biologically immortal like a Lobster (your limited immunity to aging), and use Create Life get bodies that look like your original one that you can posess with Animal Minion so you can interact with the rest of the world without endangering yourself while your Lobster-self stays in the pocket realm(your Ersatz-Ochemata).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ykWPyaqbebo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ykWPyaqbebo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ykWPyaqbebo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ykWPyaqbebo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Do ever you think this is how chutluian entities get their start? Just some clever get who lost his mind to eternity? This all sound very yithian","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:38:12-07:00","id":954589,"title":"","content":"Seeing as immunity to aging generally useless in the context of Player Characters unless you are playing a millennia hopping crossover campaign with Mummies, the above is the only life extension method I'd seriously consider using precious Spell Control slots on.<br /> Because the idea of living as the infamous Lobster Mage, second degree Master of the Arcana, is hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:55:35-07:00","id":954600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954517#post954517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, Masters of Life and Space can basically transform themselves into 'mini-archmasters'.<br /> Use Space to create your own pocket realm (your miniature golden road), use Life to transform into something biologically immortal like a Lobster (your limited immunity to aging), and use Create Life get bodies that look like your original one that you can posess with Animal Minion so you can interact with the rest of the world without endangering yourself while your Lobster-self stays in the pocket realm(your Ersatz-Ochemata).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so you turn yourself into a lobster, lock yourself into a vault and puppet a conjured meat puppet out into the world where if you want to cast spells you have to cast them sympathetically?<br /> <br /> Okay. If that's what you want to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:40:20-07:00","id":954622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954600#post954600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay so you turn yourself into a lobster, lock yourself into a vault and puppet a conjured meat puppet out into the world where if you want to cast spells you have to cast them sympathetically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a quibble, but it's via Remote Viewing, not sympathetically. One costs an extra Reach, the other costs Mana.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954600#post954600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. If that's what you want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, it makes for a funny NPC.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:13:44-07:00","id":954672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=954517#post954517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and use Create Life get bodies that look like your original one that you can posess with Animal Minion so you can interact with the rest of the world without endangering yourself while your Lobster-self stays in the pocket realm(your Ersatz-Ochemata).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great idea and it reminds me of my own t- <span style=\"font-size:16px\">ASSUMING DIRECT CONTROL</span>.<br /> <br /> It reminds me of my- <span style=\"font-size:16px\">YOU CANNOT STOP US</span>.<br /> <br /> Oh, come on, I- <span style=\"font-size:16px\">THIS FORM IS IRRLEVANT</span>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:51:47-07:00","id":957198,"title":"","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> I actually finally got my account validated. This thread was the main reason I created it, hope I'm not too late.<br /> <br /> So, first, I think mages are actually, amongst the supernatural creatures of the world (except maybe the sin-eaters) the least likely to look for immortality. They just don't need it. Mages know that death is not the end. They do not believe it: they know it. A fifth of them have actually been to the Afterlife (the Moros). A lot of them speak to ghosts and go to the Underworld on a regular basis. They pretty much all know about the existence of the Soul. They ALL have met some kind or another of divine beings when they went to their watchtower. Why would they want immortality?<br /> <br /> Mages are beings who, by their very nature, are looking for the answers of the universe. For them, knowing what they know, why would/should they try to escape death? There are more secrets waiting to be found on the other side of the great veil. They shouldn't welcome it easily but neither should they actively try to escape it forever. Archmages are just on one of the roads to Gnosis (albeit, a very interesting one) but not the only one. Do remember that for mages power is just a side-effect of their true passion: knowledge.<br /> <br /> So that's why, IMHO, most way to become immortal are sins against wisdom: it's because it's basically immature of them. It's like a kid not wanting to graduate from school because he'll lose his friends. There's a wider world waiting for you out there if you are ready for it. It's not to say that all kids should graduate (some should be allowed to if it's better for their development in the long term) but there are good reasons and ways to repeat a year and then there are the bad ones. And most of them are bad. And whatever happens it's not something that should be left to the kid. In much the same way, if some ways to become immortal can be acceptable for mages, most of them aren't, most of the reasons to look for them go against Wisdom and anyway it's not up to the mage but to the Gods/Universe/Magic/whatever to decide for them.<br /> <br /> So that's my first point and I think it's pretty much canon, or at the very least it fits in the canon. My second point is rather dubious, it's more about how I play the question myself.<br /> <br /> From my point of view, Mage is fondamentally a game about personnal development and restraint of power. Mages are arguably amongst the most powerful supernatural creatures there is in the Darkness. They have reality defining powers. So I think that Mage isn't a game about what the players can do but about what they should do. The way i understand Mage it's a game about beings with incredible powers on a path to understand themselves, the world and the relationship between the two. I understand the canon as supporting that: there is a purpose to the world, an intended direction for fate. Mages were supposed to be teachers and protectors for humanity until, as a race, they became ready to Ascend (even though some could ascend first). But the Exarch cheated their way in the Supernal, overthrew the Gods and slammed the doors shut behind them. That is to say that it's not that mages shouldn't become immortals. They shouldn't YET. They aren't ready. Death is a part of the human experience, it's a part of the Gods'intended structure for the Universe and the Enlightenment of Humanity. One day, they'll be free from it as they will be free from Fate or Time. But they aren't there yet. And that ties to the notion of Hubris: hubris is basically overconfidence which leads to defy the laws of the gods. Wisdom is all about &quot;a mage can do that. Should he?&quot;. So, by its very definition, &quot;skipping&quot; on Death if you are not yet ready is hubristic. And that ties me pretty neatly, I think, with my first point.<br /> <br /> There. Sorry for my English, I'm French, so if I'm not clear or I made some horrible grammar mistake, feel free to point it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12295,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","user":"Lokiel","date":". 08-24-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:02:39-07:00","id":957211,"title":"","content":"Yes, Moros have been to an afterlife. An incredibly shitty one. Not wanting to go the Underworld isn't immature, it's logical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:13:17-07:00","id":957218,"title":"","content":"Well, no. The Soul disappears when someone dies. Nobody knows where, if anywhere, it goes. Ghosts are heavily implied if not outright stated (and I'm pretty sure outright stated in several places) to be just echoes left behind upon death. They aren't the soul of a person. Even a Master of Death doesn't know if an afterlife actually exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:18:27-07:00","id":957222,"title":"","content":"Actually, no. There are no real description of Stygia in the 2nd ed but according to the first edition, Stygia is a midway point of sort. Souls wait there for whatever happens after that. But there IS an after, of that Moros are pretty much sure (with the caveat that they're not sure if it still works properly after the Fall).I quote the corebook in second edition, in the section under &quot;the Underworld&quot;, p246, which is the closest source we have on the matter: &quot;as for the soul itself, Moros say that all souls once went to Stygia to be purified and reborn, but nobody knows if this still happens or even if it was ever true.&quot; A belief about reincarnation is also heavily implied by the section about &quot;symbols and myths&quot; on page 28 in the description of the Moros. I don't have the first ed (it was lent to me when I considered chronicling) but I'm pretty sure it described Stygia as a place where souls wait for the afterlife, whatever it is.<br /> <br /> And I stand by my point: mages know of the afterlife, they know of fate, they know of the true gods of creation. They know there's a path to enlightenment and that death may be a part of it for them or that at the very least looking for it could impede their progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12295,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","user":"Lokiel","date":".  Added the quote from the corebook and some stuff 08-24-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:04:45-07:00","id":957251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The origin and destination of souls remains a Mystery even<br /> to the Awakened \u2014 they appear at birth and vanish completely<br /> at the moment of death. </div> </div> </div>pg 98.<br /> <br /> Along with the fact that they're interchangeable (that is, putting someone else's soul into a soulless person doesn't cause any problems) kind of indicates that the nature of souls changed between 1e and 2e. Even in 1e, they were pretty interchangeable to my memory, but there was a difference between Sleeper souls and Awakened ones.<br /> <br /> Even your quote just says &quot;they believe this used to be true, but we don't know if it still is or if it ever was to begin with.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's just a matter of personal belief, just like any Sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:19:46-07:00","id":957253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957251#post957251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> pg 98.<br /> <br /> Along with the fact that they're interchangeable (that is, putting someone else's soul into a soulless person doesn't cause any problems) kind of indicates that the nature of souls changed between 1e and 2e. Even in 1e, they were pretty interchangeable to my memory, but there was a difference between Sleeper souls and Awakened ones.<br /> <br /> Even your quote just says &quot;they believe this used to be true, but we don't know if it still is or if it ever was to begin with.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's just a matter of personal belief, just like any Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understand those conflicting passages, they know there is something after death, they just don't know exactly what. They have some clues (Stygia, for instance) but not much more. A lot like they see the train tracks, they can pretty much see in what direction it goes but they don't know for how long, if it takes turns and where are the stations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:33:23-07:00","id":957259,"title":"","content":"@Lokiel: You seem to be making <b>a lot</b> of conjectures: (<i>italics</i> mine)<br /> <br /> - mages are actually, amongst the supernatural creatures of the world (except maybe the sin-eaters) the least likely to look for immortality <i>(why?)</i><br /> - they just don't need it (<i>decides who?</i>)<br /> - Mages know that death is not the end They do not believe it: they know it <i>(how?)</i><br /> - A fifth of them have actually been to the Afterlife (the Moros). <i>(were they?)</i><br /> - There are more secrets waiting to be found on the other side of the great veil <i>(what &quot;Veil&quot;?)</i><br /> - that's why, IMHO, most way to become immortal are sins against wisdom<i> (we don't know all ways =&gt;irrelevant statement)</i><br /> - There's a wider world waiting for you out there if you are ready for it <i>(is there?)</i><br /> - there are good reasons and ways to repeat a year and then there are the bad ones <i>(&quot;repeat a year&quot;, you mean live longer? How do you define &quot;bad&quot; and &quot;good&quot;)</i><br /> - most of them are bad <i>(we can't know all the reasons)</i><br /> - I think it's pretty much canon, or at the very least it fits in the canon <i>(it doesn't, too many conjectures, see above)</i><br /> - there is a purpose to the world, an intended direction for fate <i>(is there?)</i><br /> - They shouldn't YET <i>(why?)</i><br /> - They aren't ready <i>(why?, says who?)</i><br /> - Death is a part of the human experience <i>(It isn't. You are *dead*. You don't experience anything. That's the point.)</i><br /> - One day, they'll be free from it as they will be free from Fate or Time (<i>Why? How? Why &quot;then&quot; and not &quot;now&quot;?)</i><br /> - So, by its very definition, &quot;skipping&quot; on Death if you are not yet ready is hubristic <i>(define &quot;ready&quot;)</i><br /> - But there IS an after, of that Moros are pretty much sure (<i>they *say* that</i>)<br /> - mages know of the afterlife, they know of fate, they know of the true gods of creation. They know there's a path to enlightenment and that death may be a part of it for them or that at the very least looking for it could impede their progress <i>(they <b>don't</b>)<br /> - </i>they know there is something after death <i>(they don't)</i><br /> <br /> - Why would they <i>(even)</i> want immortality? <i>(Why *not*? They have their reasons.)</i><br /> - why would/should they try to escape death? <i>(Why *not*? They have their reasons.)</i><br /> - neither should they actively try to escape it forever <i>(Why *not*? They have their reasons.)</i><br /> - for mages power is just a side-effect of their true passion: knowledge <i>(Not necessarily. Often the other way around.)</i><br /> - it's because it's basically immature of them (<i>define &quot;immature&quot;</i>)<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> - it's not up to the mage but to the <i>Gods/Universe/Magic</i>/whatever to <i>decide for them</i><br /> - it's a part of the <i>Gods' intended structure for the Universe</i> and the Enlightenment of Humanity<br /> - <i>hubris</i> is basically overconfidence which <i>leads to defy the laws of the gods</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.reactiongifs.us/wp-content/uploads/2013/03/nevermind_nathan_fillion.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> [/angry thearch]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:09:18-07:00","id":957274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957259#post957259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Lokiel: You seem to be making <b>a lot</b> of conjectures: (<i>italics</i> mine)<br /> <br /> - mages are actually, amongst the supernatural creatures of the world (except maybe the sin-eaters) the least likely to look for immortality <i>(why?)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>For the reasons stated after?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - they just don't need it (<i>decides who?</i>) </div> </div> </div>See above, I explained why after that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mages know that death is not the end They do not believe it: they know it <i>(how?)</i> </div> </div> </div>Well, they know of at least two afterlives, they've met god-like beings, ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - A fifth of them have actually been to the Afterlife (the Moros). <i>(were they?)</i> </div> </div> </div>Well, I could have phrased it more clearly. What I meant is: they've been to one of them, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - There are more secrets waiting to be found on the other side of the great veil <i>(what &quot;Veil&quot;?)</i> </div> </div> </div>I just didn't know how to phrase it without repeating Death. What I meant is: they know that after death, some form of you survive and even evolve. Stygia is stated as a waiting room where you let go of your passions, a purgatory of sorts. Even the Underworld has some sort of built-in purification system. That heavily implies some sort of progression of the soul and new mysteries to discover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - There's a wider world waiting for you out there if you are ready for it <i>(is there?)</i> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, according to the description of Stygia in first ed and the Moros description in second ed, as stated. Death isn't the destruction of the being in the CoD, or at least not in its first &quot;stages&quot;. So I feel like trying to escape one of the biggest mystery of them all would be strange for a mage, especially if they know there are things out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - there are good reasons and ways to repeat a year and then there are the bad ones <i>(&quot;repeat a year&quot;, you mean live longer? How do you define &quot;bad&quot; and &quot;good&quot;)</i> </div> </div> </div>In this case, according to the intendend &quot;drive&quot; for a mage: learning and self improvement. It seems to me that page 11 of the corebook clearly says that curiosity and wisdom are amongst the major themes of Mages (with power).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - most of them are bad <i>(we can't know all the reasons)</i> </div> </div> </div>No, we can't. But that would be relevant if I sayed they were all bad reasons. But I said that, from my understanding of the game, it runs so contradictory to what it means to be a mage that there can only be few who would be in accordance with the universe they're living in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - I think it's pretty much canon, or at the very least it fits in the canon <i>(it doesn't, too many conjectures, see above)</i> </div> </div> </div>It seems we disagree on that.<br /> <br /> The rest seems a bit like nitpicking, especially since I said it was more of the way I played it, so I won't respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12295,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","user":"Lokiel","date":". 08-24-2016, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T18:58:42-07:00","id":957326,"title":"","content":"I like your take, but I have a nitpick. Souls that leave when you die are not likely to be carrying any kind of relevant continuity of self along with them since they seem to be identical to the ones that can be swapped around like batteries. This would seem to poke a hole in the theory that Stygia is a place where self continuous people are refined before moving on to whatever is after Stygia. If that's correct and it's not a continuous self kind of soul/journey then Mages still have reasonable room for doubt or fear of death. Granted, this is a grey area in the game specifically because it could be a great place to hang a Mystery so it could go either way an actual refinement of soul/self as a step on the journey of existence, or annihilation of self as the soul stuff gets purified before being re-purposed. Because of this lack of certainty though, yeah, even Moros have a reason to fall for the immortality trap. My general opinion is that when you think you're about to run up against the hard facts about the cosmology of the setting you'll suddenly find yourself on not so solid ground after all.<br /> <br /> Reality is a debate between the gods, Mages are the arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T19:54:19-07:00","id":957347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957326#post957326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souls that leave when you die are not likely to be carrying any kind of relevant continuity of self along with them since they seem to be identical to the ones that can be swapped around like batteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless souls work like escape pods/life boats; they don't contain the self until the main vessel dies and the self needs to escape, then the self climbs aboard the soul and escapes the fallen world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:09:56-07:00","id":957360,"title":"","content":"Immortality is such a great motivation for characters to seek out and make sacrifices for. It's the once universal human experience that is both certain and sucks ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T00:03:21-07:00","id":957443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957274#post957274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest seems a bit like nitpicking, especially since I said it was more of the way I played it,</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Sorry, it seems I've missed that. Blame the 2AM when I've written that post. And the end was supposed to be a joke, it's exactly how a thearch would react to the last few statements.<br /> <br /> But, in a nutshell, my problem with all those statements in the 'canon' part of your post was that they <i>aren't</i> canon. They simply aren't supported anywhere in the official mage cosmology and seem more like homebrewed parts of a setting, or in some cases maybe personal opinions of a few mages, than facts they were made to appear to be. My remarks were supposed to highlight that. Apologies if it came out wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:25:12-07:00","id":957509,"title":"","content":"It's implied in the myths sidebar of Imperial Mysteries that even the exarchs experience a form of mortality and groom ministers to replace them (Replace them entirely or feed them? Tremere Exarchs. Even less fun then regular exarchs). <br /> <br /> I'm fairly certain that one of the impacts of the Corpus Author's ascension was that her belief that &quot;Magic is alive&quot; became a Truth of the world. What the full implications of being alive means for truth symbols is unknown.<br /> <br /> Merlin still seems to have survived the removal of Arthur's kingdom from the timeline but the legend has been romanticised and changed a lot. Perhaps that's what death is to truth symbols now. <br /> <br /> My point is that if even truth symbols experience a recurrent transformation resembling the tarot description of death (change and subsequent renewal) it could provide a compelling explanation for why dying is a supernal truth, and why deviating from that necessarily risks wisdom, although your mileage may vary. You have to accept that magic is alive, that the corpus author created this truth through imperium, that it applies to all truth symbols, that that fact also translates to the Fallen phenomena of mortal lifespans and that undermining that Truth necessarily drags you from the supernal.<br /> <br /> It certainly makes the Mysterium assertion that &quot;Magic is alive, and therefore, magic can die&quot; much more anxiety inducing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12329-gravity-srainbro","name":"Gravity'sRainbro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:11:25-07:00","id":957797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957326#post957326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your take, but I have a nitpick. Souls that leave when you die are not likely to be carrying any kind of relevant continuity of self along with them since they seem to be identical to the ones that can be swapped around like batteries. This would seem to poke a hole in the theory that Stygia is a place where self continuous people are refined before moving on to whatever is after Stygia. If that's correct and it's not a continuous self kind of soul/journey then Mages still have reasonable room for doubt or fear of death. Granted, this is a grey area in the game specifically because it could be a great place to hang a Mystery so it could go either way an actual refinement of soul/self as a step on the journey of existence, or annihilation of self as the soul stuff gets purified before being re-purposed. Because of this lack of certainty though, yeah, even Moros have a reason to fall for the immortality trap. My general opinion is that when you think you're about to run up against the hard facts about the cosmology of the setting you'll suddenly find yourself on not so solid ground after all.<br /> <br /> Reality is a debate between the gods, Mages are the arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that &quot;souls-that-can-be-swapped&quot; (let's call it stcbs from now) aren't the totality of the soul. For instance, the way mages interact with the soul doesn't seem that coherent with how other beings do (such as Demons, for instance). And I think earlier in this thread it was pointed out that the Anima Mundi as the &quot;soul of the world&quot; doesn't mean that it's a soul in the Death and Life arcana sense. There is something strange, also, with how some beings are &quot;soulless&quot; but seems functionnally not that different from humans (spirits, and I believe promethean also? And what about demons? And Beasts?). I think mummies also recognize several &quot;components&quot; of the soul.<br /> <br /> So the way I understood it is that the STCBS (or arcana souls, whatever) are a part of what we tend to call souls in the common sense of the term but not the totality. They're like an important part of the soul, true, but not all. Much like how you can swap hearth but still have the same &quot;body&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is, there seem to be some incongruity between game lines about what the soul is so I think that the stuff mages can manipulate is only the tip of the iceberg there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957443#post957443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Sorry, it seems I've missed that. Blame the 2AM when I've written that post. And the end was supposed to be a joke, it's exactly how a thearch would react to the last few statements.<br /> <br /> But, in a nutshell, my problem with all those statements in the 'canon' part of your post was that they <i>aren't</i> canon. They simply aren't supported anywhere in the official mage cosmology and seem more like homebrewed parts of a setting, or in some cases maybe personal opinions of a few mages, than facts they were made to appear to be. My remarks were supposed to highlight that. Apologies if it came out wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>No trouble at all. Since English isn't my main language, I was wondering if I wasn't misreading it anyway.<br /> <br /> Well, I think I listed my references on that matter, so saying that they aren't supported anywhere in the official mage cosmology seems a bit harsh. Maybe I misunderstood the true meaning the author wanted to give it but that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12295,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","user":"Lokiel","date":". 08-25-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:34:20-07:00","id":957815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957797#post957797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was under the impression that &quot;souls-that-can-be-swapped&quot; (let's call it stcbs from now) aren't the totality of the soul. For instance, the way mages interact with the soul doesn't seem that coherent with how other beings do (such as Demons, for instance). And I think earlier in this thread it was pointed out that the Anima Mundi as the &quot;soul of the world&quot; doesn't mean that it's a soul in the Death and Life arcana sense. There is something strange, also, with how some beings are &quot;soulless&quot; but seems functionnally not that different from humans (spirits, and I believe promethean also? And what about demons? ).<br /> <br /> So the way I understood it is that the STCBS (or arcana souls, whatever) are a part of what we tend to call souls in the common sense of the term but not the totality. They're like an important part of the soul, true, but not all. Much like how you can swap hearth but still have the same &quot;body&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is, there seem to be some incongruity between game lines about what the soul is so I think that the stuff mages can manipulate is only the tip of the iceberg there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And that's the point, its clear that the Soul that mages can interact with is not the real full soul of a person (if there even is such a thing). All of the evidence you pointed to was based on that Soul (or STCBs). So Mages still have uncertainty about what happens when you die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:45:19-07:00","id":957825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957815#post957815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's the point, its clear that the Soul that mages can interact with is not the real full soul of a person (if there even is such a thing). All of the evidence you pointed to was based on that Soul (or STCBs). So Mages still have uncertainty about what happens when you die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Personal opinion here: seems a lot of energy wasted with the souls for destroying them in the end. But I do admit that it could be something else: for instance, maybe Stygia is just a processing line for recycling STCBS into something else (food?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:00:56-07:00","id":957833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957825#post957825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. Personal opinion here: seems a lot of energy wasted with the souls for destroying them in the end. But I do admit that it could be something else: for instance, maybe Stygia is just a processing line for recycling STCBS into something else (food?).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a Mystery to me. Good Chronicle fodder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:12:34-07:00","id":957836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957833#post957833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds like a Mystery to me. Good Chronicle fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but it got me thinking: do mages know that what they manipulate aren't really souls in their totality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:21:31-07:00","id":957840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957836#post957836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but it got me thinking: do mages know that what they manipulate aren't really souls in their totality?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have to since they're aware of the fact that legacies are a form of soul shaping that's non-transferable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:10:08-07:00","id":966551,"title":"","content":"Been thinking about this, and it's really a shame the road the game went down RE mortality. The &quot;immortality and transhumanism are eeeeeeeeevil and unnatural&quot; part is ultimately the reason I can't even get into Awakening as the occult superhero game it works best as, because the whole idea of &quot;fight oppressive false reality&quot; has no resonance to me if you can't actually change the things I would actually try to change if I were a gnostic superhero.<br /> <br /> And having &quot;this is right and natural and this is bad and unnatural&quot; spelled out so clearly is really a waste, because there's not really any fun in playing out a &quot;war for reality itself&quot; scenario when the developers make it clear that there is One True And Good Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:19:25-07:00","id":966556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966551#post966551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking about this, and it's really a shame the road the game went down RE mortality. The &amp;quot;immortality and transhumanism are eeeeeeeeevil and unnatural&amp;quot; part is ultimately the reason I can't even get into Awakening as the occult superhero game it works best as, because the whole idea of &amp;quot;fight oppressive false reality&amp;quot; has no resonance to me if you can't actually change the things I would actually try to change if I were a gnostic superhero.<br /> <br /> And having &amp;quot;this is right and natural and this is bad and unnatural&amp;quot; spelled out so clearly is really a waste, because there's not really any fun in playing out a &amp;quot;war for reality itself&amp;quot; scenario when the developers make it clear that there is One True And Good Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says you....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:29:11-07:00","id":966559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966551#post966551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking about this, and it's really a shame the road the game went down RE mortality. The &quot;immortality and transhumanism are eeeeeeeeevil and unnatural&quot; part is ultimately the reason I can't even get into Awakening as the occult superhero game it works best as, because the whole idea of &quot;fight oppressive false reality&quot; has no resonance to me if you can't actually change the things I would actually try to change if I were a gnostic superhero.<br /> <br /> And having &quot;this is right and natural and this is bad and unnatural&quot; spelled out so clearly is really a waste, because there's not really any fun in playing out a &quot;war for reality itself&quot; scenario when the developers make it clear that there is One True And Good Path.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Especially since human society has been struggling to achieve immortality since we crawled out of whatever primordial ooze spawned us. Over the course of human history, we've managed to expand our lives many times beyond what they would have been originally.<br /> <br /> But giving us an indefinite life span? Nope, suddenly that crosses a line!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:50:02-07:00","id":966567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966559#post966559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But giving us an indefinite life span?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can be done at Time 2. Prime 2 and the right Sanctum configuration can make it especially secure. If you just want to live forever you have a significant array of tools at your disposal.<br /> <br /> The heinous shit that trucks with substitution pacts and alien powers beyond mortal ken tends to be easier and longer-lasting because it is part of the nature of the Fallen World to bring those aspects of the occult into prominence as both warning and temptation. Playing the game of immortals means dealing with the fact that most of your contemporaries by volume are hungry aliens who don't like competition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:07:53-07:00","id":966580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966551#post966551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking about this, and it's really a shame the road the game went down RE mortality. The &quot;immortality and transhumanism are eeeeeeeeevil and unnatural&quot; part is ultimately the reason I can't even get into Awakening as the occult superhero game it works best as, because the whole idea of &quot;fight oppressive false reality&quot; has no resonance to me if you can't actually change the things I would actually try to change if I were a gnostic superhero.<br /> <br /> And having &quot;this is right and natural and this is bad and unnatural&quot; spelled out so clearly is really a waste, because there's not really any fun in playing out a &quot;war for reality itself&quot; scenario when the developers make it clear that there is One True And Good Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;fight oppressive false reality?&quot; O_o That's not the theme of Awakening. Addicted to mysteries is the theme of Awakening. This whole thing about immortality is a sidebar of a side issue to Awakening's theme.<br /> <br /> Like someone else has said in this thread, unless you play a game where you have someone old (or at least old enough to begin experiencing aging after being in their prime), this isn't as much of an issue to game play as it is a possible side issue to background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:24:33-07:00","id":966626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966551#post966551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking about this, and it's really a shame the road the game went down RE mortality. The &quot;immortality and transhumanism are eeeeeeeeevil and unnatural&quot; part is ultimately the reason I can't even get into Awakening as the occult superhero game it works best as, because the whole idea of &quot;fight oppressive false reality&quot; has no resonance to me if you can't actually change the things I would actually try to change if I were a gnostic superhero.<br /> <br /> And having &quot;this is right and natural and this is bad and unnatural&quot; spelled out so clearly is really a waste, because there's not really any fun in playing out a &quot;war for reality itself&quot; scenario when the developers make it clear that there is One True And Good Path.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No one cares. It would be nice to be done with this conversation. The game has humanist interests in mind. Fine. You know what you do? You question the majority in the game instead of insisting it be addressed by the developers. You're not going to change their mind and your whinging isn't doing anything but annoying everyone else who hasn't got a problem with it.<br /> <br /> I think you could probably make the case that the game itself delivers little judgement on how bad immortality is or isn't. The majority of Mage society doesn't trust immortals? The majority of Mages are dumbasses full of their own trite philosophies about how to make the universe tick properly! Fuck 'em. Immortality isn't easy to accomplish? Nothing worthwhile is! Get over it, play a Mage who is dead set against buying into the stupid morality of death that the majority of Mages accept and who will prove them wrong, prove them all wrong! Who knows, if you keep at it long enough you might Ascend and make immortality an intrinsic positive value in the universe.<br /> <br /> You don't like the thing. Fine. Good job. Here's your card. Do something productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:47:16-07:00","id":966640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966551#post966551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking about this, and it's really a shame the road the game went down RE mortality. The &amp;quot;immortality and transhumanism are eeeeeeeeevil and unnatural&amp;quot; part is ultimately the reason I can't even get into Awakening as the occult superhero game it works best as, because the whole idea of &amp;quot;fight oppressive false reality&amp;quot; has no resonance to me if you can't actually change the things I would actually try to change if I were a gnostic superhero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, where do I even begin with this paragraph? Mage doesn't say transhumanism is evil, it doesn't work best as an occult superhero game, and fighting an oppressive false reality is not a focus in your typical Mage game.<br /> <br /> Hear me out here. Is it at all possible that the reason Mage doesn't resonate with you that you're looking at it from the wrong angle? It seems like trying to make it a &quot;gnostic superhero&quot; game is causing you more problems than it's solving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966551#post966551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And having &amp;quot;this is right and natural and this is bad and unnatural&amp;quot; spelled out so clearly is really a waste, because there's not really any fun in playing out a &amp;quot;war for reality itself&amp;quot; scenario when the developers make it clear that there is One True And Good Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage doesn't really feature a war for reality, and it's generally pretty amoral. Like, the only thing Mage really comes out and says &quot;this is bad!&quot; about is Hubris. Immortality is entirely possible for mages through safe, responsivle means. It's just that it's much easier to do it through dubious, harmful means. And that's to emphasize the theme of Hubris. Do you live with the limitations of doing it the safe way, or do you throw caution to the winds and pursue your goals at any cost? Do you take the quick and easy path, or do you take the time to do it right and proper? That's the point, not a condemnation against transhumanism or whatever your bugbear is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:01:14-07:00","id":966645,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> In Gecko's defense, the book explicitly says that immortality is &quot;a sign that the mage has deeper-rooted issues than the fear of death that comes complete with being a functional human being,&quot; which seems like an odd stance to take beyond personal opinion; one could certainly take the in-character stance that mortality is just as much a part of the Lie as anything else, and you see this idea in a lot of occult writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:38:19-07:00","id":966653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966645#post966645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> In Gecko's defense, the book explicitly says that immortality is &quot;a sign that the mage has deeper-rooted issues than the fear of death that comes complete with being a functional human being,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Immortality&quot; is not the entirety of the paragraph preceding that quote.<br /> <br /> The context in which mages exist makes goal-oriented reaper-delays in the pursuit of transcendence a more attractive option than shackling your magical development to the notion of being Preston The Changeless for all eternity. A character's magic says things about them; using it to ensure that you're around forever tends to extrapolate outward from the symbolic ramifications of why you did that, and a lot of the usual reasons have neighbors with some pretty nasty edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:42:17-07:00","id":966654,"title":"","content":"Remember, as a mage, that your smallest intentions drag knives over the face of reality and leave bloody wounds and ugly scars all over the place unless you are firmly the master of yourself, and that involves accepting things you'd really rather not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:44:53-07:00","id":966655,"title":"","content":"Mortality being part of the Lie and immortality being morally corrosive are not actually mutually exclusive. It wouldn't be possible to achieve immortality any of the ways presented if one weren't Awakened and capable of seeing that mortality is not necessary. There's a difference between knowing you 'can' do something and knowing whether you 'should' do something. Mortality is definitely part of the Lie, but at what cost come conquering it? For as many references as exist to achieving immortality through enlightenment there are as many cautionary tales. The quest for immortality in history and fiction is possibly one of the most prominent examples of hubris we have as a species, and hubris is one of Mage's core themes. <br /> Mage is about having incredible power with a big fat asterisk on the end, a &quot;but...&quot; If you remove that qualifier then what is the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:52:51-07:00","id":966679,"title":"","content":"Mortality is not part of the Lie: it's an Arcanum, even if there were no Abyss things would end.<br /> <br /> Fear of Death is an Exarch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T05:28:31-07:00","id":966720,"title":"","content":"Even completely appart from Mage as a game: from an ethical standpoint I would generally argue that everybody, who fanatically chases to prolong his lifetime instead of using the time he has to achieve something has issues.<br /> And additionally from a scientific stand point: humanity is not and never was able to prolongue human live above a &quot;natural lifespan&quot;, medicine has become really good at eradicating stuff that cuts this lifetime short, but up to today there is nothing that can actually prevent the decay of a human body over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T06:23:38-07:00","id":966726,"title":"","content":"The focus of mage is on the dangers of hubris. Yeah, you wield godly powers that most humans can't even conceive of, but don't let it go to your head.<br /> <br /> Kind of like the Tevinter Imperium, they thought themselves equal to the Gods they served, and when they fell, they hit the ground like an extinction level meteor.<br /> <br /> As for mortality being part of the lie, I can understand that point. I mean you have an entire watchtower dedicated to manipulating death itself. Even if the Necromancers do accept death as a part of life, they're still reanimating corpses and consorting with ghosts who shouldn't be up and walking around anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966720#post966720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even completely appart from Mage as a game: from an ethical standpoint I would generally argue that everybody, who fanatically chases to prolong his lifetime instead of using the time he has to achieve something has issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing you achieve in life matters in the long run. Any contributions you bring to society will become obsolete in a few decades. And just when you've reached your prime, your body starts to degrade and your accomplishments along with it. You'll die, you'll be forgotten, and the world will move on without you. Life is ultimately pointless for a mortal being.<br /> <br /> But if you're immortal...? You don't have to become obsolete, you don't have to become forgotten, and you can remain in your prime until you run out of ideas, rather than becoming too degraded to continue working.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-10-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T06:49:47-07:00","id":966733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966580#post966580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;fight oppressive false reality?&quot; O_o That's not the theme of Awakening. Addicted to mysteries is the theme of Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966640#post966640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> fighting an oppressive false reality is not a focus in your typical Mage game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are three themes to Awakening, conviently listed under the Themes section in the core book for purusal. Addicted to Mysteries is one. &quot;Hubris and Power&quot; is a second, though it doesn't get an official subtitle in the book. The third theme is &quot;The World is a Lie.&quot; And, if you read the paragraphs under that heading, yes, it does specifically say that fighting against the Lie imposed by the Exarchs on reality is a major part of the game. One third of the game is devoted to fighting tyrannical forces.<br /> <br /> The immortality thing is part of the hubris/power bits. So, yes, it is very much part of the game's themes.<br /> <br /> EDIT - Immortality a different part from The World is a Lie theme, though. You can't reduce Mage to just any one of the three themes, you have to keep all three in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-10-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:56:47-07:00","id":966753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966733#post966733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are three themes to Awakening, conviently listed under the Themes section in the core book for purusal. Addicted to Mysteries is one. &amp;quot;Hubris and Power&amp;quot; is a second, though it doesn't get an official subtitle in the book. The third theme is &amp;quot;The World is a Lie.&amp;quot; And, if you read the paragraphs under that heading, yes, it does specifically say that fighting against the Lie imposed by the Exarchs on reality is a major part of the game. One third of the game is devoted to fighting tyrannical forces.<br /> <br /> The immortality thing is part of the hubris/power bits. So, yes, it is very much part of the game's themes.<br /> <br /> EDIT - Immortality a different part from The World is a Lie theme, though. You can't reduce Mage to just any one of the three themes, you have to keep all three in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll notice I didn't say &quot;reality is false&quot; isn't a theme of Mage. I said &quot;fighting an oppressive false reality&quot; isn't a major part of your typical Mage game. Yes, the reality we know is a Lie imposed by Tyrants, and yes, the pentacle aims to fight that Lie. But the fight isn't a huge part of your typical Mage's day to day life. It isn't a hot war where you're going around killing Seers and blowing up their headquarters and stuff. The thing about a &quot;war against reality&quot; is that it can't really resemble war in any meaningful sense of the word, because reality isn't a thing you can commit violence against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:07:11-07:00","id":966758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966753#post966753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll notice I didn't say &quot;reality is false&quot; isn't a theme of Mage. I said &quot;fighting an oppressive false reality&quot; isn't a major part of your typical Mage game. Yes, the reality we know is a Lie imposed by Tyrants, and yes, the pentacle aims to fight that Lie. But the fight isn't a huge part of your typical Mage's day to day life. It isn't a hot war where you're going around killing Seers and blowing up their headquarters and stuff. The thing about a &quot;war against reality&quot; is that it can't really resemble war in any meaningful sense of the word, because reality isn't a thing you can commit violence against.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're taking the word &quot;reality&quot; too literal. &quot;Reality&quot; in this case is refering to the Lie, and that's actually what mages fight against. It all comes down to fighting for humanity and against systems of oppression. And, yes, it is part of many mages' day-to-day lives. Do they maintain a mystery cult? That's fighting against the Lie by encouraging Truth and Awakening. How about a job that undermines the blind faith that the Paternoster fosters? Fight the Lie. <br /> <br /> Not every day has to be a mage battle against the Seers to fight the Lie with spells flying everywhere. But there's lots of ways to support the war effort and push for enlightenment on a day-to-day basis. And I will argue that it is part of most mages' lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:16:44-07:00","id":966762,"title":"","content":"I would just add that I agree that fear of death is bad, simply because it will cripple you and prevent you from actually living your life. Fearing death and not wanting to die are two separate things, though. However, Death arcanum is about <i>change in general</i> being a necessary part of existence, which doesn't really mean anything in itself.<br /> <br /> The key thing here is to understand, that you can and <i>have to</i> choose which change is good and which is bad with every choice you make in your life, all the while recognizing what choices are even allowed to be made by the rules the universe is build upon, and occasionally you may even have the ability to change the rules, if you possess the knowledge of how to.<br /> <br /> Why am I saying this? Because cessation of continuation of a specific sequence of perceptions that define a single human mind, happening by the virtue of degradation of brain cells and organism as a whole, with similar processes not even happening in some existing animals, is a <i>very</i> specific kind of change. One of many changes happening in the world. Just like some things simply *don't* happen, like heat suddenly changing into a tree. And with aging, like with everything you can or could affect, you and only you can decide, if that change is &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; for you, and if it's bad, than you can attempt to 'change the rules' for it to <b>not happen</b>. There is nothing that makes human death as a condition inherently a taboo to change (notice the irony here, even certain aspects of death can die), in comparison to all the other possible changes, that you could make in the world.<br /> <br /> True immortality is most likely achievable through Ascension, after all, anything immortal basically is a concept around which the universe is built anyway, might as well be Supernal. In comparison, defeating human aging is perfectly concievable without Ascension, if done properly even without breaking any metaphysical barrier. The death of you has no more or less symbolic significance in the Death arcanum than a death of a tortoise. And a tortois can live for a very long time. A mayfly for a short while. The difference between either of them and a human in lifespan is biological. You change your biology, possibly with a little help from Life magic, you prolong your life, and metaphysics won't be able to hate you for that, like it can't hate you for any other non-soul mauling change you've caused by your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:18:20-07:00","id":966763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966758#post966758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're taking the word &amp;quot;reality&amp;quot; too literal. &amp;quot;Reality&amp;quot; in this case is refering to the Lie, and that's actually what mages fight against. It all comes down to fighting for humanity and against systems of oppression. And, yes, it is part of many mages' day-to-day lives. Do they maintain a mystery cult? That's fighting against the Lie by encouraging Truth and Awakening. How about a job that undermines the blind faith that the Paternoster fosters? Fight the Lie. <br /> <br /> Not every day has to be a mage battle against the Seers to fight the Lie with spells flying everywhere. But there's lots of ways to support the war effort and push for enlightenment on a day-to-day basis. And I will argue that it is part of most mages' lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we're saying the same thing here. You don't fight systems of oppression with soldiers and weapons. Mages don't fight the Lie by casting direct damage spells at it. If there's a word I'm taking too literally it's not reality, it's war. And I think it's appropriate to do so in this case because the word carries a lot of baggage and that baggage is in many ways the opposite of what &quot;fighting&quot; the lie actually looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:12:50-07:00","id":966782,"title":"","content":"I kinda liked the graduation metaphor Lariel used.<br /> <br /> As many have the setting has &quot;things end&quot; as one of the major metaphysical truths of the verse. It simply is that way, you shouldn't use your real world biases as arguments for why the game is &quot;wrong&quot; cause in the end it's a fictional verse with magic and a lot of other thing. I don't think of death as something &quot;profound&quot; but it is so in game as that's it. You may not like at, and thats ok but it's not &quot;bad&quot; because of that<br /> <br /> Also I don't think Mages as something of a big deal. Sure your existence changes into something different (changes cause as any Moros would assure you nothing ever vanishes from the world) but it's not like your existence but even when you die the choices you made still shape the world, the changes you made cause other changes, your life sustains new life, your ideas can possibly be in the Astral forever and the order won't collapse because of your death. Upsetting the laws of the universe for something petty is quite hubristic if you ask me. Besides there's a big mystery beyond that gate and you'll never know what lies there untill you pass through. And you're a failure of a Mage if you don't want to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:14:17-07:00","id":966783,"title":"","content":"Umm.... *scratches head* First, I've been using &quot;fight,&quot; not &quot;war&quot; for this conversation. And fight can imply non-violent, non-physical struggles as well as military-style fights.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I feel compelled to point out that one of the basic underlying principles in Mage is that the Pentacle and Seers are engaged in a <i>cold</i> <i>war</i>. Cold wars come with implications of espionage and propaganda instead of bloody battles, and that comes with different connotations. This is Mage, a game of mental challenges, not Werewolf, the game of hunting prey.<br /> <br /> Third? I think that you can't assume that war is carrying the same baggage for everyone, nor critize someone for using the term correctly - even Marriam-Webster says that &quot;war&quot; can mean &quot;a situation in which people or groups compete or fight against each other.&quot; Even the most literal interpretation of the use of war here is correct. And we don't live in a literal world - we live in one with figurative meanings and different perspectives.<br /> <br /> So, when you say that <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;fighting an oppressive false reality is not a focus in your typical Mage game,&quot; </span></span></i></span>I have to disagree. There are fights of all sorts, and there is a focus on opposing the Exarchs and Seers, as those are the major antagonists of the whole game. I think its rather typical in most Mage games to have fights against the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-10-2016, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:42:14-07:00","id":966901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966679#post966679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortality is not part of the Lie: it's an Arcanum, even if there were no Abyss things would end.<br /> <br /> Fear of Death is an Exarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>See? This is what I was talking about when I said that the restrictive nature of the setting kept me from getting into it. One of devs showed up specifically to say that my interpretation of mortality as part of the Lie, which would actually make me interested in the setting, was Very Wrong, and that Only Bad Guys Want To Be Immortal (as he has said in the past). I have no interest in playing a game where one of the developers explicitly shows up to remind people that the game is partially based on the premise that one of the ideologies most important to me is Bad And Wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:46:48-07:00","id":966928,"title":"","content":"Them ummm... don't ??? <br /> <br /> You seem to be taking it too personally, nobody's telling you the ideology is wrong, it's just that way in the game's world. Like for instance being a zealous close minded fanatic is kind of a sensible thing in WH40k and while such a notion would normally apall me but that doesn't prevent me from enjoying the verse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:48:44-07:00","id":966930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966901#post966901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See? This is what I was talking about when I said that the restrictive nature of the setting kept me from getting into it. One of devs showed up specifically to say that my interpretation of mortality as part of the Lie, which would actually make me interested in the setting, was Very Wrong, and that Only Bad Guys Want To Be Immortal (as he has said in the past). I have no interest in playing a game where one of the developers explicitly shows up to remind people that the game is partially based on the premise that one of the ideologies most important to me is Bad And Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gecko i think you're missing something here. at least in a Mage centric worldview death is a whole tenth of the entire universe. Death is part of everything. Eliminating death from the univese is totally a noble and worthy cause. but not to a Mage,a Mage sees knows for a fact we need Death. it's part of the setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:58:23-07:00","id":966934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966930#post966930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gecko i think you're missing something here. at least in a Mage centric worldview death is a whole tenth of the entire universe. Death is part of everything. Eliminating death from the univese is totally a noble and worthy cause. but not to a Mage,a Mage sees knows for a fact we need Death. it's part of the setting</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I'm missing that, in that I explicitly said that that was one of my major problems with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:05:02-07:00","id":966940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966679#post966679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fear of Death is an Exarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but nobody really likes him and his followers. They never get invited to the really good Seer parties. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:13:05-07:00","id":966946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966901#post966901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See? This is what I was talking about when I said that the restrictive nature of the setting kept me from getting into it. One of devs showed up specifically to say that my interpretation of mortality as part of the Lie, which would actually make me interested in the setting, was Very Wrong, and that Only Bad Guys Want To Be Immortal (as he has said in the past). I have no interest in playing a game where one of the developers explicitly shows up to remind people that the game is partially based on the premise that one of the ideologies most important to me is Bad And Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you should ignore him. No, seriously kudos for him to make the game but if you think death as part of the lie is cool, then run with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966783#post966783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm.... *scratches head* First, I've been using &quot;fight,&quot; not &quot;war&quot; for this conversation. And fight can imply non-violent, non-physical struggles as well as military-style fights.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I feel compelled to point out that one of the basic underlying principles in Mage is that the Pentacle and Seers are engaged in a <i>cold</i> <i>war</i>. Cold wars come with implications of espionage and propaganda instead of bloody battles, and that comes with different connotations. This is Mage, a game of mental challenges, not Werewolf, the game of hunting prey.<br /> <br /> Third? I think that you can't assume that war is carrying the same baggage for everyone, nor critize someone for using the term correctly - even Marriam-Webster says that &quot;war&quot; can mean &quot;a situation in which people or groups compete or fight against each other.&quot; Even the most literal interpretation of the use of war here is correct. And we don't live in a literal world - we live in one with figurative meanings and different perspectives.<br /> <br /> So, when you say that <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;fighting an oppressive false reality is not a focus in your typical Mage game,&quot; </span></span></i></span>I have to disagree. There are fights of all sorts, and there is a focus on opposing the Exarchs and Seers, as those are the major antagonists of the whole game. I think its rather typical in most Mage games to have fights against the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree here, war agaisnt the lie doesnt have the &quot;baggage&quot; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> assumes it has to be honest. Yeah you cant &quot;fireball to the face&quot; the lie true but even in Ascension i doubt many players read the &quot;Fight the consensus&quot; and interpret &quot;oh i can kill it with fire&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the typical game i agree with MCN. The &quot;typical&quot; mage game is usually fight...erm conflict with the Lie (tm)......in whatever violent or non violent way you choose. I have seen countless game about fighting the seers/the Lie(tm)/the exarch indirectly or directly, specially in 1st ed.<br /> <br /> I know because im on the minority of dm/players who just dont care about the Lie (tm) aspect and the whole prisioners of the Lie (tm) analogy for mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966640#post966640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage doesn't really feature a war for reality, and it's generally pretty amoral. Like, the only thing Mage really comes out and says &quot;this is bad!&quot; about is Hubris. Immortality is entirely possible for mages through safe, responsivle means. It's just that it's much easier to do it through dubious, harmful means. And that's to emphasize the theme of Hubris. Do you live with the limitations of doing it the safe way, or do you throw caution to the winds and pursue your goals at any cost? Do you take the quick and easy path, or do you take the time to do it right and proper? That's the point, not a condemnation against transhumanism or whatever your bugbear is.</div> </div> </div> </div>how do you reach immortality responsibly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:13:23-07:00","id":966947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966934#post966934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I'm missing that, in that I explicitly said that that was one of my major problems with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>kay then,so let me throw my two cents here. i think Empathy as concept is tied to Death as concept. We know murder is wrong because we all know how death hurt us. many people value their friendships and relationships because,among other reasons, they know nothing is forever. if everything is eternal,it's much harder to value other things,including other people feelings. it's hard to be kind when you're immortal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:26:25-07:00","id":966951,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's been asked the other way, so I'm gonna risk being the fool and ask &quot;Why shouldn't immortality be such a big deal?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, c'mon, it's one been one of the big holy grails for humanity since day one. This is a game where your obsessions lead you to bad places, where the greater of worth a prize is in your mind, the more it's you'll break yourself for it, or condemn others to burn for it(which is still breaking yourself). For something humanity has dreamt of for so long with a central story premise like that, not only was this kind of the way it was going to always be, it's just good storytelling and gaming conflict. Here's what you want, and here's a thousand roads where the toll might not be worth it. Will you take them, or will you dig to find a road that doesn't make you more of a monster than you already are?<br /> <br /> Wanting immortality to be free just makes it a cheap wank-off fantasy. Immortality with a Price-that's conflict, that's engagement, that's <i>fun</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:33:05-07:00","id":966954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966901#post966901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See? This is what I was talking about when I said that the restrictive nature of the setting kept me from getting into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry you feel that way. Unfortunately, the game can't be everything to everyone, and if the game doesn't satisfy you personally, you're free to change it in your home games or to not play it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966901#post966901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of devs showed up specifically to say that my interpretation of mortality as part of the Lie, which would actually make me interested in the setting, was Very Wrong, and that Only Bad Guys Want To Be Immortal</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what he said at all. He made the completely accurate statement that Death is an Arcanum, and extrapolated that it must therefore not be part of the Lie by the setting as-written. He then said that the fear of death is one of the symbols that defines current reality that was not present in the Time Before. He made no condemnation against your preferences, and no implication that immortality is something only immoral people desire. Heck, if fear of death is an Exarch, good and bad people alike should feel it, as it's an inherent part of reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966901#post966901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no interest in playing a game where one of the developers explicitly shows up to remind people that the game is partially based on the premise that one of the ideologies most important to me is Bad And Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's not something Dave actually said. He made a statement about the facts of the setting, with no inherent value judgment attached to it, and you chose to take it personally. Frankly, who cares what Dave says? If you want to run Mage as a gnostic superhero game where death is an illusion and the good guys fight to break humanity of that illusion, go for it! Have fun. It doesn't really matter if that's the default assumption of the setting or not, that's the beauty of RPGs. If you don't like the default setting you are fully empowered to play under different setting assumptions that you do like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:41:05-07:00","id":966958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966946#post966946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree here, war agaisnt the lie doesnt have the &amp;quot;baggage&amp;quot; <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> assumes it has to be honest. Yeah you cant &amp;quot;fireball to the face&amp;quot; the lie true but even in Ascension i doubt many players read the &amp;quot;Fight the consensus&amp;quot; and interpret &amp;quot;oh i can kill it with fire&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the typical game i agree with MCN. The &amp;quot;typical&amp;quot; mage game is usually fight...erm conflict with the Lie (tm)......in whatever violent or non violent way you choose. I have seen countless game about fighting the seers/the Lie(tm)/the exarch indirectly or directly, specially in 1st ed.<br /> <br /> I know because im on the minority of dm/players who just dont care about the Lie (tm) aspect and the whole prisioners of the Lie (tm) analogy for mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's cool. I still don't really think we're saying different things here, I just made assumptions about what Gecko meant by &quot;fight against oppressive reality&quot; based on my own baggage and worded my response poorly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966901#post966901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do you reach immortality responsibly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Veil of Moments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:44:29-07:00","id":966960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966951#post966951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's been asked the other way, so I'm gonna risk being the fool and ask &amp;quot;Why shouldn't immortality be such a big deal?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, c'mon, it's one been one of the big holy grails for humanity since day one. This is a game where your obsessions lead you to bad places, where the greater of worth a prize is in your mind, the more it's you'll break yourself for it, or condemn others to burn for it.(which is still breaking yourself). For something humanity has dreamt of for so long with a central story premise like that, not only was this kind of the way it was going to always be, it's just good storytelling and gaming conflict. Here's what you want, and here's a thousand roads where the toll might not be worth it. Will you take them, or will you dig to find a road that doesn't make you more of a monster than you already are?<br /> <br /> Wanting immortality to be free just makes it a cheap wank-off fantasy. Immortality with a Price-that's conflict, that's engagement, that's <i>fun</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://67.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m7nyqunANL1rziwwco1_400.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:05:27-07:00","id":966971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966951#post966951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's been asked the other way, so I'm gonna risk being the fool and ask &quot;Why shouldn't immortality be such a big deal?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, c'mon, it's one been one of the big holy grails for humanity since day one. This is a game where your obsessions lead you to bad places, where the greater of worth a prize is in your mind, the more it's you'll break yourself for it, or condemn others to burn for it(which is still breaking yourself). For something humanity has dreamt of for so long with a central story premise like that, not only was this kind of the way it was going to always be, it's just good storytelling and gaming conflict. Here's what you want, and here's a thousand roads where the toll might not be worth it. Will you take them, or will you dig to find a road that doesn't make you more of a monster than you already are?<br /> <br /> Wanting immortality to be free just makes it a cheap wank-off fantasy. Immortality with a Price-that's conflict, that's engagement, that's <i>fun</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside how needlessly dismissive &quot;cheap wank-off fantasy&quot;, you can get immortality in ChroD for the cost of a single willpower dot if you can find a vampire willing to make the trade. In Ascension, immortality was a two-dot merit. I get that Awakening isn't either of those, but some of the points people have made are two-way streets. Immortality is unlikely to have a gameplay effect and few mages live to die of old age anyway. Those things given, I'm not why immortality shouldn't be cheap. And this isn't even about it not being cheap- it's about how Dave has explicitly said that he's opposed to the idea and the game is structured to oppose it. <br /> <br /> Dave has explicitly said in other places that he's against anyone being able to become immortal and that Mage is anti-transhumanist. I would obviously ignore that if I were to play it, but I'm sure you can see how disheartening it is for me to know that one of the leading designers holds those beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-10-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:13:28-07:00","id":966975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting aside how needlessly dismissive &quot;cheap wank-off fantasy&quot;, you can get immortality in ChroD for the cost of a single willpower dot if you can find a vampire willing to make the trade. In Ascension, immortality was a two-dot merit. I get that Awakening isn't either of those, but some of the points people have made are two-way streets. Immortality is unlikely to have a gameplay effect and few mages live to die of old age anyway. Those things given, I'm not why immortality shouldn't be cheap. And this isn't even about it not being cheap- it's about how Dave has explicitly said that he's opposed to the idea and the game is structured to oppose it.<br /> <br /> Dave has explicitly said in other places that he's against anyone being able to become immortal and that Mage is anti-transhumanist. I would obviously ignore that if I were to play it, but I'm sure you can see how disheartening it is for me to know that one of the leading designers holds those beliefs.<br /> <br /> Also, I actually think that posts consisting only of reaction images are against forum rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said this in other places too, but I firmly believe that after a text is published, the author's intention is just as relevant as anyone else's. I apply this standard just as strongly to my own work. What matters is what's in the text. And since the games are intended to be toolbox, you can use or ignore whatever you want. You understand that, which is why you're making a game of your own. I feel like the conversation we're having is a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:30:16-07:00","id":966984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting aside how needlessly dismissive &amp;quot;cheap wank-off fantasy&amp;quot;, you can get immortality in ChroD for the cost of a single willpower dot if you can find a vampire willing to make the trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and you know, being a vampire, which pretty much sucks, and not just because of the pun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Ascension, immortality was a two-dot merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of all the not remotely horrifying escapist urban fantasy that plagued cWoD, Acenscion was the least horrifying, most escapist bit of urban fantasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that Awakening isn't either of those, but some of the points people have made are two-way streets. Immortality is unlikely to have a gameplay effect and few mages live to die of old age anyway. Those things given, I'm not why immortality shouldn't be cheap. And this isn't even about it not being cheap- it's about how Dave has explicitly said that he's opposed to the idea and the game is structured to oppose it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is a default assumption of the setting. Again, sorry you don't like that being a default assumption, but it is what it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave has explicitly said in other places that he's against anyone being able to become immortal and that Mage is anti-transhumanist. I would obviously ignore that if I were to play it, but I'm sure you can see how disheartening it is for me to know that one of the leading designers holds those beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I very much doubt that Dave has actually said that. I don't doubt that you interpreted that from something he said, but I do doubt that was his intended message. And even if it was? Death of the author, friend. If you want something out of Mage that Dave didn't intend in the developing of it, it's your right as the audience to not give a crap about his intent. Or do give a crap about it, it's really up to you. Just seems like if you have such a problem with Dave's take on the setting you'd save yourself a lot of grief by either hacking the setting or passing on it than griping about it not being what you want it to be by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I actually think that posts consisting only of reaction images are against forum rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not, posts that only contain images and/or brief text that serve only to express displeasure with the thread are considered threadcrapping, which is against the rules. That said, if you think something I post in black text is against the rules, by all means, flag it. One of the other mods will review it. I'm not above the rules. If it's in red text, use the Contact Us link instead of the flag function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:40:05-07:00","id":966987,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> Well, you're unhappy and determined to be so. Here's a hanky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:40:42-07:00","id":966988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting aside how needlessly dismissive &quot;cheap wank-off fantasy&quot;, you can get immortality in ChroD for the cost of a single willpower dot if you can find a vampire willing to make the trade. In Ascension, immortality was a two-dot merit. I get that Awakening isn't either of those, but some of the points people have made are two-way streets. Immortality is unlikely to have a gameplay effect and few mages live to die of old age anyway. Those things given, I'm not why immortality shouldn't be cheap. And this isn't even about it not being cheap- it's about how Dave has explicitly said that he's opposed to the idea and the game is structured to oppose it.<br /> <br /> Dave has explicitly said in other places that he's against anyone being able to become immortal and that Mage is anti-transhumanist. I would obviously ignore that if I were to play it, but I'm sure you can see how disheartening it is for me to know that one of the leading designers holds those beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although you note Awakening is not the same, your comparisons to Ascension and Requiem are nevertheless odd.<br /> <br /> Ascension is a totally different setting, with far different foundations and presumptions. Requiem is at least in the CofD, but you claim all it costs is one Willpower dot and a vampire for immortality. That's disingenuous. There are pages and pages of mechanical and narrative disadvantages to the vampiric condition (e.g., no sunlight, no food, drinking blood, the Beast, etc.) that accompany such immortality.<br /> <br /> ArcaneArts primary point was that in the CofD (and virtually all classic horror and fantasy settings), immortality has a high price. To suggest that price in the CofD is only one willpower point and a willing vampire, and nothing else, is just not true.<br /> <br /> You are, of course, free to change any aspect of a setting you so choose (or not play a particular game at all). However, complaining that Dave, the developer of Mage, is willing to engage in fan discussion and honestly answer fundamental questions about the setting is also strange. <i>He's not attacking you or your beliefs</i>. He's stating facts about a horror game that you are free to play or not. Moreover, even if he were to offer his personal opinions on relevant topics such as the wisdom of immortality, he's entitled to his views as much as you are to yours, and that's one of the points of an open forum such as this. <br /> <br /> If you want transhuman values, easy immortality and other mostly science fiction setting elements and themes, the CofD might not simply suit you tastes in anything resembling its canon form. That's certainly acceptable, but no game is perfectly tailored to everyone, and repeatedly offering the same complaints accomplishes nothing. <br /> <br /> There are good rpgs and settings such as Eclipse Phase and GURPS: Transhuman Space that appear to offer what you want. I would recommend you check them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:41:22-07:00","id":966989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966987#post966987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> Well, you're unhappy and determined to be so. Here's a hanky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very helpful. I wonder, do you lurk around restaurants and leap out whenever someone criticizes the food, insults at the ready?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-10-2016, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:42:03-07:00","id":966990,"title":"","content":"There isn't any helping someone who insists on not being helped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:45:19-07:00","id":966992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966990#post966990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't any helping someone who insists on not being helped.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet for some arcane reason you insist on keeping up a constant stream of snide comments. <br /> <br /> And yes, Dave has explicitly described Mage as anti-transhumanist and has said that he personally finds the idea of immortality &quot;abhorrent&quot;. I can object to that and to the ways it manifests in the game, and say that it harms my ability to enjoy it. The fact that I'm perfectly willing to ignore what Dave say doesn't mean that I can't say why I'm ignoring it. <br /> <br /> And the reason why I object to immortality being monstrous in Awakening is because I don't really think it works as a horror game. I think it's much less horror-y and much more wish-fulfillment-y than Ascension was, and I don't think it does a good job of presenting Mages as monsters. If I were to play Awakening, and not Transgression, I would be playing it as essentially an urban fantasy superhero game, and I'm talking about it in those terms, since I think that's basically what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:52:21-07:00","id":966993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting aside how needlessly dismissive &quot;cheap wank-off fantasy&quot;, you can get immortality in ChroD for the cost of a single willpower dot if you can find a vampire willing to make the trade. In Ascension, immortality was a two-dot merit. I get that Awakening isn't either of those, but some of the points people have made are two-way streets. Immortality is unlikely to have a gameplay effect and few mages live to die of old age anyway. Those things given, I'm not why immortality shouldn't be cheap. And this isn't even about it not being cheap- it's about how Dave has explicitly said that he's opposed to the idea and the game is structured to oppose it.<br /> <br /> Dave has explicitly said in other places that he's against anyone being able to become immortal and that Mage is anti-transhumanist. I would obviously ignore that if I were to play it, but I'm sure you can see how disheartening it is for me to know that one of the leading designers holds those beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for Ascension. Ascension had different gaming principles to Awakening. The 90's were a weird time.<br /> <br /> In regards to how cheap immortality is, I can do you one cheaper and point at Mummy, where you not only live forever but also never really have to run the risk of dying due to destruction.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Vampire and Mummy are <i>exactly</i> what people fighting over in this thread, a prime example of Immortality without costs that make you more of a monster. Cutting the sarcasm and going for an aside here, both of those don't just give you immortality just for the sake of having and going &quot;Woo hoo&quot; with it, it makes us reveal things about ourselves with it.<br /> <br /> But yeah, no, the larger context is not &quot;I just want immortality&quot;, it's &quot;I want immortality with no strings attached&quot;, and that's honestly just flat escapism, and that's boring to me. I play games to have conflicts, not to just exercise power all willy-nilly. I am interested in prices paid and people changed. Having Immortality as an Obsession and trying to fulfill it without falling into the pitfalls of making light of a thing I desire? That sounds way cooler to me.<br /> <br /> Putting Dave aside for a second here, my point is that Mage is a game of the human will and the consequences of it's conquest against reality as it is. Immortality, on this stage,is more interesting and fun as a fight, a thing to achieve. The game still has options for immortality that are, at the very least, morally/ethically neutral. Ascension is the grandest immortality of all, and while there's mixed feelings on that one, it's not, say, the Tremere. Hell, Ascension is still mostly treated as desirable in Awakening. And that's just one thing. You might disagree with Dave's attitude and how that has structured Mage, but all the same, there is a fun conflict available. Immortality can still be sought. It can theoretically be obtained barring ST fiat. And thus, the quest for a long held dream of humanity is a good stage for a game. It's fun, it's conflict.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not going to speak for Dave or about Dave. That said, I know I am pretty widely regarded as, what's the word, a deathist? Yeah, one of them. Now, by and large my context on that has always been &quot;Personal dislike of it aside*, if I could get immortality, then I have to assume other people can too, and that just sounds like a great way to break society&quot;-by and large, I just don't think humanity as a species is mature enough to handle having immortality. We don't even have equal pay between genders or the ability to go a presidency with a black guy without calling him a nigger, yeah, society could only get more fucked up at this point if we had the ability to make people immortal. Once the human family grows up some? Sure, we can talk about it, but for now? Nah, not worth the shit. Cyberpunk, worth remembering.<br /> <br /> And, personally, I see that Mage works in accordance to that idea. Hell, even what it says about immortality as a negative fits into that principle-while immortality itself might be a problem, the larger problem is the lack of wisdom and maturity in the people who seek it, a lack of wisdom and maturity that the species as a whole is prone to. Mage's main &quot;moral thrust&quot; is that a person owns themselves, that their Power is firmly kept in the hand of their Will rather than relying on more ephemeral supports provided by Lies we tell ourselves(and man oh man is Mage a game about Lying to our Selves) or accept from beyond us.<br /> <br /> Dave has sharpened the anti-transhumanist points in Mage(They were always there). I get that, I respect his opinion, and I actually share them to some degree. But I think there's very clearly room in Mage to fight that notion if someone so desired. So, fuck any of us who disagrees. Play a game of Mage where you obtain immortality, and you do not make of it a light thing, but instead show with power and maturity it's worth. Pay for it with conflict and drama and growing understanding and bright defiance.<br /> <br /> It's not like Promethean, where you will gut out far more of the game trying to play against intentions. Mage may not be thrilled about it, but it has the room for that story. It's there for you to tell it. It is there for you to Will it, if you are Wise enough to do so.<br /> <br /> This, by the way, has been why I've mostly ignored this thread. I don't see the conflict. I can tell that story. It's not barred to me. But maybe that's just me.<br /> <br /> *I'm not willing to argue about this point, but suffice it to say, one of the more important things I've heard is &quot;There is always such a thing as too much living&quot; and I have been around too many people who I feel have proven the point for me to greatly personally desire endless life. Fight to extend the lifespan, sure, some people don't live enough, but endless life? Nah. I can feel that there will be that time when I have lived all I need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:56:11-07:00","id":966994,"title":"","content":"I think things are mostly settled (though I don't think what I want for Promethean is really that radical), but I should say that if I did become immortal and got tired of it, I'd put myself in some kind of stasis instead of killing myself. I don't like death because it's irreversible. You can't decide you don't like it and go back. Death doesn't end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:01:06-07:00","id":966996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966989#post966989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With all due respect, you're basically complaining that Awakening does not positively portray or allow transhuman or similar values, and the developer admits as much. The problem is that no one, whether it be OPP, Dave, or anyone else, ever promised or suggested this modern horror game would give you what you want.<br /> <br /> We get that you want a modern wizard game that includes elements like easy immortality. Your are entitled to your tastes and preferences, but no rpg game suits everyone. The canon setting and themes of Mage are apparently not what you want. You can either change them at your table or not play at all. Heck, if you believe the market demands a transhuman modern horror magic game, you are free to write it yourself. However, repeatedly complaining that a game setting than a great many very much enjoy is somehow bad or deficient or must officially change to suit your own tastes is presumptuous and unproductive.<br /> <br /> Simply, what you want or expect from Mage in many ways appears incompatible with the setting as fundamentally designed and intended. Rather than complain about what you don't like (and attacking the developer for not giving it to you), start threads requesting and discussing <i>alternative </i>settings or hacks to achieve what you like. Threads such as this are always popping-up in all the particular game forums, and results in far more amicable and constructive dialogue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:12:20-07:00","id":966999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966994#post966994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think things are mostly settled (though I don't think what I want for Promethean is really that radical), but I should say that if I did become immortal and got tired of it, I'd put myself in some kind of stasis instead of killing myself. I don't like death because it's irreversible. You can't decide you don't like it and go back. Death doesn't end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. I personally don't know that for sure. I'm sure you could blame that on a deep entrenchment in the mythos and spiritual perspectives of the world, and I wouldn't blame you if you did. But the possibility of death as transformation is a strong feeling in my life, so I'm not going to worry about it.<br /> <br /> Either way, if I come back, I'd want to be something new. I don't think I could bear being the same person for always and eternity. Even if I did the stasis thing, I'd want to come back not as I was. So I might as well just die.<br /> <br /> I am an infinite being. There's no point to that if I am only merely a portion of my infinity. There is always more to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:12:35-07:00","id":967000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966992#post966992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, Dave has explicitly described Mage as anti-transhumanist and has said that he personally finds the idea of immortality &quot;abhorrent&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do remember that conversation, and credit where it's due, it was in response to being directly asked about it. He's entitled to that opinion, just as you're entitled to disagree with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966992#post966992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can object to that and to the ways it manifests in the game, and say that it harms my ability to enjoy it. The fact that I'm perfectly willing to ignore what Dave say doesn't mean that I can't say why I'm ignoring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor does it mean that others can't disagree with your reasoning and explain why. That's kind of how forum discussions work. But it does seem like that discussion causes you a great deal of distress, which leaves me wondering why you continue to engage in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966992#post966992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the reason why I object to immortality being monstrous in Awakening is because I don't really think it works as a horror game. I think it's much less horror-y and much more wish-fulfillment-y than Ascension was, and I don't think it does a good job of presenting Mages as monsters. If I were to play Awakening, and not Transgression, I would be playing it as essentially an urban fantasy superhero game, and I'm talking about it in those terms, since I think that's basically what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I said earlier that trying to treat Mage as a superhero game seems to be causing you more problems than it's solving. It seems that the root of your issue is a refusal to meet Mage on its own terms. You don't treat it as a horror game, so the elements that are intended as horror strike you as out of place. Go figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:13:59-07:00","id":967001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966994#post966994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think things are mostly settled (though I don't think what I want for Promethean is really that radical), but I should say that if I did become immortal and got tired of it, I'd put myself in some kind of stasis instead of killing myself. I don't like death because it's irreversible. You can't decide you don't like it and go back. Death doesn't end.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you know death doesn't end if you've never died before?<br /> <br /> Personally, I find it highly unlikely that it's as permanent as you seem to think. We don't fully understand what the heck consciousness is yet, but most other things that make up a living organism can't ever be created or destroyed, they can only change state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:23:43-07:00","id":967005,"title":"","content":"I would just note that not positively portraying transhuman ideas and mores in a modern <i><b>horror</b></i> setting is really not that unusual or provocative. The CofD is not bright future science fiction or a superhero setting.<br /> <br /> I can only imagine the reaction of some people when Deviant, also developed by Dave, is released and very directly deals with setting and themes concerning body horror. I don't believe inspirations like David Cronenberg were fans of transhumanism...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-10-2016, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:23:56-07:00","id":967006,"title":"","content":"I'd add a note to what Charlaquin said above that regardless of how you think off death in real life (lets please not start that discussion here) in the game's world the guys who know the most about death will tell you that it's a transition and not a stare. AND it actually is reversible, it just comes with a cost/risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:52:49-07:00","id":967022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967001#post967001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you know death doesn't end if you've never died before?<br /> <br /> Personally, I find it highly unlikely that it's as permanent as you seem to think. We don't fully understand what the heck consciousness is yet, but most other things that make up a living organism can't ever be created or destroyed, they can only change state.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the kind of thing I'd ever gamble with. I have no evidence that consciousness can persist after death, so the logical answer is to resist death for as long as possible rather than gamble that somehow, in defiance of all known science on the subject, human consciousness persists after death. This statement is roughly equivalent to &quot;we don't really know that leprechauns don't exist, so you might as well drink bleach because one of them might save you&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think so many of my characters have been gamblers or con artists because I'm fascinated by the idea of sucker bets.<br /> <br /> And in the game world? Every bit of evidence the Moros have about what happens after you die indicates that death sucks. I have and love Book Of The Dead- that's the afterlife the Moros know about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:56:28-07:00","id":967027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967022#post967022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not the kind of thing I'd ever gamble with. I have no evidence that consciousness can persist after death, so the logical answer is to resist death for as long as possible rather than gamble that somehow, in defiance of all known science on the subject, human consciousness persists after death. This statement is roughly equivalent to &quot;we don't really know that leprechauns don't exist, so you might as well drink bleach because one of them might save you&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think so many of my characters have been gamblers or con artists because I'm fascinated by the idea of sucker bets.<br /> <br /> And in the game world? Every bit of evidence the Moros have about what happens after you die indicates that death sucks. I have and love Book Of The Dead- that's the afterlife the Moros know about.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Maybe this is too much of a different conversation, and if the mods think so, please please tell me, but)<br /> <br /> May I ask what scares you about death, Gecko? And just a bit more framing, is it death in general, or death at this point in time, if that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:07:49-07:00","id":967033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967027#post967027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Maybe this is too much of a different conversation, and if the mods think so, please please tell me, but)<br /> <br /> May I ask what scares you about death, Gecko? And just a bit more framing, is it death in general, or death at this point in time, if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've made it clear. The most likely guess for me to make is that death is the complete and irreversible cessation of consciousness. Nothing could possibly scare me as much as that. The permanence of it is a part of it. Pain ends. Illnesses can be healed. Boredom passes. Even diseases and problems we can't cure now could potentially be fixed. But bringing people back from the dead, really resurrecting them and not just copying them, is probably truly impossible.<br /> <br /> At this moment in time, I feel satisfaction regarding the dinner I just ate. I feel happy that you asked me in such a compassionate way. I feel a slight pain in my leg. I feel pleasant anticipation for a movie I'm going to watch tonight. If I died, I could never feel any of those things, or anything else, ever again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:13:57-07:00","id":967035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967033#post967033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I've made it clear. The most likely guess for me to make is that death is the complete and irreversible cessation of consciousness. Nothing could possibly scare me as much as that. The permanence of it is a part of it. Pain ends. Illnesses can be healed. Boredom passes. Even diseases and problems we can't cure now could potentially be fixed. But bringing people back from the dead, really resurrecting them and not just copying them, is probably truly impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>What scares you about cessation of consciousness? The inability to create? The inability to interact with family and loved ones? I'm trying to dig deeper here.<br /> <br /> Because like I understand what others are saying about how we don't really know what happens to the consciousness upon death. Personally, I agree with you that death is probably the end. But I find I'm not scared by that, and whenever my family dies (my uncle just died in the past week, actually, so I've recently faced this), I find I'm not sad or scared by it as such. I'm more somber and accepting. Both of my mother's grandmother's died realy, really old. One of them died at 107, the other died at 101. And my mother was and still is extremely affected by it. For me, I was just like, &quot;I lived a good life with them, they lived a good life, I'm not upset, it was time&quot;. Honestly, I don't even cry, and I didn't when I got the call about my uncle. I was somber, and more introspective, and I'm not a crier in general. So I guess I'm trying to understand the position of others who react differently. I'm interested in the philosophy of it.<br /> <br /> (Unrelated side-note, my great-grandmother who died at 107 dated Al Capone.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 09-10-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:33:18-07:00","id":967079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966992#post966992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet for some arcane reason you insist on keeping up a constant stream of snide comments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm likewise mystified by your insistence on continuing to bring up a topic that's going in circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:42:59-07:00","id":967090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967035#post967035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What scares you about cessation of consciousness? The inability to create? The inability to interact with family and loved ones? I'm trying to dig deeper here.<br /> <br /> Because like I understand what others are saying about how we don't really know what happens to the consciousness upon death. Personally, I agree with you that death is probably the end. But I find I'm not scared by that, and whenever my family dies (my uncle just died in the past week, actually, so I've recently faced this), I find I'm not sad or scared by it as such. I'm more somber and accepting. Both of my mother's grandmother's died realy, really old. One of them died at 107, the other died at 101. And my mother was and still is extremely affected by it. For me, I was just like, &amp;quot;I lived a good life with them, they lived a good life, I'm not upset, it was time&amp;quot;. Honestly, I don't even cry, and I didn't when I got the call about my uncle. I was somber, and more introspective, and I'm not a crier in general. So I guess I'm trying to understand the position of others who react differently. I'm interested in the philosophy of it.<br /> <br /> (Unrelated side-note, my great-grandmother who died at 107 dated Al Capone.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be perfectly honest: I am genuinely not sure how one can not be scared of the permanent and irreversible cessation of consciousness. In fact, Terror Management Theory says that a great deal of human behavior comes from the human need to suppress the terror of death, because of how disastrous it is mentally and emotionally to fully comprehend it. I've explained it- death means that you can never experience anything or feel anything ever again. And that horrifies me, and I would do anything to put it off or escape it. <br /> <br /> To be honest, if I lived in ChroD, I'd be more willing to die- magic exists there, so there could be an afterlife, and even the Underworld, shitty as it is, would be better than ceasing to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:47:47-07:00","id":967093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967090#post967090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've explained it- death means that you can never experience anything or feel anything ever again. And that horrifies me, and I would do anything to put it off or escape it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry. I haven't meant to ask you to repeat yourself, I honestly want to understand. I've been trying to understand where you're coming from this whole time. All I wanted was what you posted there, that helps me understand. I'm sorry that been hostile. I haven't meant to, but what I meant to do doesn't matter as much as what I actually did, and I apologize.<br /> <br /> I really, really have just been trying to understand, because I don't feel the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:52:50-07:00","id":967095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967093#post967093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry. I haven't meant to ask you to repeat yourself, I honestly want to understand. I've been trying to understand where you're coming from this whole time. All I wanted was what you posted there, that helps me understand. I'm sorry that been hostile. I haven't meant to, but what I meant to do doesn't matter as much as what I actually did, and I apologize.<br /> <br /> I really, really have just been trying to understand, because I don't feel the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>No no no, please don't apologize. You haven't been hostile at all. You have been incredibly polite and compassionate throughout all of this. <br /> <br /> I wasn't expressing frustration, I was saying that I couldn't understand how someone couldn't find the idea of cessation of existence terrifying. My reason for hating death isn't anything more complicated than a fear of permanent cessation of existence, because to me, I don't really need another reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:01:06-07:00","id":967103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967095#post967095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No no no, please don't apologize. You haven't been hostile at all. You have been incredibly polite and compassionate throughout all of this.<br /> <br /> I wasn't expressing frustration, I was saying that I couldn't understand how someone couldn't find the idea of cessation of existence terrifying. My reason for hating death isn't anything more complicated than a fear of permanent cessation of existence, because to me, I don't really need another reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I didn't want to invalidate you or your concerns if I actually had hurt you.<br /> <br /> I understand that. I suppose I just see the potential to live on in other ways, like my influences in the field of history, fiction writing, by raising children (I want to, I'm not saying it's for everyone), etc. That feels more fulfilling to me personally than the thought of living forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:03:55-07:00","id":967105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966984#post966984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of all the not remotely horrifying escapist urban fantasy that plagued cWoD, Acenscion was the least horrifying, most escapist bit of urban fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont agree there. To me Ascension revised, with the resonance mechanic, reached personal horror way better than Awakening has so far by understanding the &quot;personal&quot; in &quot;personal horror&quot; by allowing your actions to shape your magic through time instead of one-size-fits-all morality system which is passable for &quot;horror&quot; but not so much &quot;personal horror&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966971#post966971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave has explicitly said in other places that he's against anyone being able to become immortal and that Mage is anti-transhumanist. I would obviously ignore that if I were to play it, but I'm sure you can see how disheartening it is for me to know that one of the leading designers holds those beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look i feel you, i dislike many of the views/ideas Dave has for mage. From his views on astral over the umbra, mages powerlevel being so unecesary high for a thematic to a level that is beating a deadhorse more than driving the point home and his idea that hunters should all suffer quiessence because humans should never be a treat to mages.<br /> <br /> So i suggest a different approach to see the situation, now that you know why he doesnt support the rules/concept you like you can remove or add the elements you like without doubting if you &quot;not getting it&quot; or &quot;playing it wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally i wouldnt make inmortality available because i like the reaper legacies too much but if you dont mind making them kinda pointless then all good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966993#post966993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, no, the larger context is not &quot;I just want immortality&quot;, it's &quot;I want immortality with no strings attached&quot;, and that's honestly just flat escapism, and that's boring to me. I play games to have conflicts, not to just exercise power all willy-nilly. I am interested in prices paid and people changed. Having Immortality as an Obsession and trying to fulfill it without falling into the pitfalls of making light of a thing I desire? That sounds way cooler to me.<br /> <br /> Putting Dave aside for a second here, my point is that Mage is a game of the human will and the consequences of it's conquest against reality as it is. Immortality, on this stage,is more interesting and fun as a fight, a thing to achieve. The game still has options for immortality that are, at the very least, morally/ethically neutral. Ascension is the grandest immortality of all, and while there's mixed feelings on that one, it's not, say, the Tremere. Hell, Ascension is still mostly treated as desirable in Awakening. And that's just one thing. You might disagree with Dave's attitude and how that has structured Mage, but all the same, there is a fun conflict available. Immortality can still be sought. It can theoretically be obtained barring ST fiat. And thus, the quest for a long held dream of humanity is a good stage for a game. It's fun, it's conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with some parts of this.<br /> <br /> 1) Even in mage Ascension Inmortality isnt with not strings attached. Unaging as a merit has to come from somewhere the example given are<br /> <br /> &quot;tasted the Peach of Immortality, or she ate the Apples of the Hesperides, or she dined on the forbidden savor of mermaid\u2019s flesh. Perhaps she was injected with the perfect Iterator nanotech or Progenitor symbiote&quot;<br /> <br /> So while yes, you pay for the merit and pam your character is ageless it doesnt come from nowhere and is really up to the DM whether is factor in the story or not.<br /> <br /> The other inmortality was just casting a permanent spell on you and that was it. As carry some of the same drawback than in awakening (it could be dispelled) with the added drawback that eventually you will raise so much permanent paradox that you were forced to leave earth.<br /> <br /> 2)The question i would put consider would be &quot;is inmortality is gonna be a main focus of this PC or its just be a nifty detail&quot; not everything has to be a epic struggle. I had a player who play a half fae mage with the ageless merit and it wasnt a big deal to him.<br /> <br /> The inmortality wasnt as important as to how he processed and was affected by said inmortality which was more interesting to us than said &quot;looking for the grail&quot; as an unchanging body meant (plus life magic) a body that never learned which in this particular PC was kinda a hippy version of bojack horseman.<br /> <br /> So i dont think having inmortality as &quot;easy&quot; like in ascension is flat out boring escapism, there is way to much &quot;conventional wisdom&quot; about the follys of searching for inmortality and not that much about dealing with it...except vampire i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-10-2016, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:04:11-07:00","id":967106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967103#post967103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. I didn't want to invalidate you or your concerns if I actually had hurt you.<br /> <br /> I understand that. I suppose I just see the potential to live on in other ways, like my influences in the field of history, fiction writing, by raising children (I want to, I'm not saying it's for everyone), etc. That feels more fulfilling to me personally than the thought of living forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that doesn't appeal to me at all, because it isn't like I'd be able to experience it in any way. To me, it doesn't matter what would happen after I died if I died, because I wouldn't experience it or be aware of it in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:16:01-07:00","id":967114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=966951#post966951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's been asked the other way, so I'm gonna risk being the fool and ask &quot;Why shouldn't immortality be such a big deal?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> If you're asking that as a serious question, then my answer is, &quot;because mages make a shit ton of changes to their personal body and spirit through Attainments and spells. Why is this one bad all the rest are acceptable or laud worthy?&quot; And don't you become effectively immortal when you reach archmagery? That's what always struck me as strange. But YMMV. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm more interested in telling stories about ancient mages because of the crazy things they do as a mage with lots of experiences under their belt than trying to make anything about immortality naturally wise or hubristic or whatever. Got a ghost mage running around? I'm less concerned about the &quot;lichdom&quot; than I am about what the ghost is currently doing and why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:35:42-07:00","id":967121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967105#post967105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look i feel you, i dislike many of the views/ideas Dave has for mage. From his views on astral over the umbra, mages powerlevel being so unecesary high for a thematic to a level that is beating a deadhorse more than driving the point home and his idea that hunters should all suffer quiessence because humans should never be a treat to mages.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't want to further derail the thread or speak for Dave, I don't believe you're correctly stating or characterizing Dave's opinions or you are letting your disagreements with him color your tone.<br /> <br /> For instance, Dave never said the Quiescence is necessary so Hunters cannot be a threat to mages. Rather all humans suffer from the Quiescence. and human Hunters are no exception, thus hunting mages is unsurprisingly difficult for regular humans. <br /> <br /> I have no idea what you mean by &quot;astral over the umbra&quot; as the umbra is a WoD term, and to the extent you mean the Shadow, you point is still unclear.<br /> <br /> As to arguments about Mage's purported power level, those discussions existed well-before Dave even began writing for Mage 1e, and will likely continue after he's gone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:38:57-07:00","id":967123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967114#post967114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're asking that as a serious question, then my answer is, &quot;because mages make a shit ton of changes to their personal body and spirit through Attainments and spells. Why is this one bad all the rest are acceptable or laud worthy?&quot; And don't you become effectively immortal when you reach archmagery? That's what always struck me as strange. But YMMV.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm more interested in telling stories about ancient mages because of the crazy things they do as a mage with lots of experiences under their belt than trying to make anything about immortality naturally wise or hubristic or whatever. Got a ghost mage running around? I'm less concerned about the &quot;lichdom&quot; than I am about what the ghost is currently doing and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i agree with this, sometime mage morality (not wisdom, i mean the morality reflected in the game) feels confused with itself. There is ton of fluff that basically boils down to &quot;conventional wisdom is part of the Lie (tm) and it is just there to limit your potential by the exarchs&quot; but then there this big no-no that are so because &quot;conventional wisdom&quot;, the silver ladder is founded on that particular tennet.<br /> <br /> Remember in 1st edition, being the purple man was barely a sin (wisdom 9, maybe 8). Change the timeline wasnt even an act of hubris. Reading other peoples mind (thus violating their privacy) is not a sin nor is frowned upon in mage. Creating life is not a sin of any kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Forgot one of the basic sins 09-11-2016, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:41:02-07:00","id":967126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967114#post967114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're asking that as a serious question, then my answer is, &quot;because mages make a shit ton of changes to their personal body and spirit through Attainments and spells. Why is this one bad all the rest are acceptable or laud worthy?&quot; And don't you become effectively immortal when you reach archmagery? That's what always struck me as strange. But</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all changes are the same. The end of life transition is a fundamental supernal truth as expressed by Stygia. That's why fearing death is an expression of the oppression of the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Also, becoming effectively long-lived is not the same as being truly immortal. You might not find the distinction meaningful, but the nuance is important within the setting's cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-11-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:50:52-07:00","id":967130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967105#post967105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont agree there. To me Ascension revised, with the resonance mechanic, reached personal horror way better than Awakening has so far by understanding the &quot;personal&quot; in &quot;personal horror&quot; by allowing your actions to shape your magic through time instead of one-size-fits-all morality system which is passable for &quot;horror&quot; but not so much &quot;personal horror&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Look i feel you, i dislike many of the views/ideas Dave has for mage. From his views on astral over the umbra, mages powerlevel being so unecesary high for a thematic to a level that is beating a deadhorse more than driving the point home and his idea that hunters should all suffer quiessence because humans should never be a treat to mages.<br /> <br /> So i suggest a different approach to see the situation, now that you know why he doesnt support the rules/concept you like you can remove or add the elements you like without doubting if you &quot;not getting it&quot; or &quot;playing it wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally i wouldnt make inmortality available because i like the reaper legacies too much but if you dont mind making them kinda pointless then all good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree with some parts of this.<br /> <br /> 1) Even in mage Ascension Inmortality isnt with not strings attached. Unaging as a merit has to come from somewhere the example given are<br /> <br /> &quot;tasted the Peach of Immortality, or she ate the Apples of the Hesperides, or she dined on the forbidden savor of mermaid\u2019s flesh. Perhaps she was injected with the perfect Iterator nanotech or Progenitor symbiote&quot;<br /> <br /> So while yes, you pay for the merit and pam your character is ageless it doesnt come from nowhere and is really up to the DM whether is factor in the story or not.<br /> <br /> The other inmortality was just casting a permanent spell on you and that was it. As carry some of the same drawback than in awakening (it could be dispelled) with the added drawback that eventually you will raise so much permanent paradox that you were forced to leave earth.<br /> <br /> 2)The question i would put consider would be &quot;is inmortality is gonna be a main focus of this PC or its just be a nifty detail&quot; not everything has to be a epic struggle. I had a player who play a half fae mage with the ageless merit and it wasnt a big deal to him.<br /> <br /> The inmortality wasnt as important as to how he processed and was affected by said inmortality which was more interesting to us than said &quot;looking for the grail&quot; as an unchanging body meant (plus life magic) a body that never learned which in this particular PC was kinda a hippy version of bojack horseman.<br /> <br /> So i dont think having inmortality as &quot;easy&quot; like in ascension is flat out boring escapism, there is way to much &quot;conventional wisdom&quot; about the follys of searching for inmortality and not that much about dealing with it...except vampire i guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This might be true, but more on point, I was not talking about Ascension. It's principles are different from the area I was talking about. I said as much when I started.<br /> <br /> 2) Since much of what we're saying is the same, just ordered and framed differently, we'll put this down as difference in tastes. Much as it is not impossible to tell a story where one finds an answer to immortality that is not terrible in Mage, it is not impossible to tell a story where one is immortal and therefore deals with the consequences of it. Mage has room for that story too.<br /> <br /> That said, there are <i>consequences</i>. There is a <i>story</i>. That story <i>can change you</i>. The threat under this conversation is to have a 'mere immortality', that does nothing but pour into a bottomless glass. If I have an objection, it's that underlying pretext that immortality should be served for escapist purposes.<br /> <br /> Being blunt, Fuck Escapism. It may be a good and healthy thing for speculative fiction to provide, but it sure as shit isn't why I'm here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-11-2016, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:03:45-07:00","id":967135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967121#post967121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, Dave never said the Quiescence is necessary so Hunters cannot be a threat to mages. Rather all humans suffer from the Quiescence. and human Hunters are no exception, thus hunting mages is unsurprisingly difficult for regular humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have separate those into two related but different issue. Personally i dont like Quiessence, i think the theme of isolation from humanity is overdone and a cliche at this point and better explore in other lines. As for hunters Dave has said that he doesnt think on the balance of the other splats when making mage which is all well and good except &quot;humans&quot; are an adversary to all supernaturals (or at least, imo they should)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967121#post967121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to arguments about Mage's purported power level, those discussions existed well-before Dave even began writing for Mage 1e, and will likely continue after he's gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>What i said in my post was more about how i understand gecko about not liking the direction a particular author has given the game. I dont particularly like the approach 1st gave to the powerlevel of mage. And while 2nd is an improvement, Dave keep the theme of *this* high powelevel is necesary for the theme of abuse of power when to me, personally, it was too much and less power could still drive the point home.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967121#post967121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what you mean by &quot;astral over the umbra&quot; as the umbra is a WoD term, and to the extent you mean the Shadow, you point is still unclear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always struggle with the astral, i never got it or knew how to use or find it interesting and then i read broken diamond found this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broken diamond;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the Astral Realms as presented in Awakening and it's supplements, by the way. All the possibilities of the Umbra from the oWoD without ever forgetting that what you're experiencing is not strictly physical. The Abyss and the Supernal Realms are inside all of us, more states of the soul's being than physical places.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then it hit me, it wasnt that i didnt got it or was missing out on something, what happened was that i will never like because its all the things i consider boring and annoying. Is all the weirdness of the umbra without the fun that it actually happening and is instead is navel gazing. Its like using the thing i hate most in Ascension, the seeking, with its navel gazing boring symbolism and giving it central stage instead of being able to bypass it with a merit. I preffer to be an actual pink talking triceratops in mars who is the last of his specie than said dinosaur being a manifestation of my PCs inner child. <br /> <br /> And thats fine, i get why he like it and why he keep it in 2ed but now i know im not missing out or not &quot;getting it&quot; i just hate it. Personally i would have remove it from 2ed and expand on Emmantions. So now that i know that i disagree with the author on this fundamental level i can remove astral without doubting if i missing out on something. So my point being that once you know that you dont agree with the motive behind something in the game is easier to remove said aspect.<br /> <br /> Again, just to clarify, this is my opinion and i totally get why other people do like symbolism and exploring the inner working of soul of the world, i just dont share that taste. Not trying derail this into Astral is bad or not, just trying to exemplify how one can find the silver linning when ones view of a game doesnt line with it author.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-11-2016, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:58:30-07:00","id":967165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967106#post967106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, it doesn't matter what would happen after I died if I died, because I wouldn't experience it or be aware of it in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. For me, that's exactly the reason I'm totally comfortable with the idea of death. The way I see it, the worst case scenario is that I just cease to be, and there's nothing else. In which case, I won't be aware of my nonexistance anyway; in a manner of speaking, I won't know what I'm missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:19:58-07:00","id":967176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967165#post967165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. For me, that's exactly the reason I'm totally comfortable with the idea of death. The way I see it, the worst case scenario is that I just cease to be, and there's nothing else. In which case, I won't be aware of my nonexistance anyway; in a manner of speaking, I won't know what I'm missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. if it turns out I'm not infinite, eh, conclusions anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:59:43-07:00","id":967208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967165#post967165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. For me, that's exactly the reason I'm totally comfortable with the idea of death. The way I see it, the worst case scenario is that I just cease to be, and there's nothing else. In which case, I won't be aware of my nonexistance anyway; in a manner of speaking, I won't know what I'm missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Though personally I don't believe Death is an end but a transition so whatever. Humanity at it's current state of maturity isn't meant for actual physical Immortality of the Earth or this plane of reality until the rules set by the creator change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-11-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:28:04-07:00","id":967216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967079#post967079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm likewise mystified by your insistence on continuing to bring up a topic that's going in circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you drag your distaste for the game all over the place here like a trail left by an unhappy slug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:36:08-07:00","id":967222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967022#post967022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in the game world? Every bit of evidence the Moros have about what happens after you die indicates that death sucks. I have and love Book Of The Dead- that's the afterlife the Moros know about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Ghosts aren't the people that died (and not every dead person leaves a ghost behind) and the Underworld isn't the afterlife. I think that it was hinted that the existence of the Underworld was caused by the Fall or maybe the sundering (havn't read Dark Eras but i vaguely remember someone saying something about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T01:34:49-07:00","id":967235,"title":"","content":"What I believe about death in the real world has nothing to do with it. The game's stance on immortality is predicted on avoiding the worst parts of Ascension's setting and following through on Death being one of the foundations blocks of the setting's universe.<br /> <br /> If Death weren't an Arcanum, if we didn't have Moros in the game, I'd make &quot;is immortal&quot; a 1-dot Merit because it has no bearing on a game mechanical level. Hell, the Tremere get it as a side effect of what they do to themselves (the focus of their theme being what they did to themselves and their Hunger)<br /> <br /> I greatly enjoy games like Eclipse Phase where (as its strapline says) death is a disease that can be cured. But <i>in Mage</i> death is something the enlightened grow to accept.<br /> <br /> On that, the game happens to agree with my own real-world beliefs. It contradicts many others: In our world magic is not real, consciousness is nothing but a biochemical process and free will an illusion (most of our &quot;decisions&quot; are rationalised after the event by our brains.) While it's comforting to say &quot;that's not him&quot; in regard to people whose personalities change due to illness, it's an illusion. You are nothing more than a program running on a meat computer. When that meat breaks down, the program will end. You (anyone who reads this) are going to die. There is no afterlife, you will not &quot;go&quot; anywhere, you'll just stop. Get used to it.<br /> <br /> Awakening presents a world with Meaning behind everything. Our world has none. That's why it's compelling fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-11-2016, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T01:41:48-07:00","id":967238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967222#post967222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except Ghosts aren't the people that died (and not every dead person leaves a ghost behind) and the Underworld isn't the afterlife. I think that it was hinted that the existence of the Underworld was caused by the Fall or maybe the sundering (havn't read Dark Eras but i vaguely remember someone saying something about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Back into the game world;<br /> <br /> So, the one thing mages know that sin eaters only suspect is that ghosts aren't souls. A ghost will spend some time in the Underworld before eventually breaking down, while the soul vanishes upon death and goes... somewhere.<br /> <br /> Those mages who want to believe in an afterlife or reincarnation pin such things on the soul, and regard a ghost as an ephemeral footprint left behind by someone dying (or something, inanimate objects and animals leave ghosts, while they don't have souls. For that matter, people without souls leave ghosts. And some people leave ghosts without actually dying)<br /> <br /> The moral question is then how you treat ghosts, when your powers can warp then beyond all recognition. Is a damaged copy of someone's personality enough of a person to care about their suffering? Asshole mages and some non-sin eater bound say no. The player character types say yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T02:28:09-07:00","id":967242,"title":"","content":"(This post ended up hilariously rambly, sorry)<br /> It would be easier to follow this if there was a clearer delineation between immortality meaning 'not aging', and immortality meaning 'cannot be killed'.<br /> <br /> Only the latter is part of the CofD that &quot;is an Arcanum&quot;, the former isn't an inherent part of life even in our world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quick detour, why is using spellt to protect yourself against dying of old age bad because it's serves the Exarch that is fear of Death, but using shielding spells to protect yourself against dying from bullets morally neutral? Or is every time you activate Mage Armour also a small offering to that Exarch? Wouldn't Sanctum Defense spells be Wisdom Sins.<br /> <br /> It feels the potential to die from violence is far more intrinsic to life than the potential to age. Several forms of life have already given the middle finger to dying from age, but nothing is wholly immune to violence. Yet it is protecting yourself from ageing that is the worse sin in Mage Society, not even the most fanatical guardian will call you a Lich for activating your Mage Armour before getting into a fight... or is there a cutoff age where they <i>will</i> do that? I.e. &quot;you are above 150 years old, any attempt to prolong life including Mage Armour is considered unnatural now&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> What if humans in the CofD developed fully mundane means of becoming biologically immortal, would Mages over a certain age still be considered Liches because the idea that at some point you should pass on is so entrenched in their culture? Or would that taboo morph into a Iain Banks Culture style social pressure to not overstay your welcome in this world (not unrealistic from an OOC perspective, AFAIR Dave likes the Culture books.... or at least the Also People which IMO is one of the best Culture books). Alternatively, maybe mundane biological immortality is impossible in CofD, but then what about all the organisms that are biologically immortal in our world, do they not exist in CofD? If the humans of the CofD have to live their lifes without ever tasting Steamed Lobsters with Seared Wild Mushrooms then it truly is a world of Darkness.<br /> Random Monster idea: Trying to damage certain monsters with the spells Weight of Years or Rend Lifespan instead adds the spells' potency to their physical stats... age doesn't affect them negatively and they aren't static like the undead, they just grow bigger and meaner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T03:27:38-07:00","id":967251,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"166\" data-vbnamecard=\"166\">Joker</a> Nice ninja post. Pretty much my thoughts, saved me a lot of time writing it. Thanks. As I mentioned earlier, what about mages using magic like Life or Fate and getting ahead of modern medicine by using the Arcana as, for example, gene editing tools, with Lasting effects? The changes would be purely biological, after all, and more of a matter of convenience in getting the technology a few years earlier than other people.<br /> <br /> As for my take on immortality, to not be capable of dying means by definition to be a fundamental aspect of reality (pretty much equal to Ascending, there might be other similar forms of existence). Not aging is a wholly different matter, as I've also already mentioned.<br /> <br /> For people like Arcane, who want to know my reasons for not wanting to die of old age: I may be an aspiring scientist (B.Sc in genetics so far) but in my heart I'm really a pioneer and an explorer. In this era, you can at most explore places like dark bottoms of oceans or maybe depths of rainforests, but that doesn't bring with it the thrill of finding a widespread advanced civilization or finding a whole different continent with different climate and exciting vistas. I'm sure you know what I mean. Humans could explore like this for most of our species' history. And we will be able to do this again, at least regarding the vistas and setting up new colonies, once we leave our planet, which will hopefully be in not too distant future.<br /> <br /> So, here I am, someone who grew up with Jules Verne's books, encyclopaedias about the universe and sci-fi comics, living in the one era when I can't really fulfill my dreams. There has to be more to life than <i>this</i>. To want to extend life by supressing human aging was a completely natural conclusion of my dreams about the future to which I came at some point in my early teens. I considered the decision completely natural, an extension of all my hopes. Typical responses about &quot;family and enjoying the life now&quot; might be understandable, but after a while started to cause an allergic reaction, because those people who say this don't generally know much about human psychology to understand that what they enjoy may be uninteresting to others at best, or torturing at worst, due to drastically different personalities people tend to have. I'm happy they love their lives, but *I* could never enjoy that.<br /> <br /> Hell, even the fear of death doesn't really play a role. Fearing death has no point, it cripples you. It's the hopes, and ambitions to achieve those hopes that drive me.<br /> <br /> Now, in a mage game, consider how a character with at least a hint of my personality would react to an idea that a certain hope-crushing process is a &quot;virtue&quot; that is supposed to be &quot;embraced&quot;, combined with certain information about cosmic tyrants wanting to rid humanity of all hope and dreams. There is <i>no way</i> they wouldn't connect the two concepts, especially as culling the herd before they get too many ideas about life would be an effective control tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T04:13:41-07:00","id":967256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967251#post967251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, in a mage game, consider how a character with at least a hint of my personality would react to an idea that a certain hope-crushing process is a &quot;virtue&quot; that is supposed to be &quot;embraced&quot;, combined with certain information about cosmic tyrants wanting to rid humanity of all hope and dreams. There is <i>no way</i> they wouldn't connect the two concepts, especially as culling the herd before they get too many ideas about life would be an effective control tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go mad from the revelation? Arcana aren't just ideas, they're fundamental elements of reality that get incorporated into the way you think. You can rationalise around it, but you'll still know in your core.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems implied that the Awakened have a sort of intuitive idea of what the Lie is. There could be some secondary Lie or something like that, but Mage society in general doesn't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T04:42:12-07:00","id":967260,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5973_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5973\" data-vbnamecard=\"5973\">Prometheus</a> Two things: First, it's specifically the fear of death that the Psychopomp represents - the idea that you want to live forever not for any purpose, but simply because you're terrified of what'll be on the other side once you finally do kick it (or that there will <i>be</i> no &quot;other side&quot; at all, and you've just used up the last of your existence).<br /> <br /> Second, with your <i>particular</i> reasons for not wanting to die, I think a Mage designed around that would be better served by the Time Arcanum than just extending their life. Nowhere to explore in this era? Go back (or forward) in Time until you're in an era where that's not the case. Admittedly, with the timespans you're talking about you'd probably need an Iris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T04:53:39-07:00","id":967263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967260#post967260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5973_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5973\" data-vbnamecard=\"5973\">Prometheus</a>Second, with your <i>particular</i> reasons for not wanting to die, I think a Mage designed around that would be better served by the Time Arcanum than just extending their life. Nowhere to explore in this era? Go back (or forward) in Time until you're in an era where that's not the case. Admittedly, with the timespans you're talking about you'd probably need an Iris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought about that. The problem is that even so, the typical human life is too short. The &quot;I can't ever die&quot; type of immortality prevented by how the Death Arcanum works would not be necessary, but prolongation of life to be able to explore for longer than a bunch of decades would certainly be an important factor. You don't really create a bunch of colonies on different planets or even different systems over a few years (especially obvious when watching the current sluggish progress of space colonization), and just jumping through time to a given era would not make you a part of that exploration process, merely an outside obsever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T05:14:14-07:00","id":967271,"title":"","content":"The problem with Time magic for this is also that, yes, you could just have your character cast Temporal Stutter with a conditional Duration of 'until medicine has advanced to the point where dying of old age is choice, not a fate'. The only actual result will be your ST nodding, handing you a new character sheet and asking you to make a new character if you want to continue playing with the other PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T05:29:46-07:00","id":967274,"title":"","content":"This got me wondering, on the social side searching for inmortality is wrong per mage society morals....but what about searching inmortality for others beings?<br /> <br /> Im just picturing a mage searching for a way to extend his dog/cat life so it doesn't die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T06:10:18-07:00","id":967282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967126#post967126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all changes are the same. The end of life transition is a fundamental supernal truth as expressed by Stygia. That's why fearing death is an expression of the oppression of the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh... fearing death is an expression of tyranny because it can be used to control people, or drive them to extremes. That has nothing to do with regular mages - when effective immortality is a simple spell, you can't even say that fear motivates it to any extent. Why NOT do it? Its not a fear of death, but simply having more time to study Mysteries and achieve goals in a manner that takes more time, and likely safer since you'll feel less rushed.<br /> <br /> Fear of death... is more like the state of being a vampire or ghoul*. You are willing to do anything to be able to keep on living. You eat people. You <i>murder</i> people. Die so that I might live. And then, after time, you become a monster because you become bored. You start playing with people's lives because of you don't want to die, but you cam't feel alive either. You addict yourself to vitae, so that you can feel the rush and the power flowing through you, so you can <i>feel</i>. You're dead inside, but the body keeps on moving. That's what fear of death is like. For a mage? There's no need to go that far. You can very easily hold onto your morals, because there's nothing to compromise. There's no need to risk other's lives. There's no need to fear ennui, because mages are driven to uncover mysteries - that's their raison d'etre, and the world is full of mysteries to solve to the point a ten thousand year old magus would unlikely be bored. Granted, mages will still manipulate people, because that's how you gain mysteries and ascend and stuff, but that's no different than a non-immortal mage.<br /> <br /> Also, ascending effectively makes you immortal, and that's a desired state. So, clearly, there's caveats to the whole immorality = bad thing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm left with the feeling that liches are trying to be set up as a potential antagonist, like ghost mages were in 1e, or that one really old mage that turned into a goetic from one of DaveB's actual plays. I mean, from a story perspective, they're a rich mine of plot hooks. Its a classic thing. &quot;Super ancient mages tend to be trouble.&quot; That's actually pretty cool idea. I think the problem is more the presentation of these ancients alongside Banishers and liches and the Mad, rather than anything else. Its like people's problems with the initial presentation of Heroes, and now alchemists in Promethean. It makes sense that there would be a notable population of non-bad immortal mages, but these are an antagonist group to challenge the PCs, so they get portrated in an unfavorable light.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-11-2016, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T06:58:41-07:00","id":967290,"title":"","content":"'Immortal mage' is the definition of 'lich' though. So it's kind of weird to say 'alongside Banishers and liches and the Mad.' Are you specifically thinking of the Tremere, who are the sweet spot in the venn diagram between 'Reaper' and 'Lich?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:11:35-07:00","id":967386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967242#post967242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick detour, why is using spellt to protect yourself against dying of old age bad because it's serves the Exarch that is fear of Death, but using shielding spells to protect yourself against dying from bullets morally neutral? Or is every time you activate Mage Armour also a small offering to that Exarch? Wouldn't Sanctum Defense spells be Wisdom Sins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think using spells to protect yourself against dying of old age <i>is</i> bad, <i>per se</i>. That's pretty much the function of Veil of Moments, and that spell isn't considered evil. The things Liches do to make themselves immortal aren't bad because they serve the Exarch, they're bad because they require you to fuck with people's souls, which is a pretty serious Act of Hubris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967242#post967242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels the potential to die from violence is far more intrinsic to life than the potential to age. Several forms of life have already given the middle finger to dying from age, but nothing is wholly immune to violence. Yet it is protecting yourself from ageing that is the worse sin in Mage Society, not even the most fanatical guardian will call you a Lich for activating your Mage Armour before getting into a fight... or is there a cutoff age where they <i>will</i> do that? I.e. &amp;quot;you are above 150 years old, any attempt to prolong life including Mage Armour is considered unnatural now&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that prolonging your life, whether against aging or violence, isn't inherently &quot;bad&quot; in Mage. It's just that agelessness and/or invulnerability is very difficult to achieve, given that &quot;all things must end&quot; is a supernal truth of the universe. It's achievable, but the methods all have strings attached, and most of those strings are Hubris-related. A Wise Mage knows that she too will pass, and while she might do her best to insure her life is long, she doesn't go messing around with people's souls for the sake of forestalling that passing. Not dying isn't a bad thing, people do it all the time. What makes it bad is if you go to extreme and Hubristic lengths in order to not die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967242#post967242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if humans in the CofD developed fully mundane means of becoming biologically immortal, would Mages over a certain age still be considered Liches because the idea that at some point you should pass on is so entrenched in their culture? Or would that taboo morph into a Iain Banks Culture style social pressure to not overstay your welcome in this world (not unrealistic from an OOC perspective, AFAIR Dave likes the Culture books.... or at least the Also People which IMO is one of the best Culture books).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is beyond the scope of CofD by default, as it's assumed to be a modern or near-modern setting. These would be interesting questions for a transhuman future shard to pose, though. I'd be inclined to say that Mages would be ok with mundane methods of agelesness if they were available, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967242#post967242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, maybe mundane biological immortality is impossible in CofD, but then what about all the organisms that are biologically immortal in our world, do they not exist in CofD? If the humans of the CofD have to live their lifes without ever tasting Steamed Lobsters with Seared Wild Mushrooms then it truly is a world of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>More good questions for the game to pose. Maybe death by aging is an inherent quality of the human soul. Who knows?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967242#post967242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random Monster idea: Trying to damage certain monsters with the spells Weight of Years or Rend Lifespan instead adds the spells' potency to their physical stats... age doesn't affect them negatively and they aren't static like the undead, they just grow bigger and meaner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be a cool quality to give an Abyssal entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:02:30-07:00","id":967408,"title":"","content":"The fact that Dave considers the real world to be more horrifying than the horror-themed tabletop roleplaying game he wrote is pretty interesting. <br /> <br /> You can run a program for a pretty long time, though. I'm not sure about forever, but I'd rather live for a thousand years than a hundred, no matter what I had to do. I want to see space exploration too. I want to move my brain into a new body. I want to do and see a lot of things that I can't do in a human lifetime, and that's entirely apart from the sheer terror of irreversible cessation of existence. <br /> <br /> I think saying that death is inevitable is a bit presumptuous, actually. Think of how absurd the Internet would have seemed to somehow who lived just decades ago. Even the laws of thermodynamics can be beaten. Matter and energy can't be created or destroyed...but then where did they come from in the first place? Either they actually can be created, or casuality can be distorted or reversed. Either way provides options for the continued survival of humanity. Plus, the laws of thermodynamics only apply to our universe, which might not be the only game in town. <br /> <br /> There I go again with the gambling analogies. At least I resisted the urge to write the entire post in carny slang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:20:02-07:00","id":967417,"title":"","content":"Little off topic ( <a href=\"http://nhne-pulse.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/Reincarnation.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://nhne-pulse.org/wp-content/upl...ncarnation.jpg</a> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:25:18-07:00","id":967425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967408#post967408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Dave considers the real world to be more horrifying than the horror-themed tabletop roleplaying game he wrote is pretty interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave didn't write Mage 1e or 2e. The game's primary themes were established well before he was one author out of many in later Mage 1e supplements (and virtually every other nWOD/CofD gameline). Dave simply didn't change the primary Mage themes after he became developer for 2e.<br /> <br /> It's also not clear that Dave find's the real world more horrifying than Mage/CofD. You're interpreting his matter of fact comments under you own standards and values concerning immortality and related issues. <br /> <br /> Dave stated that currently death is inevitable. Given our current state of technology and spiritual understanding, this appears to be a simple fact, although one you would like to change.<br /> <br /> Similarly, our world does not have the magic and other supernatural matter inherent in Mage that would totally alter any discussion concerning death, immortality, any afterlife, etc.<br /> <br /> Lastly, and to some extent, most importantly, the lack of easy immortality was necessary in Mage to correct one of the biggest problems of Ascension. Immortality necessarily creates innumerable ancient and super-powerful beings that often drive the plot rather than the PC's. By taking <i>most</i> of these entities out of the setting, it allows PC's much greater free agency and direct impact on their individual chronicles and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:31:59-07:00","id":967428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967408#post967408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Dave considers the real world to be more horrifying than the horror-themed tabletop roleplaying game he wrote is pretty interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't say that. He said existance has meaning in Mage, unlike in real life. Just because you find that less horrifying doesn't mean Dave does. Personally, I find the meaninglessness of existence to be a tremendous comfort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:45:30-07:00","id":967435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967408#post967408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Dave considers the real world to be more horrifying than the horror-themed tabletop roleplaying game he wrote is pretty interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said anything about horrifying?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can run a program for a pretty long time, though. I'm not sure about forever, but I'd rather live for a thousand years than a hundred, no matter what I had to do. I want to see space exploration too. I want to move my brain into a new body. I want to do and see a lot of things that I can't do in a human lifetime, and that's entirely apart from the sheer terror of irreversible cessation of existence. </div> </div> </div>That's nice.<br /> <br /> You won't.<br /> <br /> In a hundred years, you wil be dead and no one will remember you. Fantasies about the creation of the internet somehow correlating to perfect human/machne transference aside, if such technology ever is invented you will not be able to afford it. In the meantime, any time you could have spent enjoying yourself instead of worrying about something you have no control over will be wasted when you are hit by a bus, catch something irreversible, or eat something inadvisable.<br /> <br /> This is not &quot;horrifying;&quot; (well, it isn't to me), it's just a fact of life. When I die, and I will, maybe a couple dozen people will be sad, depending on how many of my friends and family go before me. Hundreds of thousands of people die every year - to think that the universe will notice my absence seems incredibly childish, especially when it will be busily recycling the chemicals making up my body.<br /> <br /> None of us matter, in the grand scale of things. but we are all in the same situation, so best thing you can do is take any shots at happiness come your way and enjoy the ride. Small things matter more when life is pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:56:34-07:00","id":967445,"title":"","content":"Related to all this, I do still wonder: Why does the explicitly 'anti-death' position of the Silver Ladder not work for people whose mages want to defeat death? The Silver Ladder has a strong position against human potential being cut short, period, and they do a lot of a work in this regard, fighting to change the system and help people live longer, fuller lives.<br /> <br /> They just don't as an organization exalt the individual route of 'I will spend all my energy and resources, and make some highly questionable decisions, to ensure I live longer' but rather 'I will work to ensure that someday, all of humanity attains command of the universe.' If you want to talk about the Culture, that's a pretty Ladder perspective - a civilization where humans command all aspects of their reality and are ruled by benevolent human-created superbeings sounds very much like Imperium to me!<br /> <br /> So... why not do that? Is it because the Silver Ladder focuses more on improving everyone's lives, and in theory risking themselves to improve the world, rather than focusing on specifically acquiring individual immortality?<br /> I would think that helping as many people as possible to live long lives and achieve their potential would be far more valuable to the Ladder than an individual living forever, but it's frankly the case in our world that people do a lot more good against human suffering with malaria netting than with cryonics. That's just a fact.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:01:31-07:00","id":967448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967428#post967428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He didn't say that. He said existance has meaning in Mage, unlike in real life. Just because you find that less horrifying doesn't mean Dave does. Personally, I find the meaninglessness of existence to be a tremendous comfort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, This. And it's reflected in Mage's setting - Awakening posits a world in which everytging does have meaning and purpose, and that in turn requires the Exarchs to exist. Because if there is a God, with this universe you can be sure he's a fucker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:09:48-07:00","id":967453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfSilkAndStone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967445#post967445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related to all this, I do still wonder: Why does the explicitly 'anti-death' position of the Silver Ladder not work for people whose mages want to defeat death? The Silver Ladder has a strong position against human potential being cut short, period, and they do a lot of a work in this regard, fighting to change the system and help people live longer, fuller lives.<br /> <br /> They just don't as an organization exalt the individual route of 'I will spend all my energy and resources, and make some highly questionable decisions, to ensure I live longer' but rather 'I will work to ensure that someday, all of humanity attains command of the universe.' If you want to talk about the Culture, that's a pretty Ladder perspective - a civilization where humans command all aspects of their reality and are ruled by benevolent human-created superbeings sounds very much like Imperium to me!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The SL doesn't strive for all humanity to attain command of the universe. The want everyone to find their appropriate place and function. Not everyone should or can be a mage, and even in the Time Before, most people were Sleepwalkers, not mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:14:12-07:00","id":967456,"title":"","content":"Well, these are all personal idea and viewpoints.<br /> For a beliver all this can be... not so agreeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:20:58-07:00","id":967458,"title":"","content":"Sorry for any offence, Gecko's attention-seeking posts just opened the &quot;Dave clearly believes in this&quot; door one too many times for it to go unchallenged.<br /> <br /> I will simply say that I find religious belief to be a charming character flaw in the friends who do believe. Like mild racism, or voting Conservative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:30:11-07:00","id":967463,"title":"","content":"I appreciate your honesty Dave: you say, that this is your belief just as any beliver can see e found answer in her chosen belief.<br /> The real problem born from taking as granted that other people experience are wrong, false and stupid.<br /> Everybody can have very wrong idea or motivation for belief or absence of belif.<br /> As very good.<br /> I dont think that atheist or agnostic are bad people: i simply think that this is the best solution for her/his own life and evolution on this time, now and here.<br /> <br /> I dont seek, or need, nodding qualification from nobody: but hope that we all can share experiece with mutual respect.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:30:13-07:00","id":967464,"title":"","content":"Another interesting and related discussion is what happens when really powerful mages directly updend rather than cheat supernal truths like death.<br /> <br /> For instance, if an archmage with Death 7 completely excises his ability to die, can he even truly Ascend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:36:54-07:00","id":967466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967458#post967458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for any offence, Gecko's attention-seeking posts just opened the &quot;Dave clearly believes in this&quot; door one too many times for it to go unchallenged.<br /> <br /> I will simply say that I find religious belief to be a charming character flaw in the friends who do believe. Like mild racism, or voting Conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see...accusing me of seeking attention and assuming bad faith, In This Moment I Am Euphoric-level smug atheism, lashing out at me by deliberately saying triggering things targeting what I have explicitly said is my greatest fear and source of anxiety (I know you don't find death and mortality terrifying. I find snakes cute, but if you said they terrified you I wouldn't immediately start posting pictures of them.)...<br /> <br /> And you're really making a ton of assumptions. I'm not doing this for attention, I genuinely want to talk about Awakening. And you seem incredibly sure that A. No one would remember me if I died, which is also a very rude thing to say, B. Life extension technology will never be developed, and C. I wouldn't be able to make use of it. <br /> <br /> I honestly think you have some things you need to look at about yourself. I acknowledge that I've been an asshole in a lot of ways, and I've been making amends for it. I also acknowledge that this discussion might not have been a good idea. <br /> <br /> Dave, I've been where you are. I was where you are just a few weeks ago during my meltdown about Mage/Promethean/Arc's Genius review. I was lashing out. I was deliberately trying to say the things I thought would anger him or hurt him the most. And it was a fucking shitty place to be for everyone involved. <br /> <br /> I'm leaving this debate, and I'm probably going to stay out of it in the future, but I know what you're going through. My initial instinct was to rant and rave and sulk, but I realized: I know why you wrote that. I've been there. Arc hit a nerve with me, so I started lashing out and trying to hurt him. I hit a nerve with you, so you tried to hurt me. I made a lot of mistakes. Well, not so much mistakes as I was a giant asshole for no reason. But let me be a lesson, then.<br /> <br /> Also? I don't believe mind uploading will ever work either. But, there's no reason why the human brain couldn't be kept alive longer than its natural lifespan, and it's already possible to directly connect electronic systems to mental impulses. <br /> <br /> If you want to talk, I'm here. I'm sorry if this seems condescending, it probably is. But I also remember that when I was in that dark place, the people who tried to help me seemed condescending. If I had listened to them earlier, things would have been much less painful.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Removed part of it due to Hayley's request.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-11-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:39:54-07:00","id":967467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967466#post967466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you seem incredibly sure that A. No one would remember me if I died, which is also a very rude thing to say, B. Life extension technology will never be developed, and C. I wouldn't be able to make use of it.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Where!? He dont say nothing about your lifespan or your dear... try to quote where he did, please.<br /> Edit<br /> He writed about a common situation for anybody, not for you only...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-11-2016, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:41:59-07:00","id":967468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967453#post967453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The SL doesn't strive for all humanity to attain command of the universe. The want everyone to find their appropriate place and function. Not everyone should or can be a mage, and even in the Time Before, most people were Sleepwalkers, not mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say Imperium meant everyone gets magic - but they clearly outline their plan for a utopia, often called 'Hieraconis,' in the Silver Ladder book. In said cosmic reordering, they expect all reality to be commanded by humans, and death (among other inconveniences) to be under that command. There's an explicit note that many thearchs believe the resurrection (in some meaningful form) of everyone who ever died will be on the table, come Hieraconis. So the question remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:01:43-07:00","id":967477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967466#post967466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see...accusing me of seeking attention and assuming bad faith, In This Moment I Am Euphoric-level smug atheism, lashing out at me by deliberately saying triggering things targeting what I have explicitly said is my greatest fear and source of anxiety (I know you don't find death and mortality terrifying. I find snakes cute, but if you said they terrified you I wouldn't immediately start posting pictures of them.)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Spare me the false sincerity. I read your tumblr. <br /> <br /> How many times have you quit this forum, or posted &quot;clearly no one cares about this&quot; in your homebrew threads? You have a pattern of demanding we give you all our attention. <br /> <br /> You call me a Deathist (a word stemming from some really quite ugly right-wing systems, by the way) and shit all over this forum for months. You constantly drag my personal opinions into discussions about a game because the game conflicts with <i>your</i> personal hangups? We are under no obligation to respect those hangups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:07:14-07:00","id":967483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967477#post967477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spare me the false sincerity. I read your tumblr. <br /> <br /> How many times have you quit this forum, or posted &amp;quot;clearly no one cares about this&amp;quot; in your homebrew threads? You have a pattern of demanding we give you all our attention. <br /> <br /> You call me a Deathist (a word stemming from some really quite ugly right-wing systems, by the way) and shit all over this forum for months. You constantly drag my personal opinions into discussions about a game because the game conflicts with <i>your</i> personal hangups? We are under no obligation to respect those hangups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay then. <br /> <br /> I'm sorry. I have been looking for attention, and I haven't acknowledged that as fully as I should. So I'm sorry about that. I will try to do better on that front. I'm trying to learn to let go of things, and as badly as that's been going, it's not worth giving up. <br /> <br /> But again, I know where you are right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:11:45-07:00","id":967486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967458#post967458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will simply say that I find religious belief to be a charming character flaw in the friends who do believe. Like mild racism, or voting Conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">I'm sorry, Dave, but this is a pretty textbook example of a rule 1 violation.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:13:39-07:00","id":967489,"title":"","content":"You don't know shit about me, and this sudden magnanimity reads like yet another attempt to win the approval of internet strangers. We are not your support group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:22:04-07:00","id":967496,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Knock it off, both of you. I really don't want to have to thread ban anyone.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:56:26-07:00","id":967515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967466#post967466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, as an aside, I would like to mention that engaging with Hayley on the topic was genuinely enjoyable, due to her compassionate and respectful questions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't try to pit me and a colleague against each other. Thanks in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:58:19-07:00","id":967517,"title":"","content":"All this talk about death and existence. And Dave's thoughts about The eventual unmaking and cosmic indifference of our lifes. I believe this really brings home to me, the Differences between Asc and Awak.<br /> <br /> Asc has been about forcing your meaning onto reality. Which now that I'm older I realize was foolishness and pure fantasy. If you &quot;lose&quot; / give up you find yourself with mundane reality with bitter dreams. And if you &quot;win&quot; you're effectively forced off the playground everyone else plays on. So in the end you find you could never force your meaning onto the world.<br /> <br /> Awak or at least I have found it. Did away with the high power level distractions and led you into finding/crafting meaning in your own in your life/ world. It's about reattaching you to your connects and what important in your character's life. <br /> <br /> Mages are still the Reality Brokers they always were. but now they have a reason to give a sht about the world around them. we are all just prisoners here, of our own device <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G0ATsOXSPBw\" data-code=\"G0ATsOXSPBw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/G0ATsOXSPBw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Noone belongs Anywhere <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E_qvy82U4RE\" data-code=\"E_qvy82U4RE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/E_qvy82U4RE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Its not a defeatist statement. It's self empowering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:24:42-07:00","id":967558,"title":"","content":"I was going to just leave this thread, and I'm certainly not going to keep arguing or attacking people, but I felt like I should come back to publicly apologize to the people I attacked. <br /> <br /> I haven't come far enough. I thought I had identified my problems, but I came back and did essentially the same thing again. This is not an issue of personal beliefs or taste, I'm realizing. The problem is not that I dislike Mage and deathism and support immortality and others don't. The problem is that my inability to handle disagreement led me to start an unproductive argument, and I became increasingly hostile instead of realizing that I had said all I could say and was only sticking around to have the last word and jab at people. <br /> <br /> Dave, you are right: I should not have tried to drag your personal beliefs into this, and I shouldn't have picked this fight in the first place. <br /> <br /> I am aware that an apology does not mandate forgiveness, and I am aware that an apology is often done primarily for the benefit of the apologizer. That is one of many things Bojack Horseman has taught me. So I am not demanding that any of you forgive me, and I want you to know that this apology is not meant to force a moral judgment on any of you. It is purely an expression of contrition for my behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-14-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:27:03-07:00","id":967592,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> When I think of videos about Mage, particularly how they see through the Lie, this one always tops the list (and is an amusing distraction from the tone and content of the current debate):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Oe7Q8OCm5I\" data-code=\"3Oe7Q8OCm5I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3Oe7Q8OCm5I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-12-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T23:59:38-07:00","id":967799,"title":"","content":"Here's a question then, in the spirit of elevating this thread: how do you rectify the Supernal significance of Death with the desire to live forever? Death means more than just the cessation of life, but is instead wrapped up in the ends of things and entropy along with the wider Moros fascination on the transformation of things. Is lichdom an act of hubris because it is one of stasis, choosing to defy the natural flux of Death imposed over time - and would pursuing a transformative escape from mortality be less of a sin against Wisdom than simply prolonging one's current state?<br /> <br /> I have to wonder if engineering a new form with Life or becoming something entirely different via Spirit or Mind might be a better avenue towards living forever instead of remaining fundamentally the same forever might be more agreeable, and while Mind has the negative example of the solipsistic, unchanging Morpheans, I have to imagine becoming an astral being without a meat body, free to wander the dreams of man eternally... surely that's a noble pursuit of Gnosis, and the undying curiosity of the Awakened soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:19:45-07:00","id":967827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967799#post967799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question then, in the spirit of elevating this thread: how do you rectify the Supernal significance of Death with the desire to live forever? Death means more than just the cessation of life, but is instead wrapped up in the ends of things and entropy along with the wider Moros fascination on the transformation of things. Is lichdom an act of hubris because it is one of stasis, choosing to defy the natural flux of Death imposed over time - and would pursuing a transformative escape from mortality be less of a sin against Wisdom than simply prolonging one's current state?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. It probably got lost in the relatively long posts I've written, but in a nutshell I would say that for things to properly define themselves, they must interact with other things and that interaction requires change. But things are defined as much by when they are static as when they change. If everything changed all the time, universe would be in utter chaos, and there <i>are</i> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physical_constant\" target=\"_blank\">certain constants</a> present in this reality.<br /> <br /> The key would be how to prevent specifically, and I quote my previous post, &quot;the cessation of continuation of a specific sequence of perceptions that define a single human mind, happening by the virtue of degradation of brain cells and organism as a whole, with similar processes not even happening in some existing animals&quot;. This is a deliberately mouthful term to show just how narrow kind of change we are talking about. The goal would be to make static only and only this particular process, and let everything else change (personality, memories, muscle mass if you exercise, etc...).<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm a transhumanist and *I* wouldn't accept anything less. Rather than becoming a static thing unable to be shaped by outside stimuli, I would really prefer death. Transhumanism isn't about overcoming humanity, it's about overcoming physical limitations so that you can be <i>more</i> human, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:58:33-07:00","id":967835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967386#post967386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think using spells to protect yourself against dying of old age <i>is</i> bad, <i>per se</i>. That's pretty much the function of Veil of Moments, and that spell isn't considered evil. The things Liches do to make themselves immortal aren't bad because they serve the Exarch, they're bad because they require you to fuck with people's souls, which is a pretty serious Act of Hubris.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure you are confusing Liches and Reapers here, which happens pretty often probably thanks to Tremere being both Liches and Reapers and the best known example of both.<br /> Nothing about being a Lich <i>requires</i> you to fuck with people's souls. In fact, extending your life without harming anyone else is extremely easy in Mage. The description of Liches even acknowledges that, but handwaves it away as those tactics being dispellable (which completely ignores the existence of Legacy attainments, but maybe the rules for Legacies were written after the part about Liches).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:16:59-07:00","id":968033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967835#post967835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am pretty sure you are confusing Liches and Reapers here, which happens pretty often probably thanks to Tremere being both Liches and Reapers and the best known example of both.<br /> Nothing about being a Lich <i>requires</i> you to fuck with people's souls. In fact, extending your life without harming anyone else is extremely easy in Mage. The description of Liches even acknowledges that, but handwaves it away as those tactics being dispellable (which completely ignores the existence of Legacy attainments, but maybe the rules for Legacies were written after the part about Liches).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is more or less an issue for the ST, simply ruling that Legacies can't accomplish this without serious drawbacks as part of the bargain can maintain the theme of immortality coming at great cost to one's sense of humanity. Or not, depending on the style of game.<br /> <br /> I think Legacies are perhaps a bit too easy to start thinking of in purely mechanical terms, especially since the mechanics for constructing their powers are as precise as they are (this is not a bad thing mind). But I've found they work best for me as a ST if there's a greater focus on an underlying assumption that, as an in-setting thing, a mage *can't* just define whatever powers they might want in the process of creating one, but that they arise organically from that Mage's development of Gnosis as they come into contact with Supernal truth. Legacy attainments to provide drawback free immortality by duplicating long duration life and death spells would have to come out of a narrative that made sense for those powers, and if the campaign setting has innate themes that say doing this makes you a monster, becoming a monster would have to arise in the legacy itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:27:34-07:00","id":968040,"title":"","content":"Mages who become Astral beings are called Morpheans and they appear in Astral Realms. They're a bit of a sad existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T17:00:26-07:00","id":968254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957360#post957360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortality is such a great motivation for characters to seek out and make sacrifices for. It's the once universal human experience that is both certain and sucks ass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, but I don't want the writers to tell me how its done. I want them to tell me how others have failed. It doesn't make it cool if a bunch of mages have already done it. Not nearly as cool as one of my players being one of the first in the world to achieve it. There is no rule against it being an obsession, but why make it common? Why make it easy? If you want a character to become immortal, just have them succeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T17:09:24-07:00","id":968260,"title":"","content":"They kind of did that. They told you how a bunch of Mages have pulled it off, but how much it sucks for them that they did. Leaving the goal of &quot;perfect&quot; immortality just out of sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T17:13:41-07:00","id":968262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968260#post968260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They kind of did that. They told you how a bunch of Mages have pulled it off, but how much it sucks for them that they did. Leaving the goal of &quot;perfect&quot; immortality just out of sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like great plot hooks for a character seeking Immortality. It gives them not soul eating monsters to ask questions of, and potentially lets them to be one who delivers hope to those NPCS. While side stepping the inevitable player or GM looking for a way to make a character all powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T17:55:49-07:00","id":968280,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:37:47-07:00","id":968542,"title":"","content":"Basically, anyone who accomplished some level of imperfect immortality mentioned in the core is a great plot point, hook or story thread of the character that eventually succeeds. A PC with the obsession mining the successes and failures of others whom ultimately achieves immortality is a great story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:54:16-07:00","id":968581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967458#post967458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> posts just opened the &amp;quot;Dave clearly believes in this&amp;quot; door one too many times for it to go unchallenged</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, much of a pain in the ass as it must have been for you, it's kinda fascinating for me; it's like watching the start of a religion and people referencing its prophet. In this weird twist, it's been fantastic inspiration for how the Awakened act towards Archmasters and Oracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:04:49-07:00","id":968587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968581#post968581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y'know, much of a pain in the ass as it must have been for you, it's kinda fascinating for me; it's like watching the start of a religion and people referencing its prophet. In this weird twist, it's been fantastic inspiration for how the Awakened act towards Archmasters and Oracles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's hilarious.<br /> <br /> &quot;I do hereby swear myself to the Great Dave, I do solemnly swear to forsake the false promise of immortality...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:08:22-07:00","id":968590,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure someone already made the Mystery Cult of Dave merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:11:05-07:00","id":968625,"title":"","content":"From 4Chan by AmyV:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adherents of DaveB<br /> <br /> Among the few Onyx Path freelancers that subject themselves to /wodg/ on a regular basis, none are more beloved than Dave Brookshaw. His word trumps all in these threads, and a single post from him can turn the tide of a conversation and leave participants recanting, should they be unfortunate enough to have disagreed with Dave. Any that hold their beliefs even after the target of this cult's worship can look forward to being shitposted into oblivion until they recant.<br /> <br /> Cultists: Anon, tripfag, nMage fan, newbie freelancer, aspiring writer, fa/tg/uy just passing by<br /> <br /> Initiation benefits.<br /> <br /> \u2022 All initiates are familiar with the rules and themes of Mage: The Awakening. They gain a M:tAw specialty in Academics.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 Further-initiated Adherents have memorized the entire David Brookshaw literary canon. They gain the Eidectic Memory merit, but only for books either developed or written by Brookshaw.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 DaveB likes Komodo dragons, right? Somehow, the cult's dedication to this guy grants the 8 again benefit to Animal Ken rolls involving Komodo Dragons<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Such close study of the game's developer unlocks the secrets of Mage: The Awakening in their entirety. A character with Adherents of DaveB \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 can talk about or play nMage without sounding like a twat. That is its own reward.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Oh my god, you're actually friends with DaveB! When you do something on social media, roll presence + computer. On a success, he'll like or retweet the post. On an exceptional success, he'll actually reply to you! Now don't freak out. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:14:28-07:00","id":968629,"title":"","content":"That's the one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:25:57-07:00","id":968636,"title":"","content":"Well this took a dramatic turn away from the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> I thought we were discussing whether or not it would be easy to become immortal, and now we got... this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bowing out of this thread, was fun while it lasted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:38:13-07:00","id":968642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968636#post968636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this took a dramatic turn away from the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> I thought we were discussing whether or not it would be easy to become immortal, and now we got... this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bowing out of this thread, was fun while it lasted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thread took a number of unfortunate turns well before the injection of some much needed levity,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:41:06-07:00","id":968644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=957360#post957360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortality is such a great motivation for characters to seek out and make sacrifices for. It's the once universal human experience that is both certain and sucks ass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That depends on what kind of immortality we're talking about, and the effects of death.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eternal Youth = Awesome. You get to remain healthy and beautiful forever. And when you're finally bored with life, you have your pick of ways to go out.<br /> <br /> <br /> True Immortality = Living Hell. Even after you get bored, you still stuck here.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Death + No Magic = Shitty afterlife. You work so hard to obtain your power and occult secrets, only to lose them just because your body gives out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Death + Magic = Tolerable afterlife. Your body may have been destroyed, but at least you still keep your hard earned powers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:47:20-07:00","id":968650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968587#post968587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's hilarious.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;I do hereby swear myself to the Great Dave, I do solemnly swear to forsake the false promise of immortality...&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hilarious, insightful, just a little bit creepy.<br /> <br /> AmyV's summary does it more justice than me; it's that weird fusion of cult of celebrity meeting actual authority, which is really right where cult leaders sit in reality.<br /> <br /> It's easy to lose sight of the insight associated with Arcana and Gnosis dots in the setting when there's no specific enforcement of them mechanically, but for the Awakened, a master is so in tune with a fundamental aspect of reality as to have absolute control over it in the most immediate sense. An Archmaster steps beyond that and the Ascended even further.<br /> <br /> People squabbling over game rules and setting structure isn't a bad analogy; obsessives discussing understandings and interpretations that are rapidly altered by pronouncements of a figure they see as authoritative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:55:50-07:00","id":968658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968650#post968650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hilarious, insightful, just a little bit creepy.<br /> <br /> AmyV's summary does it more justice than me; it's that weird fusion of cult of celebrity meeting actual authority, which is really right where cult leaders sit in reality.<br /> <br /> It's easy to lose sight of the insight associated with Arcana and Gnosis dots in the setting when there's no specific enforcement of them mechanically, but for the Awakened, a master is so in tune with a fundamental aspect of reality as to have absolute control over it in the most immediate sense. An Archmaster steps beyond that and the Ascended even further.<br /> <br /> People squabbling over game rules and setting structure isn't a bad analogy; obsessives discussing understandings and interpretations that are rapidly altered by pronouncements of a figure they see as authoritative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More importantly, why doesn't Mage have more Komodo dragons? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:59:34-07:00","id":968660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967435#post967435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... In a hundred years, you wil be dead and no one will remember you. Fantasies about the creation of the internet somehow correlating to perfect human/machne transference aside, if such technology ever is invented you will not be able to afford it. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So bit late to this party, but this line stood out to me as it was related to what I was thinking of formulating a response to things as I was reading from page 6 of the thread. That even in the most optimistic current scenarios with anagathic technology, we barely can get people to have some basic medical things now (vaccines, nutritious food, mosquito nets, electric lighting, indoor plumbing). That I living where I do don't have to worry about malaria, Ebola, polio or vitiman D deficiency are all things that are a result of privilege. And by the same dint, the fact that I'm financially kind of always in a spot where a major medical emergency or problem would financially ruin me is a privilege I don't have. Donald Trump or Bill Gates can get the anagathics. I probably won't.<br /> <br /> This seems especially emphasized with the nature of immortality in Awakening. SInce the nature of Supernal magic means that Quiessence makes it hard if not impossible to use it to give immortality to Sleepers. So you give it to yourself. Death is 1/10th the rules of the universe, but like the flow of time, the boundries of space, the vageries of Life or the secrets of the mind, you can flaunt or ignore them with effort. It gives you a privilege most people can't have. It plays a bit to I think a theme talked about with Mage before in that ultimately, the Wise are ultimately privileged people. I think making immortality easy simply stacks this privilege on. It simply makes a group of people, who while enlightened and different, just easily &quot;better&quot;. It's a free beenie. <br /> <br /> That's interesting, but I think a thing that makes stories of privlege more interesting is when you want <i>more</i>. Or at least, if it is something you don't get for it but only it allows you to have. To some extent, that's the vibe I get with immortality in Mage. Being Awakened already is a huge privilege. You get to see the Truth, impose your will on the world and unlock its secrets. By being Awakened, you probably already live longer than most people. By being Awakened, you get to already do a lot others don't get to do or even can conceive of doing. But by wanting to be immortal, to live forever to do it more, it feels on some level kind of greedy and gross to me. It's basically to me like the billionaire who's upset they don't have a private jet or don't have enough influence when they spend millions on politicians. Note, this goes with real world immortality too. Likely who gets it will be the super-rich if it ever happens. And it'll let them be super-rich in a way that lets their wealth grow larger, keep to themselvers longer and generally means they get more while the rest of us get to die to the bidding of immortal corpses.<br /> <br /> There's also a bit where the world can't support 10 billion immortals. So someone needs to die eventually. WHich again, brings the question for the folks hwo want ultimate immortaltiy: What makes you so deserving of it? Nothing I have seen ever has convinced me that folks see immortality as a privilege to have, not a right. And those who want it as a right, don't seem to get the privilege needed to have or justify it.<br /> <br /> This is barring other things like how I'm pretty sure I'm a completely different person in mindset of time and people now than I was when I turend 20. ANd that I'll be different again at 50 and 60. And that someone at 200 is going to be a fucking alien with their perception of time and people. So that it's not really &quot;me&quot; there I'm projecting in the future anyhow, but some continuation that identifies with the general bundle of amtter I am now as part of it. But I also fully admit having a fairl Humian sense of the self and identity, so that's another matter.<br /> <br /> But yeah, in a big span of things, to me Mage: the Awakening has a bit of an unstated sense of quesitoning privilege in power. And I think the immortality themes it plays on play a lot on those and how much rallying against them in itself is an exercise of power, even if you don't get exactly what you want out of it.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:27:08-07:00","id":968678,"title":"","content":"I suspect mages don't tend to live longer than Sleepers in their part of the world - not because of magic itself, but because they're going to chase their obsessions down rabbit holes where the rabbits turn out to have entirely too many teeth and break certain fundamental laws of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:50:14-07:00","id":968720,"title":"","content":"I don't think I understood the uproar in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules seem to demonize attempting to become immortal quite a bit, especially on p. 237 under Liches, claiming that any mage having the austerity to want to live forever has &quot;deeper rooted problems&quot;, because who would dare be so bold as to survive their own children? It's also claimed that it's incredibly difficult to live such a long time. But why? It seems like a Life Perfecting spell should do the job. The example spell &quot;Knit&quot; can only repair damage that your body could repair on its own, but I don't see why that should logically be the case. Seems someone was really worried about mages going for immortality?<br /> <br /> It's not very important to me, but it seems like an odd stance and I wondered if I missed anything. </div> </div> </div>This is the first post. There is no &quot;good&quot; or &quot;perfect&quot; way to become immortal according to the rules. This is true. But it is your game, and it could be possible if you want it to be. There is even a mechanism in game that applies to the journey. An obsession with the mystery of immortality would do it. Now, if as a player, you wish to be an ageless immortal then find a Storyteller willing to let you be an ageless immortal. Same goes if you wish to be impervious from harm. <br /> <br /> By the current rules you might not be able to be an immortal, but what good is a game of mysteries when all the solutions are in a core book limited by things like page count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:00:38-07:00","id":968724,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a><br /> <br /> Love the post. You're describing some of the themes of vamp. The elongated existence and distancing from the human perspective. Minus the Hunger and Beast. But the idea that others will fall while you continue is still in there. In fact one of the oldest spins of the Vampire was the aristocratic Vamp, who feed from the poor. Sometimes killing them.<br /> <br /> Which is just an allegorical interpretation of Feudalism. The serf worked the land while the lord profited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":".  Spelling 09-13-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:14:48-07:00","id":968771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968720#post968720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I understood the uproar in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is the first post. There is no &quot;good&quot; or &quot;perfect&quot; way to become immortal according to the rules. This is true. But it is your game, and it could be possible if you want it to be. There is even a mechanism in game that applies to the journey. An obsession with the mystery of immortality would do it. Now, if as a player, you wish to be an ageless immortal then find a Storyteller willing to let you be an ageless immortal. Same goes if you wish to be impervious from harm.<br /> <br /> By the current rules you might not be able to be an immortal, but what good is a game of mysteries when all the solutions are in a core book limited by things like page count.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Heck, just magicking yourself some new stem cells could probably do the trick. Stop your body from experiencing cellular degeneration.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think one of the major points about why immortality is such a big deal is due to the fact that unlike Werewolves, Vampires, Changelings and such, a Mage has little reason to be tortured by their longevity. They have the potential to live perfectly happy, normal human lives and blend seamlessly into society. That's something the other monsters don't get to do.<br /> <br /> Sounds like they're jealous, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-13-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:18:16-07:00","id":968777,"title":"","content":"Let's face it, the reason there's an &quot;uproar&quot; is that I was an asshole and couldn't leave it alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:18:35-07:00","id":968778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968720#post968720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I understood the uproar in the first place.<br /> This is the first post. There is no &quot;good&quot; or &quot;perfect&quot; way to become immortal according to the rules. This is true. But it is your game, and it could be possible if you want it to be. There is even a mechanism in game that applies to the journey. An obsession with the mystery of immortality would do it. Now, if as a player, you wish to be an ageless immortal then find a Storyteller willing to let you be an ageless immortal. Same goes if you wish to be impervious from harm.<br /> <br /> By the current rules you might not be able to be an immortal, but what good is a game of mysteries when all the solutions are in a core book limited by things like page count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell if you really really wanted it is not so difficult to transplant the merit from Ascension<br /> <br /> &quot;Ageless: 2 point merit&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;You character is not going to age, determine with your dm the whys and hows. Enjoy an eternity of being horrified by inflation, nobody getting your refferences and kids this days&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:22:05-07:00","id":968780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=968778#post968778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell if you really really wanted it is not so difficult to transplant the merit from Ascension<br /> <br /> &quot;Ageless: 2 point merit&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You character is not going to age, determine with your dm the whys and hows. Enjoy an eternity of being horrified by inflation, nobody getting your refferences and kids this days&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oh, right... living in a Post Trump America... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core